tbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/9840ae6285dd45e8b46df0b15e0df3ed1b2d2435/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T00:12:46Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T00:12:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(#51): end-to-end ''Getting Started with Permissions'' walkthrough (#68)\n\nSequences install through audit-verified enforcement in one runnable\npath. The reference docs already existed; this is the high-value gap\nbetween \"the mechanism exists\" and \"an adopter can actually use it.\"\n\nNew: docs/getting-started/permissions.md\n\nNine numbered steps + a verification checklist:\n\n  1. Pull chart 0.6.1, pin image 0.6.2 (chart appVersion 0.6.0 is\n     stale-referencing after #64 shipped the audit module in 0.6.2).\n  2. Configure superUsers + admin.users + replace\n     PLACEHOLDER-ADMIN-GROUP in the CSV.\n  3. Copy examples/adopter-plugin as the starting shape. Call\n     permissionsRegistry.addPermissions() — load-bearing convention\n     for the runtime audit to see the plugin.\n  4. Wire the plugin id into pluginsWithPermission AND opt into the\n     chart-time guard via permissions.enforced: true.\n  5. Bind the permission to a role via the CSV; bind the role to a\n     group.\n  6. Boot and confirm the pluginsWithPermission audit clears —\n     grep for the expected \"no gaps found\" log line, or read the\n     error line if the audit caught a gap.\n  7. Verify from an admin identity (RBAC discovery shows the plugin).\n  8. Verify from a non-admin identity (gated route returns 403).\n  9. Optionally, add a conditional policy referencing the plugin''s\n     rule to gate on resource properties.\n\nEvery step is copyable; every command runs against the working\nexamples/adopter-plugin. The tutorial is prose + yaml + csv + sh\nblocks; one ts block is marked noCompile with a reason (illustrative\nsnippet pointing at the runnable version in the reference).\n\nAlso updates:\n\n- docs/getting-started/README.md gains a Next Steps entry pointing at\n  the new walkthrough.\n- docs/architecture/permissions.md points new adopters at the\n  walkthrough before the reference detail.\n- docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md points authors following the\n  end-to-end sequence at the walkthrough, framing this page as\n  reference material.\n\ndocs-compile-check PASSes with the changes — the tutorial''s noCompile\nts block satisfies the annotation contract with its explanation, and\nthe yaml/csv/sh blocks fall in the non-compile-checked-langs category.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4b2c0930b13641fdb7561dca7e770e5188ddcb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/b4b2c0930b13641fdb7561dca7e770e5188ddcb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/9840ae6285dd45e8b46df0b15e0df3ed1b2d2435","verification":{"payload":"tree b4b2c0930b13641fdb7561dca7e770e5188ddcb0\nparent d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784333566 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784333566 -0500\n\ndocs(#51): end-to-end ''Getting Started with Permissions'' walkthrough (#68)\n\nSequences install through audit-verified enforcement in one runnable\npath. The reference docs already existed; this is the high-value gap\nbetween \"the mechanism exists\" and \"an adopter can actually use it.\"\n\nNew: docs/getting-started/permissions.md\n\nNine numbered steps + a verification checklist:\n\n  1. Pull chart 0.6.1, pin image 0.6.2 (chart appVersion 0.6.0 is\n     stale-referencing after #64 shipped the audit module in 0.6.2).\n  2. Configure superUsers + admin.users + replace\n     PLACEHOLDER-ADMIN-GROUP in the CSV.\n  3. Copy examples/adopter-plugin as the starting shape. Call\n     permissionsRegistry.addPermissions() — load-bearing convention\n     for the runtime audit to see the plugin.\n  4. Wire the plugin id into pluginsWithPermission AND opt into the\n     chart-time guard via permissions.enforced: true.\n  5. Bind the permission to a role via the CSV; bind the role to a\n     group.\n  6. Boot and confirm the pluginsWithPermission audit clears —\n     grep for the expected \"no gaps found\" log line, or read the\n     error line if the audit caught a gap.\n  7. Verify from an admin identity (RBAC discovery shows the plugin).\n  8. Verify from a non-admin identity (gated route returns 403).\n  9. Optionally, add a conditional policy referencing the plugin''s\n     rule to gate on resource properties.\n\nEvery step is copyable; every command runs against the working\nexamples/adopter-plugin. The tutorial is prose + yaml + csv + sh\nblocks; one ts block is marked noCompile with a reason (illustrative\nsnippet pointing at the runnable version in the reference).\n\nAlso updates:\n\n- docs/getting-started/README.md gains a Next Steps entry pointing at\n  the new walkthrough.\n- docs/architecture/permissions.md points new adopters at the\n  walkthrough before the reference detail.\n- docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md points authors following the\n  end-to-end sequence at the walkthrough, framing this page as\n  reference material.\n\ndocs-compile-check PASSes with the changes — the tutorial''s noCompile\nts block satisfies the annotation contract with its explanation, and\nthe yaml/csv/sh blocks fall in the non-compile-checked-langs category.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWsT+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9UUQAHXdNAz2mPO8oLWsb2YQjoHp\nOx+XSBdVJKrJD8zWtqHRWrgy3kv5hxmtgEI2h+4ayiMN6RXSTso87gWk50ao/hCJ\nC/ISOFk1MYEVJbavtVHzPPrwq+ZWxqSaC25d2GLmehuVir1PUJYpJzqr+jxUHNNV\nCWYGpndXej0ps1VejwTryHnV95/O9IAH+AI4Z+MVq9/p3iF4f3frEZ5lUtmfk9sI\n5/LAAcVdJobisEfThtZj/NfvRTHr+4q85QVmI8cq7b28KCldOORPlRWBxMGnLXWN\nKzKRH6+Tj5BlyHSMFH7yWeY/sasMc3njnK8p93O0G6qqsfxOnSra0Xpr7zpYnbqM\nfRto8JIUK61q36PeypZFi4zF28mBrd54WEKWAA+dxWc8r2p8QOwX6rQf743NPrq/\naTGfCsFquK7rMKg/GW9NgVd+7yR0g5jH6XAej0MwMecswgYFSudoapp6omoQyc/p\nc6ks8uBhK9dV//I9Gkq+8e6fR523h97jQYCB/Y2nu1k75yQcU9ycePWRU9JuCLAs\nJ5vOZx4EDnEm9Z5ze+rf2WJObhpQ12y8HxyqCvXhQvJNjWOB3dS4eamgTsW4IMaS\nEZ4ShMO2tyFjng3AgFHvQRRf8/Q2Z86JpI7Xf2QoaZfpoylSNCR83bkMqSHEljU9\nTHL8xluUmbzBuxm1C3xl\n=yw7c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T00:12:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/9840ae6285dd45e8b46df0b15e0df3ed1b2d2435","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDk4NDBhZTYyODVkZDQ1ZThiNDZkZjBiMTVlMGRmM2VkMWIyZDI0MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553","sha":"d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553"}],"sha":"9840ae6285dd45e8b46df0b15e0df3ed1b2d2435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/9840ae6285dd45e8b46df0b15e0df3ed1b2d2435"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T20:58:10Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T20:58:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(#59): runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps + addPermissions convention (#64)\n\n* feat(#59): runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps + addPermissions convention\n\nCloses the loop from butlerdotdev/butler-portal#59. Adds a backend\naudit module that runs at startup, enumerates loaded dynamic plugins\nvia dynamicPluginsServiceRef, HTTP-fetches each plugin''s own\n/.well-known/backstage/permissions/metadata, and logs level=error\nper plugin that declared permissions at runtime but is missing from\npermission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission.\n\n## Why this is different from what already shipped\n\n- #42''s chart-time guard (chart 0.6.0-source, released as 0.6.1)\n  fails helm template on opted-in plugins with a wrong pluginId.\n  Sees values-file INTENT.\n- #63''s NOTES.txt warn (chart 0.6.1) surfaces uncategorized plugin\n  entries. Sees values-file INTENT.\n- 0.6.1 also shipped permissions.declared: false as an OPERATOR\n  ASSERTION about the plugin''s behavior. Silences the warn.\n  Assertions drift: a plugin updates, starts calling addPermissions,\n  the values file still says declared:false, the warn stays silent,\n  and the plugin is unenforced while the config claims that''s\n  intentional.\n\nThis module sees REALITY: it enumerates plugins the framework\nactually loaded, and asks each what it registered. Values-file\nintent is not consulted. The two mechanisms are complements — the\nchart-time guard prevents opt-in mistakes, the runtime audit catches\nassertion drift and every other case where the values file diverges\nfrom what the loaded plugins actually declared.\n\n## Coverage limit (load-bearing — see the addPermissions convention below)\n\nThe audit reads /.well-known/backstage/permissions/metadata, which\nis auto-wired by @backstage/plugin-permission-node''s\ncreatePermissionIntegrationRouter when a plugin calls\npermissionsRegistry.addPermissions() or .addResourceType(). A plugin\nthat only does createPermission({name}) + permissions.authorize()\nnever populates that endpoint, so it is invisible to the audit.\n\nCompanion doc change in this PR: the plugin-authoring guide''s\nminimal example now calls permissionsRegistry.addPermissions([...])\nin every plugin''s init(). The convention is independently correct\n(the same endpoint RBAC''s own discovery walks), and it makes\ndetection complete as the convention spreads. examples/adopter-plugin\nalready uses addResourceType, so it''s covered without a change.\n\n## What \"loud\" means for the log\n\nlogger.error at startup, one line per gap, framed as CONSEQUENCE:\n\n  [pluginsWithPermission audit] plugin ''<id>'' declared N permission(s)\n  at runtime and is NOT in permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission.\n  Authz is NOT running for this plugin: RBAC''s discovery API returns\n  [] for it, and every authorize() call for its permissions passes\n  through as ALLOW regardless of your policy CSV.\n\nLog lines survive every deployment model (helm interactive, Flux\nHelmRelease, Argo CD, kubectl apply), which was the original\ngitops-visibility motivation for #59 — but not its primary\njustification once #63 shipped the assertion-declared:false escape\nhatch. The primary justification now is that only the runtime knows\nwhat plugins actually do, and only the runtime can catch drift\nbetween values-file categorization and plugin behavior.\n\n## Third release channel\n\nThis session''s arc has now touched three release channels:\n\n- docs (#41, #54, #57, #58) — reached via github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal main\n- chart (#42, #63) — reached via oci://ghcr.io/butlerdotdev/charts/butler-portal:0.6.1\n- image (this PR) — reached via ghcr.io/butlerdotdev/butler-portal:0.6.1\n\nThe class of \"merged to source but not to what adopters pull\"\nreappeared for docs, closed via the four-part fix, reappeared for\nthe chart, closed via 0.6.1. Third channel here; do the release the\nsame way. After merge:\n\n  git tag -a v0.6.1 origin/main -m ''runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps''\n  git push origin v0.6.1\n\ntriggers the ci.yaml semver publish path. Chart 0.6.1''s appVersion\nbecomes accurate once the image is published; adopters bump\nimage.tag: \"0.6.1\" in their values files to pick up the module.\n\n* audit: skip when pluginId is unset + log info when listed plugin returns 404\n\nTwo Pass 1/2 review findings on the fresh #59 module.\n\nPass 1: pluginId fallback to manifest.name is unsafe. Package name is\nnot the pluginId — @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend registers\nas pluginId ''permission''. Falling back to the package name produces a\nbogus discovery lookup + a 404 the audit was silently accepting as\n\"plugin declared no permissions.\" Removed the fallback; skip with a\ndebug log when pluginId is unset.\n\nPass 2: 404 on /permission/metadata was uniformly treated as \"plugin\ndid not register.\" That''s correct when the plugin is NOT in\npluginsWithPermission — the audit is blind by design there and moves\non. But when the plugin IS in pluginsWithPermission, the operator\nexpected permissions from it; a 404 there means the plugin loaded\nwithout calling addPermissions/addResourceType. Surface at info so\noperators auditing logs see the surprise (listing might be stale, or\nthe plugin might be missing the registration call).\n\n* audit: extract testable function + Jest suite + architecture doc section\n\nPost-review amendments. All three items from the last three-pass:\n\n- P3#1 (tests): auditPluginsWithPermission() is now a standalone\n  function whose deps are typed via a local structural\n  DynamicPluginsForAudit shape. The createBackendModule wrapper calls\n  it after a settle window. Tests inject plain mocks and assert on\n  logger output. 7/7 passing:\n    - nothing loaded -> info \"nothing to audit\"\n    - unlisted plugin declares perms -> error naming id, count,\n      \"passes through as ALLOW\", \"authz is NOT running\", \"Add ''<id>''\"\n    - listed plugin declares perms -> no error, \"no gaps found\" info\n    - listed plugin returns 404 -> info naming both causes (stale\n      listing / missing registration)\n    - unlisted plugin returns 404 -> silent (debug only, by-design\n      coverage limit)\n    - manifest has no backstage.pluginId -> skipped with debug\n    - mixed listed+unlisted -> error only for the unlisted one\n- P3#2 (arch doc section): docs/architecture/permissions.md gains a\n  new \"Runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps\" section that\n  covers what it checks, what to do when the log fires (runbook step\n  for both the error and the info-404 case), and the coverage limit.\n  Cross-linked from the known-gotcha at the bottom.\n- P3#3 (runbook line): the new doc section''s \"If you see the log\"\n  subsection carries the runbook — add the pluginId to\n  permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission and redeploy; audit re-runs\n  and confirms the gap closed.\n\nThe image release version is v0.6.2 (not v0.6.1): chart 0.6.1 already\nclaims that string. Fix in the PR body was pushed separately.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"9369d9de3a43820f3c15134237240d5f5c01b675","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/9369d9de3a43820f3c15134237240d5f5c01b675"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553","verification":{"payload":"tree 9369d9de3a43820f3c15134237240d5f5c01b675\nparent 60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784321890 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784321890 -0500\n\nfeat(#59): runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps + addPermissions convention (#64)\n\n* feat(#59): runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps + addPermissions convention\n\nCloses the loop from butlerdotdev/butler-portal#59. Adds a backend\naudit module that runs at startup, enumerates loaded dynamic plugins\nvia dynamicPluginsServiceRef, HTTP-fetches each plugin''s own\n/.well-known/backstage/permissions/metadata, and logs level=error\nper