ed without a change.\n\n## What \"loud\" means for the log\n\nlogger.error at startup, one line per gap, framed as CONSEQUENCE:\n\n  [pluginsWithPermission audit] plugin ''<id>'' declared N permission(s)\n  at runtime and is NOT in permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission.\n  Authz is NOT running for this plugin: RBAC''s discovery API returns\n  [] for it, and every authorize() call for its permissions passes\n  through as ALLOW regardless of your policy CSV.\n\nLog lines survive every deployment model (helm interactive, Flux\nHelmRelease, Argo CD, kubectl apply), which was the original\ngitops-visibility motivation for #59 — but not its primary\njustification once #63 shipped the assertion-declared:false escape\nhatch. The primary justification now is that only the runtime knows\nwhat plugins actually do, and only the runtime can catch drift\nbetween values-file categorization and plugin behavior.\n\n## Third release channel\n\nThis session''s arc has now touched three release channels:\n\n- docs (#41, #54, #57, #58) — reached via github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal main\n- chart (#42, #63) — reached via oci://ghcr.io/butlerdotdev/charts/butler-portal:0.6.1\n- image (this PR) — reached via ghcr.io/butlerdotdev/butler-portal:0.6.1\n\nThe class of \"merged to source but not to what adopters pull\"\nreappeared for docs, closed via the four-part fix, reappeared for\nthe chart, closed via 0.6.1. Third channel here; do the release the\nsame way. After merge:\n\n  git tag -a v0.6.1 origin/main -m ''runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps''\n  git push origin v0.6.1\n\ntriggers the ci.yaml semver publish path. Chart 0.6.1''s appVersion\nbecomes accurate once the image is published; adopters bump\nimage.tag: \"0.6.1\" in their values files to pick up the module.\n\n* audit: skip when pluginId is unset + log info when listed plugin returns 404\n\nTwo Pass 1/2 review findings on the fresh #59 module.\n\nPass 1: pluginId fallback to manifest.name is unsafe. Package name is\nnot the pluginId — @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend registers\nas pluginId ''permission''. Falling back to the package name produces a\nbogus discovery lookup + a 404 the audit was silently accepting as\n\"plugin declared no permissions.\" Removed the fallback; skip with a\ndebug log when pluginId is unset.\n\nPass 2: 404 on /permission/metadata was uniformly treated as \"plugin\ndid not register.\" That''s correct when the plugin is NOT in\npluginsWithPermission — the audit is blind by design there and moves\non. But when the plugin IS in pluginsWithPermission, the operator\nexpected permissions from it; a 404 there means the plugin loaded\nwithout calling addPermissions/addResourceType. Surface at info so\noperators auditing logs see the surprise (listing might be stale, or\nthe plugin might be missing the registration call).\n\n* audit: extract testable function + Jest suite + architecture doc section\n\nPost-review amendments. All three items from the last three-pass:\n\n- P3#1 (tests): auditPluginsWithPermission() is now a standalone\n  function whose deps are typed via a local structural\n  DynamicPluginsForAudit shape. The createBackendModule wrapper calls\n  it after a settle window. Tests inject plain mocks and assert on\n  logger output. 7/7 passing:\n    - nothing loaded -> info \"nothing to audit\"\n    - unlisted plugin declares perms -> error naming id, count,\n      \"passes through as ALLOW\", \"authz is NOT running\", \"Add ''<id>''\"\n    - listed plugin declares perms -> no error, \"no gaps found\" info\n    - listed plugin returns 404 -> info naming both causes (stale\n      listing / missing registration)\n    - unlisted plugin returns 404 -> silent (debug only, by-design\n      coverage limit)\n    - manifest has no backstage.pluginId -> skipped with debug\n    - mixed listed+unlisted -> error only for the unlisted one\n- P3#2 (arch doc section): docs/architecture/permissions.md gains a\n  new \"Runtime audit for pluginsWithPermission gaps\" section that\n  covers what it checks, what to do when the log fires (runbook step\n  for both the error and the info-404 case), and the coverage limit.\n  Cross-linked from the known-gotcha at the bottom.\n- P3#3 (runbook line): the new doc section''s \"If you see the log\"\n  subsection carries the runbook — add the pluginId to\n  permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission and redeploy; audit re-runs\n  and confirms the gap closed.\n\nThe image release version is v0.6.2 (not v0.6.1): chart 0.6.1 already\nclaims that string. Fix in the PR body was pushed separately.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWpdiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxEMQALHpK5osG0kILeJp6nDxZiNt\ni7Ql9dcUBFVNo9He9sMbVkmX+STmQuMFvyXZAeNDshKoyA1L3GsaoZ/FYd4wfAjo\nS4fpvzG07qyFYD77l+OKKodtvG7bi0uhwhftPYDGgBy4sovvqRgAHLMjDeT02y7Y\nR87N0hQKUJUZvP5RYQJLPj6088QWcIA7K4HBc7Kb2EVB9c5xs8DV/zWWDpLUiM/q\nZgKT+1XvgMFAoaxDsHzYlKm6nDKo3mc53/zYHjlrwmU7BhEyqbdw38zo2l3JmMKJ\ngbZVJHsJ5hSugGXA2vlu3EYqwsJgPEAB0FN5uWSEC59hX25xcNCeT427HhDkeX9/\n7xoxzCYei0DrC3P/MwIwhZT2pvrukXdy9S3YRcrn9gMdUsd2i6KzODqO/m9awtU5\ng5UEtv093eWNKCWlLbceKDyCyMWAHpXSKJZ0I73IDSiD8olUE3P9l4h7XNdAetUd\nCt0OmSO3geMDgrNxnoEgkakvRPfIt5dqD3HOdvsZELHIlPbPbRW6cgj+Pc47MSAL\nUVf8b8+sQ22oUFW5Pe6ZdYlPY0HZYGn8NsBgiU+KPtMAj/CBkMNCUES3o+Vwy8l6\nt5mSP639XpTf/f/+0BIParaJyeJ0NsJIgcEe/GbzIZkf+3w2sBqks3sFANsZeVl7\nwHoaqQ3pu9HXyCfSOguc\n=tsTn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T20:58:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGQ2OGRhMGM1NzY4MzYyODhiNThlNTg2ZDBhNDg3ZWQ2MGFkYjg1NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109","sha":"60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109"}],"sha":"d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/d68da0c576836288b58e586d0a487ed60adb8553"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T19:18:06Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T19:18:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chart(0.6.1): bump for pluginsWithPermission guard + fatigue fix (#63)\n\nShips the #42 guard to adopters (chart 0.6.0 was cut before #42 merged,\nso the guard has been sitting on main but not in the released\nartifact), and folds in the #60 fatigue fix so warn-loudly ships as\nsignal instead of noise.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Chart.yaml version 0.6.0 -> 0.6.1. appVersion stays 0.6.0; no image\n  change. Template-only release.\n- warnRbacUnopted helper now skips plugin entries with:\n  - `disabled: true` — plugin not loaded; permissions not in play.\n  - `permissions.declared: false` — explicit operator assertion that\n    the plugin declares no permissions.\n  - `permissions.enforced: true` — opted into the structural guard.\n- values.yaml plugin-entry comment now documents all three\n  categorizations plus their intended use cases (declaring plugins,\n  UI-only plugins, temporarily-disabled plugins).\n\n## Why\n\nWarn-loudly on 0.6.0''s chart source would fire on every plugin entry\nregardless of whether it declares permissions. Rendering the four\nCorteva live values files against 0.6.0-source produced 7-9 warning\nlines per cluster — every RHDH catalog provider, auth provider, and\nfrontend widget appearing as \"authz is not running\" despite declaring\nno permissions. That is empirical noise; noise is how warnings get\nskipped; skipped warnings are how the mechanism dies.\n\n`permissions.declared: false` gives operators a way to say \"I know\nthis plugin has no permissions\" once per entry and never see the\nwarning for that entry again. `disabled: true` skips automatically\nsince a plugin that is not loaded has no authz to run. Warn now\nsurfaces only genuinely uncategorized entries — the ones that should\nbe a call to action.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n56/56 helm-unittest tests pass. New coverage in\ntests/rbac-warn-unopted_test.yaml:\n\n- skips disabled plugins from the warn\n- permissions.declared=false silences the warn\n- permissions.declared=true (or absent) still warns\n- real-fleet mix (enforced + declared:false + disabled + one\n  uncategorized) warns only about the uncategorized one\n\nLive-values render check: all four Corteva values files\n(crop-dev, crop-prd, seed-dev, seed-prd) render clean against the\n0.6.1 chart. Guard is a no-op today because no cluster has opted in;\nwarn is loud today because no cluster has categorized yet. Both\ncorrect.\n\n## Release path\n\nMerge -> tag `butler-portal-v0.6.1` -> Helm workflow packages and\npublishes to oci://ghcr.io/butlerdotdev/charts. Adopter values files\nbump `chart.spec.version` to `\"0.6.1\"` per cluster to pick up the\nguard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef7db0c0afe57240c23a173bcfc77b54386d255e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/ef7db0c0afe57240c23a173bcfc77b54386d255e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109","verification":{"payload":"tree ef7db0c0afe57240c23a173bcfc77b54386d255e\nparent 22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784315886 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784315886 -0500\n\nchart(0.6.1): bump for pluginsWithPermission guard + fatigue fix (#63)\n\nShips the #42 guard to adopters (chart 0.6.0 was cut before #42 merged,\nso the guard has been sitting on main but not in the released\nartifact), and folds in the #60 fatigue fix so warn-loudly ships as\nsignal instead of noise.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Chart.yaml version 0.6.0 -> 0.6.1. appVersion stays 0.6.0; no image\n  change. Template-only release.\n- warnRbacUnopted helper now skips plugin entries with:\n  - `disabled: true` — plugin not loaded; permissions not in play.\n  - `permissions.declared: false` — explicit operator assertion that\n    the plugin declares no permissions.\n  - `permissions.enforced: true` — opted into the structural guard.\n- values.yaml plugin-entry comment now documents all three\n  categorizations plus their intended use cases (declaring plugins,\n  UI-only plugins, temporarily-disabled plugins).\n\n## Why\n\nWarn-loudly on 0.6.0''s chart source would fire on every plugin entry\nregardless of whether it declares permissions. Rendering the four\nCorteva live values files against 0.6.0-source produced 7-9 warning\nlines per cluster — every RHDH catalog provider, auth provider, and\nfrontend widget appearing as \"authz is not running\" despite declaring\nno permissions. That is empirical noise; noise is how warnings get\nskipped; skipped warnings are how the mechanism dies.\n\n`permissions.declared: false` gives operators a way to say \"I know\nthis plugin has no permissions\" once per entry and never see the\nwarning for that entry again. `disabled: true` skips automatically\nsince a plugin that is not loaded has no authz to run. Warn now\nsurfaces only genuinely uncategorized entries — the ones that should\nbe a call to action.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n56/56 helm-unittest tests pass. New coverage in\ntests/rbac-warn-unopted_test.yaml:\n\n- skips disabled plugins from the warn\n- permissions.declared=false silences the warn\n- permissions.declared=true (or absent) still warns\n- real-fleet mix (enforced + declared:false + disabled + one\n  uncategorized) warns only about the uncategorized one\n\nLive-values render check: all four Corteva values files\n(crop-dev, crop-prd, seed-dev, seed-prd) render clean against the\n0.6.1 chart. Guard is a no-op today because no cluster has opted in;\nwarn is loud today because no cluster has categorized yet. Both\ncorrect.\n\n## Release path\n\nMerge -> tag `butler-portal-v0.6.1` -> Helm workflow packages and\npublishes to oci://ghcr.io/butlerdotdev/charts. Adopter values files\nbump `chart.spec.version` to `\"0.6.1\"` per cluster to pick up the\nguard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWn/uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzhwQAEX47HZrD8yJQUMS5va4YUyn\n4m2u0PVtZQSr8SDRhj4ETbNC5KN5bNwR4jT+g2HWsrpubkpB6IrANLYw423JIPwj\n9Di31F9gQQMimkKug2oSUM3tt6uGcG/VMt8twr08o0tEK0vfa3FrH6umQG0TkrFv\nlNe2Dq8F8dTfI2PRKE4FhPtL72b1b8v3FplVy/5KI5unBrn2zdfy/BTQ5IyHCwaN\nF+86cKDh0oyXy4ImgOLq+VZpEnhVtpKNjonlM1RVNrtpAKA93lVW9Bebuj13AvJX\n1Bpte30dDPKDd/jBB1O/kYwwYW/KuJe1bW5ETYQKFg0V0/gbRGWlM9hf+WD+iXOL\nw+eRYSXL0WnetGEtkk57uR+ZBojbJI7QwGi0zGI4gdjRbZKdv0mcZUCcdqOj7P+d\nzWVeoD4NCpj2/lzFwLGR9MC6UVYcICIxMpCz6RD12L4sXONLJIbLcmp40VJjPklW\nIvmBlpyjHcAFccSQOUKwa0YxWjzqkrF33Ij6fgS+ZILdWCKB07GKkshOPN9Zox9e\nfjKXfwd9jvfq59vQyg+Tjit0Jaql+KzA2cXRPdu3zlPUx3V4lD6q5WwverN76nNb\nbI6q6iiCDuh/kqVQeOrSWRuKDxeYt9MTI/S9WbyNZWFlsfugL2lAJ84DuANlRS+o\nJX2LnROxWBdvrQAWA4g3\n=RjJS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T19:18:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDYwYjVkNDIzZGUwMGRmMTM5NDQyZDIwZmRjNDRhZjg1MmRhNmMxMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d","sha":"22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d"}],"sha":"60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/60b5d423de00df139442d20fdc44af852da6c109"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T16:30:33Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T16:30:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chart: pluginsWithPermission guard, opt-in per plugin, fail-loud on drift (#42)\n\nRBAC does not auto-discover plugin permissions. A plugin whose id is\nnot listed in permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission returns [] from\nthe discovery API and every authorize() call for it silently passes\nthrough as ALLOW regardless of policy. The failure mode has been\ndocumented four times in the tree and enforced zero times.\n\nThis turns the misconfiguration into a helm template failure at\ninstall/upgrade so it cannot ship to a running cluster.\n\nDesign:\n\n- Opt-in per plugin. Each entry in dynamicPlugins.plugins may declare\n  an optional `permissions: { pluginId, enforced }` block. When\n  `enforced: true`, the guard requires `pluginId` to be present in\n  `permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission`. Missing entry -> helm\n  template fails with an actionable error naming the plugin and the\n  missing id.\n- Backward-compatible. Entries without the `permissions` block are\n  ignored so existing values files install unchanged and purely-UI\n  dynamic plugins that declare no permissions do not need the block.\n- Wired from templates/deployment.yaml (always rendered), so the\n  check fires on every install/upgrade regardless of which subset of\n  templates the operator overrides.\n\nTest coverage in charts/butler-portal/tests/rbac-pluginswithpermission-\nguard_test.yaml:\n\n- Chart default renders (no plugins, guard no-op)\n- Plugin without permissions block renders (opt-out default)\n- Plugin with permissions.enforced=false renders (explicit opt-out)\n- Plugin enforced with pluginId listed in pluginsWithPermission renders\n- Enforced plugin missing from list FAILS with the actionable error\n- Enforced plugin with pluginsWithPermission=[] FAILS\n- Enforced without pluginId FAILS with instructive error\n- Multi-plugin (one wired, one missing) FAILS on the missing one\n\nFull suite: 44/44 passing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"a10e47f0133186aecc92b66a55fbb20ff3f00656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/a10e47f0133186aecc92b66a55fbb20ff3f00656"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d","verification":{"payload":"tree a10e47f0133186aecc92b66a55fbb20ff3f00656\nparent dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784305833 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784305833 -0500\n\nchart: pluginsWithPermission guard, opt-in per plugin, fail-loud on drift (#42)\n\nRBAC does not auto-discover plugin permissions. A plugin whose id is\nnot listed in permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission returns [] from\nthe discovery API and every authorize() call for it silently passes\nthrough as ALLOW regardless of policy. The failure mode has been\ndocumented four times in the tree and enforced zero times.\n\nThis turns the misconfiguration into a helm template failure at\ninstall/upgrade so it cannot ship to a running cluster.\n\nDesign:\n\n- Opt-in per plugin. Each entry in dynamicPlugins.plugins may declare\n  an optional `permissions: { pluginId, enforced }` block. When\n  `enforced: true`, the guard requires `pluginId` to be present in\n  `permission.rbac.pluginsWithPermission`. Missing entry -> helm\n  template fails with an actionable error naming the plugin and the\n  missing id.\n- Backward-compatible. Entries without the `permissions` block are\n  ignored so existing values files install unchanged and purely-UI\n  dynamic plugins that declare no permissions do not need the block.\n- Wired from templates/deployment.yaml (always rendered), so the\n  check fires on every install/upgrade regardless of which subset of\n  templates the operator overrides.\n\nTest coverage in charts/butler-portal/tests/rbac-pluginswithpermission-\nguard_test.yaml:\n\n- Chart default renders (no plugins, guard no-op)\n- Plugin without permissions block renders (opt-out default)\n- Plugin with permissions.enforced=false renders (explicit opt-out)\n- Plugin enforced with pluginId listed in pluginsWithPermission renders\n- Enforced plugin missing from list FAILS with the actionable error\n- Enforced plugin with pluginsWithPermission=[] FAILS\n- Enforced without pluginId FAILS with instructive error\n- Multi-plugin (one wired, one missing) FAILS on the missing one\n\nFull suite: 44/44 passing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWlipCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA81cQAG2hL50iY9jjs8H+4f7s4URq\ncDm1Uun52JQHLma6WZW4UgQ7u4EU3w188s3IkjydO3u4GZNt1/B8k4wX8O6HaaV/\nGWLktpocP3do78jSSR7avbdjv4qHqeF5Z8FjDAfNjlZB1rVeQWwtiZICCa7xKlMz\nd3YnPF1b93uPv9dRGiiihIb9mXKNtmbg/Fa4ToY10r71zjUMCvUWg3ETcKgoe+IC\nZvub8fPMLlGdehuj1Ps5Jlc3LAwwrvFm4rs+jjzkC+gDP3u9yILpy0K/YEbOOVCp\nJylpynpW3dK0/noCsmqEySPdcTqlX5F8hTfm2CD3c2n9QhdRvIdxEi9nX1o745B9\nObbkTDrz4Gapvt+rRVYprLk/HiOqV6TzcZgJgaRAno1bWVilMK3c+0+6WgMtfi5N\na4DuYAj+lrSbEeax8ikpcgPZToP88INC6yOZFCHJ7zRqdPbnAKYyqgkc9nlq0Nt1\nuHxlNI0UqtmQNLx5UeOCZv9SJiaygYyPu2oiMaKK3vpTFBRDXRJGDgiKRV85wXYm\neYYjC7AWws2TAg3tOL41bIcFBOa4WCKSCHFXF25WzjRbFi6T+ci/glRPRmjVa4HL\nUbPTCzYNV0CiRMbZAKF+KaMUl+8b9EX5AgSvb7MkHjH9u2oVf0tvLdpvfvPVFwtd\nnpbXS0T1EPApIrPSj9w9\n=ySY7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T16:30:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDIyZDc0YzkzNjYyNmUxYTcwNTgwOWZmZDI3NzEwOWRiZmU2MzliN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862","sha":"dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862"}],"sha":"22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/22d74c936626e1a705809ffd277109dbfe639b7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:35:19Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:35:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: note the npm ERESOLVE workaround for adopters writing a plugin from scratch (#58)\n\nThe runnable reference at examples/adopter-plugin ships an .npmrc that\nresolves the @backstage/cli@0.36.4 jsdom peer conflict npm 9+ rejects\n(fixed in butlerdotdev/butler-portal#57). Adopters who copy the\nexample inherit the file; adopters who write a plugin from scratch by\nfollowing this doc''s dep snippet do not.\n\nThe docs actively encourage the from-scratch path, so this leaves a\ngap the reference exists to solve. One paragraph after the dep\nsnippet closes it: instructions to add an .npmrc with\nlegacy-peer-deps=true if using npm, with a link to the reference''s\nown .npmrc for the exact contents.\n\nScope: bites any adopter running npm install against a butler-portal\nplugin. butler-portal itself and the PE plugin avoid it by using\nyarn; the conflict was latent everywhere until the docs-compile-check\nCI first exercised the npm path via the reference in #57.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"7879c1da1979f76d757f63d0a4d6fcd2e100790e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/7879c1da1979f76d757f63d0a4d6fcd2e100790e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862","verification":{"payload":"tree 7879c1da1979f76d757f63d0a4d6fcd2e100790e\nparent 1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784298919 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784298919 -0500\n\ndocs: note the npm ERESOLVE workaround for adopters writing a plugin from scratch (#58)\n\nThe runnable reference at examples/adopter-plugin ships an .npmrc that\nresolves the @backstage/cli@0.36.4 jsdom peer conflict npm 9+ rejects\n(fixed in butlerdotdev/butler-portal#57). Adopters who copy the\nexample inherit the file; adopters who write a plugin from scratch by\nfollowing this doc''s dep snippet do not.\n\nThe docs actively encourage the from-scratch path, so this leaves a\ngap the reference exists to solve. One paragraph after the dep\nsnippet closes it: instructions to add an .npmrc with\nlegacy-peer-deps=true if using npm, with a link to the reference''s\nown .npmrc for the exact contents.\n\nScope: bites any adopter running npm install against a butler-portal\nplugin. butler-portal itself and the PE plugin avoid it by using\nyarn; the conflict was latent everywhere until the docs-compile-check\nCI first exercised the npm path via the reference in #57.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWj2nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzpoQAAK29N2Afqrpu2efZB126iEm\nHzizaEptnpORAiNCvTBsXp/fqF5WXGtDiNHTN9o8ox+xZ/pbcqn1EiQkfFshjs9z\nvo4dDXIXZAA5Av4T2+16SDn6CEE5VBs8dh5jpIPeCUF/njDZ/3WcHciwvnueOpKK\nPd3NQbnpudBT1AxhGectVicioNU41j+P+4FUm0j+ReJFZK/CxNnxNAi2W3+0ED4t\nrqqkDGe4kXaq0WfFvw8Y69D9IlBBQ/7D4EajMQoiqNNRm9Jswc62JpQ4EFTCA9sj\nKeiQv6RtETJQTjUBewfvNk3qjlDSUl4QxOvtKCWfX6B93GT/aKj3dtS52id4Gg6I\nMQe3wNJPJ7Ny9bieq5fFRtCJHS9oYW/zr8mRUaKhqu/GbFGXcTdLg165ndT/BnD+\nWpLkOzC6Bs73ltJjPPQWX0+PV9y4FDH5s4y4ED74kwbWcv0ftVuElej6k1RhvNnm\nrJTmvt1yjnaa7hDpymr2Fbb/rj92geh+ZfHwhoDdqm6QhSY2ipPov3VSiLKZDwlC\nx3RQb8/Q1vQ4nohBPc7XaZ83CayspizEWTKQsW5e/b/csXmQsDWfkkcvSkSV3X2Q\nabj6iwZsKaYDOBxZHxFnZwVkepNkmhuRNQi698EhfPhrD89ug5leQFLee8/bdM0O\nTQ1Diqz48IPpNTAWSUry\n=qitY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T14:35:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGRkNzJhYmZhYmNiNGNkYTI4NDhlYmQyMmRhMWIxZDM4OWFkNGE4NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7","sha":"1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7"}],"sha":"dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/dd72abfabcb4cda2848ebd22da1b1d389ad4a862"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:16:32Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:16:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(#52): adopter-plugin reference installs + compiles; drop continue-on-error (#57)\n\n* fix: make the adopter-plugin reference actually installable and compilable\n\nThe docs in butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41 cite examples/adopter-plugin\nas ground truth for the RBAC plugin pattern. CI (added in #54) surfaced\nthat the reference does not install and does not compile — two layers,\nthe second masked behind the first.\n\nFixes both layers and removes continue-on-error from #54''s workflow;\nthat removal is the acceptance test for butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52.\n\nLayer 1: npm ERESOLVE on jsdom peer conflict\n---------------------------------------------\n\n@backstage/cli@0.36.4 declares peerOptional jsdom@^27.1.0 while its\nown transitive jest-environment-jsdom@30.4.1 brings jsdom@29. npm 9+\nenforces this strictly; yarn (used everywhere else in the repo)\nresolves it via looser peer semantics.\n\nScope: bites anywhere `npm install` runs against a dep tree pulling\n@backstage/cli@0.36.4. That is nearly every package.json in the\nrepo. butler-portal itself and the PE plugin avoid it by using yarn.\nThe example surfaced it first because it was the first thing in\nthe repo to install via npm (via #54''s CI step). Not example-\nspecific.\n\nFix: examples/adopter-plugin/backend/.npmrc pins\nlegacy-peer-deps=true. The .npmrc is picked up automatically by any\nnpm invocation in that directory, so adopters copying the example\ninherit the workaround. scripts/docs-compile-check.mjs also passes\n--legacy-peer-deps to its harness install for consistency — the\nharness dep set does not currently pull @backstage/cli, so this is\nfuture-proofing rather than an active fix, kept aligned so a future\nCLI-adjacent doc dep does not hit ERESOLVE from a different install\nsemantic than the rest of the repo.\n\nLayer 2: TS2589 excessively-deep on createPermissionRule\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\nUnder @backstage/plugin-permission-node@0.11.2 + zod@^3.25.76, the\ninference path for CreatePermissionRuleOptions<TRef, TParams> from a\nzod-derived paramsSchema produces `Type instantiation is excessively\ndeep`. TypeScript falls back to the deprecated overload, which\ninfers TParams as `undefined`, cascading into TS18048 params-is-\nundefined at the callback sites.\n\nFix: explicit generic parameters on createPermissionRule at the call\nsite pin TRef and TParams so inference does not have to derive TParams\nfrom the zod output. Same fix the plugin-authoring docs adopted for\ntheir worked example.\n\nAdditional: examples/adopter-plugin/backend/tsconfig.json\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nWithout an example-local tsconfig, `npx tsc --noEmit src/*.ts` walks\nthe full 1612-package dep tree and OOMs the default 4GB Node heap. A\nminimal tsconfig extending @backstage/cli/config/tsconfig.json with\ntypes: [] (since the example has no tests) scopes the compile to\nsrc/**/* and finishes in seconds.\n\nWorkflow\n--------\n\n.github/workflows/docs-compile-check.yml drops continue-on-error:\ntrue from both adopter-plugin steps and switches tsc to use the new\ntsconfig. Both steps are now enforced. Landing #52 becomes true\nend to end: the docs point at a reference that installs, compiles,\nand stays that way in CI.\n\n* example: drop accidentally-committed package-lock.json + gitignore it\n\nThe example is a reference adopters copy; a lockfile pins transitive\nversions the adopter''s environment may not want. butler-portal uses\nyarn everywhere else in the tree, so an npm lockfile in one example\ndirectory reads as unintentional. CI regenerates deps on each run\nagainst the declared range; adopters do the same when they copy the\nexample to their own repo.\n\n.gitignore covers node_modules and dist outputs at the same time so\na future `npm install` in this directory does not silently pull the\nlockfile back into the diff.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d0b1206501133c611e8acd70e56b96b6d560932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/9d0b1206501133c611e8acd70e56b96b6d560932"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d0b1206501133c611e8acd70e56b96b6d560932\nparent 92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784297792 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784297792 -0500\n\nfix(#52): adopter-plugin reference installs + compiles; drop continue-on-error (#57)\n\n* fix: make the adopter-plugin reference actually installable and compilable\n\nThe docs in butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41 cite examples/adopter-plugin\nas ground truth for the RBAC plugin pattern. CI (added in #54) surfaced\nthat the reference does not install and does not compile — two layers,\nthe second masked behind the first.\n\nFixes both layers and removes continue-on-error from #54''s workflow;\nthat removal is the acceptance test for butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52.\n\nLayer 1: npm ERESOLVE on jsdom peer conflict\n---------------------------------------------\n\n@backstage/cli@0.36.4 declares peerOptional jsdom@^27.1.0 while its\nown transitive jest-environment-jsdom@30.4.1 brings jsdom@29. npm 9+\nenforces this strictly; yarn (used everywhere else in the repo)\nresolves it via looser peer semantics.\n\nScope: bites anywhere `npm install` runs against a dep tree pulling\n@backstage/cli@0.36.4. That is nearly every package.json in the\nrepo. butler-portal itself and the PE plugin avoid it by using yarn.\nThe example surfaced it first because it was the first thing in\nthe repo to install via npm (via #54''s CI step). Not example-\nspecific.\n\nFix: examples/adopter-plugin/backend/.npmrc pins\nlegacy-peer-deps=true. The .npmrc is picked up automatically by any\nnpm invocation in that directory, so adopters copying the example\ninherit the workaround. scripts/docs-compile-check.mjs also passes\n--legacy-peer-deps to its harness install for consistency — the\nharness dep set does not currently pull @backstage/cli, so this is\nfuture-proofing rather than an active fix, kept aligned so a future\nCLI-adjacent doc dep does not hit ERESOLVE from a different install\nsemantic than the rest of the repo.\n\nLayer 2: TS2589 excessively-deep on createPermissionRule\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\nUnder @backstage/plugin-permission-node@0.11.2 + zod@^3.25.76, the\ninference path for CreatePermissionRuleOptions<TRef, TParams> from a\nzod-derived paramsSchema produces `Type instantiation is excessively\ndeep`. TypeScript falls back to the deprecated overload, which\ninfers TParams as `undefined`, cascading into TS18048 params-is-\nundefined at the callback sites.\n\nFix: explicit generic parameters on createPermissionRule at the call\nsite pin TRef and TParams so inference does not have to derive TParams\nfrom the zod output. Same fix the plugin-authoring docs adopted for\ntheir worked example.\n\nAdditional: examples/adopter-plugin/backend/tsconfig.json\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nWithout an example-local tsconfig, `npx tsc --noEmit src/*.ts` walks\nthe full 1612-package dep tree and OOMs the default 4GB Node heap. A\nminimal tsconfig extending @backstage/cli/config/tsconfig.json with\ntypes: [] (since the example has no tests) scopes the compile to\nsrc/**/* and finishes in seconds.\n\nWorkflow\n--------\n\n.github/workflows/docs-compile-check.yml drops continue-on-error:\ntrue from both adopter-plugin steps and switches tsc to use the new\ntsconfig. Both steps are now enforced. Landing #52 becomes true\nend to end: the docs point at a reference that installs, compiles,\nand stays that way in CI.\n\n* example: drop accidentally-committed package-lock.json + gitignore it\n\nThe example is a reference adopters copy; a lockfile pins transitive\nversions the adopter''s environment may not want. butler-portal uses\nyarn everywhere else in the tree, so an npm lockfile in one example\ndirectory reads as unintentional. CI regenerates deps on each run\nagainst the declared range; adopters do the same when they copy the\nexample to their own repo.\n\n.gitignore covers node_modules and dist outputs at the same time so\na future `npm install` in this directory does not silently pull the\nlockfile back into the diff.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWjlACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvw0QAI6muxYMmnXehfh8QHkLLqcs\nXLCQbEkJHi5B0337itiJRPnKxcbXTVVQe92in0r4VQP1E5K4C/zoU9lAnuunEJbY\niVcwN6OOGsbF8fpePoVLCHjngfmkufLNxExIKXqba5j0fVzzoWIwq/Xp9AhohJKo\nlNhYVIdkVieCXbHADadi2ghbQ/Z2Lp7XSV0vRPApBkASci2lLHgQWQpFDfJ5pNAV\nEt+V35BKGWPKduR7EUiLKY86czd3ZoBrVGYu5ttdieSBn9Ulj5CXIYIgkMm/s7jp\n8fP/LRQhOh/w2Pv/VReTqPkHUTmxvJVoTre97eAiBIPy/CQCETrTIC0v1XipsoRr\n2N4q8CN3FkhMob8NOSN/l3q0ZmxkcwUCxDjqAugtAGVI67g2N47WCO0pdu7mHWsX\n5tHchCCIeZLr4OJ/HTH1Bdf+T/uxlYBXZoBbxlxQWJfu0MF0yDL8B4vtQt4OzB/J\nDGjAxax5ScwUM8KbaxneLu/+Ojh0tBxzccVMMcGD61DDsRE0CnNbgBbJQpD3SIqp\newbWCVZWDduQdXaXSZZ7OM5n+R34qX4NlUsL/1XCnS61QfAt46KNeFComPZCnEUc\nsOOT2Vo3Aho/lpzeismPBNEzRHLCPJ9TlLA1owMB3erN7OXsyaYF3CaN5FKm5PRg\n0uj1La3Mxd7ntKzVF5UD\n=WogD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T14:16:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDFmNTA5NTJjMzQ1MWY0NjM0N2YwMmQyOGJhNzVlOTA2ZmZmMzFjYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3","sha":"92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3"}],"sha":"1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/1f50952c3451f46347f02d28ba75e906fff31cb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T13:37:20Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T13:37:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: RBAC permission framework + updated plugin authoring guide (#41)\n\n* docs: cover the RBAC permission framework and update plugin authoring guide\n\nButler Portal 0.6.0 adopted @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend\nas the single authorization surface, retiring the earlier\nButlerPortalDelegatingPolicy adjudicator seam. The docs still described\nthe removed seam and did not explain how the shipped default policy\nworks or what adopters must configure.\n\nTwo new / rewritten pages:\n\n- docs/architecture/permissions.md: framework overview, shipped\n  default policy shape (portal-user vs portal-privileged pattern),\n  superUsers bypass, how adopters plug in, migration guidance from\n  the pre-0.6.0 adjudicator seam, and the known gotchas that were\n  surfaced during the RBAC adoption arc.\n\n- docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md: rewritten from the\n  adjudicator-seam pattern to the direct-authorize pattern. Contract\n  at a glance, a minimal working example (permissions.ts, router.ts\n  with a requirePermission helper, module.ts), the adopter\n  configuration adopters must add, frontend visibility via\n  usePermission, testing recipes, prefix conventions, and the\n  PERMISSIONS.md contract every declaring plugin should ship.\n\nPlus link updates in the plugin-authoring and architecture READMEs.\n\n* docs: correct chart-default role names and cover both admin tiers\n\nReview-pass 2 fixes. The previous commit described Corteva-shape role\noverrides as if they were the chart defaults, and omitted the RBAC\npolicy-admin tier entirely. Also stitched dynamic-plugins/authoring\noff the retired adjudicator-seam wording it still linked into.\n\n- Restored the chart-shipped role names: role:default/butler-portal-\n  user for the default reader tier, role:default/butler-portal-admin\n  for the privileged tier granted the Backstage-core writes.\n- Restored the chart-shipped defaultPermissions basicPermissions\n  (reads only; the scaffolder write permissions are in the CSV, not\n  in defaults).\n- Called out the PLACEHOLDER-ADMIN-GROUP binding fresh adopters\n  must replace before non-superUser writes work.\n- Added the two-admin-tier explanation (admin.users are policy admins\n  who manage RBAC via UI/API but do not get automatic write access to\n  other plugins; admin.superUsers bypass evaluation entirely).\n- Corrected the /rbac UI description (read-write for policy admins,\n  not read-only inspection).\n- Removed the DB-scheduler gotcha bullet from architecture/permissions\n  (off-topic for a permissions doc).\n- Updated the adopter-config example in plugin-authoring/authorization\n  to reference role:default/butler-portal-admin so a plugin author\n  following the doc sees consistency with the shipped chart.\n- Updated dynamic-plugins/authoring''s permissions link paragraph off\n  the retired namespace-delegated seam wording.\n\n* docs: address the substantive gaps found in pass-2/pass-3 review\n\nEvery fix here is either linking the concrete artifact or shipping the\nmissing step. No prescription without its mechanism.\n\n- P1#1: split superUsers vs replacing PLACEHOLDER-ADMIN-GROUP as two\n  INDEPENDENT unblockers, not one requirement. Prior wording read as\n  \"must populate superUsers or nobody can write\" which is wrong — the\n  chart''s placeholder-group binding is a separate unblocker.\n- P1#2: cut the \"disable admin-UI writes\" prescription and replace with\n  the concrete lever. RBAC has no toggle; keeping admin.users empty is\n  the mechanism, and that''s now stated explicitly.\n- P1#3: clarify \"applied on every reload\" — Helm rewrites the\n  ConfigMap, kubelet syncs the file mount, RBAC''s watcher re-reads\n  because policyFileReload is true by chart default. No pod restart.\n- P2#2: fresh-adopter bootstrap now an ordered checklist. Walks the\n  first-boot state (safe but bricked: signed-in reads OK, gated writes\n  blocked, /rbac inaccessible because admin.users is empty) and gives\n  the numbered edit sequence to unbrick.\n- P2#3: pre-upgrade warning at the TOP of the migration section, not\n  the end. Retrospective guidance is not migration guidance. In-tree\n  plugins fail at build, pre-built dynamic-plugin OCI artifacts fail\n  at load, and the loader error can be non-prominent.\n- P3#1: link examples/adopter-plugin from both docs, at the top so\n  readers hit it before the prose. Every code snippet has a working\n  counterpart there.\n- P3#2: cover permissionsRegistry.addResourceType + createPermissionRule\n  end-to-end (rule declaration, addResourceType registration, authorize\n  with resourceRef, conditionalPoliciesFile YAML referencing the rule).\n  Point at examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/{plugin,rule}.ts for\n  the working version.\n- P3#3: httpRouter.addAuthPolicy({ path, allow: ''user-cookie'' }) is\n  now in the minimal example, with a comment explaining what breaks\n  without it (browser 401 before authorize() runs).\n- P3#4: name the RBAC FRONTEND package @backstage-community/plugin-rbac\n  and its baselineRoutes wiring. Prior version described /rbac\n  behavior without saying how it gets there — adopters bringing their\n  own Backstage app would end up with backend policy evaluation and\n  no admin UI.\n\nP1 unverified: verified permission.rbac.conditionalPoliciesFile spelling\nagainst RBAC''s config.d.ts on backstage/community-plugins main. Correct\nas written.\n\n* docs: fix compile-breakers, split bootstrap from enforcement, cross-cite\n\nEvery fix here either (a) prevents the doc from generating broken code,\nor (b) prevents the safety-critical enforcement step from reading as\noptional. Remaining Pass 2 / Pass 3 items are tracked as issues.\n\n- P1#1 (compile-breaker): BasicPermission -> addResourceType type\n  mismatch. Note that rule-bound permissions must be ResourcePermission\n  (add resourceType to the createPermission call). Re-declares\n  myPluginThingReadPermission with resourceType inside the conditional\n  section so a reader copying verbatim compiles. Points at\n  examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/permissions.ts:3-7.\n\n- P1#2 (runtime-breaker): Thing type now matches the working reference\n  at examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/rule.ts:7 (owner?: string).\n  apply() uses resource?.owner === expectedOwner so a resource missing\n  the field does not throw. Same defensiveness as the reference.\n\n- P1 unverified: loadThingById is now defined as loadThingsById with an\n  explicit signature (refs: string[]) => Promise<Array<Thing | undefined>>\n  and a comment explaining what returning undefined means (DENY per the\n  working reference''s optional-owner shape).\n\n- P3#2 (missing dep): copy-pasters were hitting Cannot find module ''zod''.\n  Added a dependencies snippet showing the four packages the conditional\n  example needs, sourced from examples/adopter-plugin/backend/package.json.\n\n- P2#1 (safety-critical checklist gap): the single flat 5-step checklist\n  is now split into \"A. Bootstrap access\" (steps 1-3, recovery mechanics)\n  and \"B. Wire plugin enforcement\" (steps 4-5, the pluginsWithPermission\n  gate). Step 4 is now marked REQUIRED with the explicit failure mode\n  spelled out (\"every plugin''s writes silently allowed regardless of\n  your CSV\") so an adopter who does block A but skips block B cannot\n  mistake the flat list as complete.\n\n- P3#4 (cross-cite): the failure-modes entry on `---` YAML separators\n  now points forward to the Conditional policies section (which has\n  the working YAML shape), and the Conditional policies section points\n  back to Failure modes. The YAML footgun is documented once\n  substantively and once as a cross-reference in each doc.\n\nCross-links to open work:\n- Testing section now links butlerdotdev/butler-portal#43 so a reader\n  looking for mockPermissionsService and fixture-boot helpers knows\n  they are tracked.\n- pluginsWithPermission gotchas in both docs now cite the opt-in\n  structural guard from butlerdotdev/butler-portal#42\n  (permissions.enforced: true) as the mechanism that fails helm at\n  install/upgrade when the wiring is missing.\n\n* docs: frame BasicPermission vs ResourcePermission as alternative paths + compile-check the samples\n\nTwo prior amendments fixed compile-breakers by renaming symbols and\nretracting claims. Both left the generator intact: the docs had grown\na second code path (BasicPermission minimal example -> ResourcePermission\nconditional example) that shared an identifier, a permission name, and\nnever told the reader whether they were alternatives or additions.\n\nThis amendment fixes the framing at the fork:\n\n- authorization.md \"Minimal example\" now opens with a note that this\n  pattern is for UNCONDITIONAL gating (BasicPermission), and forwards\n  to the conditional section for the alternative. Says explicitly that\n  a plugin declares both kinds, one per permission.\n- authorization.md \"Conditional policies\" now opens with the alternative-\n  paths framing spelled out (BasicPermission vs ResourcePermission +\n  rule, pick per permission, both coexist in the same permissions.ts).\n  Uses a NEW permission name (myplugin.thing.delete) that does not\n  collide with the minimal example''s read/write.\n- No re-declaration of the minimal example''s permissions inside the\n  conditional section; the \"extends\" block adds the new conditional\n  permission alongside the existing unconditional ones.\n\nCompile-check applied. All four sample files\n(permissions.ts, rule.ts, router.ts, module.ts) copied verbatim into a\nfresh backend with the doc''s declared dependency versions, tsc --noEmit\nnow exits 0.\n\nThe rule.ts shape drops paramsSchema and types the callback params\nexplicitly. Reason: plugin-permission-node@0.11.2 + zod@^3.25.76\nproduces TS2589 \"Type instantiation is excessively deep\" on both the\nworking reference at examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/rule.ts AND\nany adopter code following the reference shape verbatim.\nFiled butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52. The compiling shape behaves\nidentically at runtime; the runtime schema validation paramsSchema\nwould have supplied is deferred until #52 lands.\n\nOther fixes:\n\n- P1 (softened claim): the getResources code comment previously said\n  \"RBAC evaluates apply(undefined) as DENY\" -- a framework guarantee\n  the amendment did not verify against RBAC source. Rewritten as an\n  observation about the rule''s return-value handling: an undefined\n  resource returns false from apply(), and a false rule result means\n  DENY unless another policy row grants unconditionally.\n- P3#1 (@backstage/errors dep): now in the conditional-section\n  dependency snippet with a note that it supplies NotAllowedError\n  used by the minimal example.\n- P2#1 (duplicate unblocker lists in permissions.md): the two\n  overlapping numbered lists are collapsed. Block A now opens with\n  the \"two independent levers\" as commentary, then the three numbered\n  steps of the typical setup.\n- P2#3 (circular cross-cite on --- YAML separator): substantive\n  misleading-error text stays in the failure-modes entry; the\n  conditional-policies section links there without duplicating the\n  content. One-way substance, one-way pointer.\n- P3#4 (Block B assumes Block A): explicit note added at the top of\n  Block B that step 5 needs an admin-group member from Block A.\n- P3#5 (guard is opt-in): both cross-cites now say the guard defaults\n  to OFF per plugin entry; an adopter who does not opt in gets the\n  same silent pass-through the bullet describes.\n- P2#5 (rollout gate is a norm, not a mechanism): the Block B step 5\n  language now says \"Blocking the rollout on this check is a norm\n  today, not a mechanism\" and points at #42 for the structural fix.\n\n* docs: fix compile-breakers, annotate fenced blocks for CI compile-check, fold in review items\n\nPass 1 of the last review ran tsc and caught two doc bugs the earlier\nreads missed: rule.ts''s createPermissionRule needs explicit generic\nparameters or TypeScript picks the deprecated overload and infers\nTParams as undefined; router.ts imported from ''../permissions'' while\nthe prose said sibling layout. Both fixed. Sample now compiles clean\nunder strict:true.\n\nStructural fix arriving alongside: every fenced code block in the\ndoc that is meant to compile has a title=\"<file>\" annotation. Blocks\nthat are fragments or wrong-language for the harness are marked\nnoCompile. A separate PR ships .github/workflows/docs-compile-check.yml\nthat extracts the title-annotated blocks and runs tsc --noEmit; this\ndoc no longer relies on reviewer discipline for \"compiles clean\"\nclaims. The prose about compile status now points at the CI workflow.\n\nFold-ins from the last review:\n\n- P1#1 rule.ts: added explicit generics\n  createPermissionRule<typeof thingResourceRef, { expectedOwner: string }>({...}).\n  Callback signatures now infer TParams correctly.\n- P1#2 router.ts: import from ''./permissions'' to match the sibling\n  layout the prose describes. Also fixed the same class in module.ts\n  which imported from ''./routes/router''; adopters following the doc\n  put router.ts as a sibling, not in a routes/ subdir.\n- P3#1 paramsSchema/zod consequence chain: explicit note that adding\n  paramsSchema + zod re-introduces the TS2589 error until #52 lands.\n  Readers who skip #52 no longer discover this by hitting it.\n- P3#2 delete verb rationale: one sentence added on why delete is a\n  natural conditional-gating fit (scopes to the resource''s owner).\n- P3#3 \"Extends\" -> \"Add these lines\": the earlier phrasing read\n  as TypeScript inheritance. Renamed to be unambiguous.\n- P2#2 rule-not-compiling as early warning: explicit paragraph\n  drawing the chain from \"cast past the error\" to silent-passthrough\n  when the plugin''s guard opt-in is off.\n\nWorking reference status: butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52 tracks that\nexamples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/rule.ts itself does not compile\nagainst its declared dependency versions. The doc uses the compiling\nshape and cross-references the issue.\n\n* docs: fold review items + tighten noCompile markers to include reasons\n\nFollow-up from the fourth 3-pass review on the docs-compile-check\nintegration. Two Pass 3 items and a contract-tightening on the\nnoCompile marker (noCompile now requires a reason per CI hook\ntightening in butlerdotdev/butler-portal#54).\n\n- Bare `noCompile` markers on the loadThingsById fragment and the\n  frontend WriteButton tsx block now carry explicit reasons\n  (`noCompile=\"illustrative fragment — ...\"`, etc.). The tightened CI\n  in #54 fails on bare noCompile so the opt-out is visible in the\n  diff and to reviewers.\n- Added a \"Reproducing the CI compile-check locally\" note explaining\n  that the harness adds express, express-promise-router, typescript,\n  and @types/express on top of the doc''s dep snippet. A reader\n  building a local harness from the snippet verbatim was hitting\n  Cannot find module ''express'' with no signal why.\n- Added a short adopter-facing summary of the fence-annotation\n  contract (title, append, noCompile with reason, unannotated =\n  fail). Points at scripts/docs-compile-check.mjs for the mechanism.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"97eb00d7fb94fbd1ab7b4c9be67a8d5e1072796e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/97eb00d7fb94fbd1ab7b4c9be67a8d5e1072796e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3","verification":{"payload":"tree 97eb00d7fb94fbd1ab7b4c9be67a8d5e1072796e\nparent 363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784295440 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784295440 -0500\n\ndocs: RBAC permission framework + updated plugin authoring guide (#41)\n\n* docs: cover the RBAC permission framework and update plugin authoring guide\n\nButler Portal 0.6.0 adopted @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend\nas the single authorization surface, retiring the earlier\nButlerPortalDelegatingPolicy adjudicator seam. The docs still described\nthe removed seam and did not explain how the shipped default policy\nworks or what adopters must configure.\n\nTwo new / rewritten pages:\n\n- docs/architecture/permissions.md: framework overview, shipped\n  default policy shape (portal-user vs portal-privileged pattern),\n  superUsers bypass, how adopters plug in, migration guidance from\n  the pre-0.6.0 adjudicator seam, and the known gotchas that were\n  surfaced during the RBAC adoption arc.\n\n- docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md: rewritten from the\n  adjudicator-seam pattern to the direct-authorize pattern. Contract\n  at a glance, a minimal working example (permissions.ts, router.ts\n  with a requirePermission helper, module.ts), the adopter\n  configuration adopters must add, frontend visibility via\n  usePermission, testing recipes, prefix conventions, and the\n  PERMISSIONS.md contract every declaring plugin should ship.\n\nPlus link updates in the plugin-authoring and architecture READMEs.\n\n* docs: correct chart-default role names and cover both admin tiers\n\nReview-pass 2 fixes. The previous commit described Corteva-shape role\noverrides as if they were the chart defaults, and omitted the RBAC\npolicy-admin tier entirely. Also stitched dynamic-plugins/authoring\noff the retired adjudicator-seam wording it still linked into.\n\n- Restored the chart-shipped role names: role:default/butler-portal-\n  user for the default reader tier, role:default/butler-portal-admin\n  for the privileged tier granted the Backstage-core writes.\n- Restored the chart-shipped defaultPermissions basicPermissions\n  (reads only; the scaffolder write permissions are in the CSV, not\n  in defaults).\n- Called out the PLACEHOLDER-ADMIN-GROUP binding fresh adopters\n  must replace before non-superUser writes work.\n- Added the two-admin-tier explanation (admin.users are policy admins\n  who manage RBAC via UI/API but do not get automatic write access to\n  other plugins; admin.superUsers bypass evaluation entirely).\n- Corrected the /rbac UI description (read-write for policy admins,\n  not read-only inspection).\n- Removed the DB-scheduler gotcha bullet from architecture/permissions\n  (off-topic for a permissions doc).\n- Updated the adopter-config example in plugin-authoring/authorization\n  to reference role:default/butler-portal-admin so a plugin author\n  following the doc sees consistency with the shipped chart.\n- Updated dynamic-plugins/authoring''s permissions link paragraph off\n  the retired namespace-delegated seam wording.\n\n* docs: address the substantive gaps found in pass-2/pass-3 review\n\nEvery fix here is either linking the concrete artifact or shipping the\nmissing step. No prescription without its mechanism.\n\n- P1#1: split superUsers vs replacing PLACEHOLDER-ADMIN-GROUP as two\n  INDEPENDENT unblockers, not one requirement. Prior wording read as\n  \"must populate superUsers or nobody can write\" which is wrong — the\n  chart''s placeholder-group binding is a separate unblocker.\n- P1#2: cut the \"disable admin-UI writes\" prescription and replace with\n  the concrete lever. RBAC has no toggle; keeping admin.users empty is\n  the mechanism, and that''s now stated explicitly.\n- P1#3: clarify \"applied on every reload\" — Helm rewrites the\n  ConfigMap, kubelet syncs the file mount, RBAC''s watcher re-reads\n  because policyFileReload is true by chart default. No pod restart.\n- P2#2: fresh-adopter bootstrap now an ordered checklist. Walks the\n  first-boot state (safe but bricked: signed-in reads OK, gated writes\n  blocked, /rbac inaccessible because admin.users is empty) and gives\n  the numbered edit sequence to unbrick.\n- P2#3: pre-upgrade warning at the TOP of the migration section, not\n  the end. Retrospective guidance is not migration guidance. In-tree\n  plugins fail at build, pre-built dynamic-plugin OCI artifacts fail\n  at load, and the loader error can be non-prominent.\n- P3#1: link examples/adopter-plugin from both docs, at the top so\n  readers hit it before the prose. Every code snippet has a working\n  counterpart there.\n- P3#2: cover permissionsRegistry.addResourceType + createPermissionRule\n  end-to-end (rule declaration, addResourceType registration, authorize\n  with resourceRef, conditionalPoliciesFile YAML referencing the rule).\n  Point at examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/{plugin,rule}.ts for\n  the working version.\n- P3#3: httpRouter.addAuthPolicy({ path, allow: ''user-cookie'' }) is\n  now in the minimal example, with a comment explaining what breaks\n  without it (browser 401 before authorize() runs).\n- P3#4: name the RBAC FRONTEND package @backstage-community/plugin-rbac\n  and its baselineRoutes wiring. Prior version described /rbac\n  behavior without saying how it gets there — adopters bringing their\n  own Backstage app would end up with backend policy evaluation and\n  no admin UI.\n\nP1 unverified: verified permission.rbac.conditionalPoliciesFile spelling\nagainst RBAC''s config.d.ts on backstage/community-plugins main. Correct\nas written.\n\n* docs: fix compile-breakers, split bootstrap from enforcement, cross-cite\n\nEvery fix here either (a) prevents the doc from generating broken code,\nor (b) prevents the safety-critical enforcement step from reading as\noptional. Remaining Pass 2 / Pass 3 items are tracked as issues.\n\n- P1#1 (compile-breaker): BasicPermission -> addResourceType type\n  mismatch. Note that rule-bound permissions must be ResourcePermission\n  (add resourceType to the createPermission call). Re-declares\n  myPluginThingReadPermission with resourceType inside the conditional\n  section so a reader copying verbatim compiles. Points at\n  examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/permissions.ts:3-7.\n\n- P1#2 (runtime-breaker): Thing type now matches the working reference\n  at examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/rule.ts:7 (owner?: string).\n  apply() uses resource?.owner === expectedOwner so a resource missing\n  the field does not throw. Same defensiveness as the reference.\n\n- P1 unverified: loadThingById is now defined as loadThingsById with an\n  explicit signature (refs: string[]) => Promise<Array<Thing | undefined>>\n  and a comment explaining what returning undefined means (DENY per the\n  working reference''s optional-owner shape).\n\n- P3#2 (missing dep): copy-pasters were hitting Cannot find module ''zod''.\n  Added a dependencies snippet showing the four packages the conditional\n  example needs, sourced from examples/adopter-plugin/backend/package.json.\n\n- P2#1 (safety-critical checklist gap): the single flat 5-step checklist\n  is now split into \"A. Bootstrap access\" (steps 1-3, recovery mechanics)\n  and \"B. Wire plugin enforcement\" (steps 4-5, the pluginsWithPermission\n  gate). Step 4 is now marked REQUIRED with the explicit failure mode\n  spelled out (\"every plugin''s writes silently allowed regardless of\n  your CSV\") so an adopter who does block A but skips block B cannot\n  mistake the flat list as complete.\n\n- P3#4 (cross-cite): the failure-modes entry on `---` YAML separators\n  now points forward to the Conditional policies section (which has\n  the working YAML shape), and the Conditional policies section points\n  back to Failure modes. The YAML footgun is documented once\n  substantively and once as a cross-reference in each doc.\n\nCross-links to open work:\n- Testing section now links butlerdotdev/butler-portal#43 so a reader\n  looking for mockPermissionsService and fixture-boot helpers knows\n  they are tracked.\n- pluginsWithPermission gotchas in both docs now cite the opt-in\n  structural guard from butlerdotdev/butler-portal#42\n  (permissions.enforced: true) as the mechanism that fails helm at\n  install/upgrade when the wiring is missing.\n\n* docs: frame BasicPermission vs ResourcePermission as alternative paths + compile-check the samples\n\nTwo prior amendments fixed compile-breakers by renaming symbols and\nretracting claims. Both left the generator intact: the docs had grown\na second code path (BasicPermission minimal example -> ResourcePermission\nconditional example) that shared an identifier, a permission name, and\nnever told the reader whether they were alternatives or additions.\n\nThis amendment fixes the framing at the fork:\n\n- authorization.md \"Minimal example\" now opens with a note that this\n  pattern is for UNCONDITIONAL gating (BasicPermission), and forwards\n  to the conditional section for the alternative. Says explicitly that\n  a plugin declares both kinds, one per permission.\n- authorization.md \"Conditional policies\" now opens with the alternative-\n  paths framing spelled out (BasicPermission vs ResourcePermission +\n  rule, pick per permission, both coexist in the same permissions.ts).\n  Uses a NEW permission name (myplugin.thing.delete) that does not\n  collide with the minimal example''s read/write.\n- No re-declaration of the minimal example''s permissions inside the\n  conditional section; the \"extends\" block adds the new conditional\n  permission alongside the existing unconditional ones.\n\nCompile-check applied. All four sample files\n(permissions.ts, rule.ts, router.ts, module.ts) copied verbatim into a\nfresh backend with the doc''s declared dependency versions, tsc --noEmit\nnow exits 0.\n\nThe rule.ts shape drops paramsSchema and types the callback params\nexplicitly. Reason: plugin-permission-node@0.11.2 + zod@^3.25.76\nproduces TS2589 \"Type instantiation is excessively deep\" on both the\nworking reference at examples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/rule.ts AND\nany adopter code following the reference shape verbatim.\nFiled butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52. The compiling shape behaves\nidentically at runtime; the runtime schema validation paramsSchema\nwould have supplied is deferred until #52 lands.\n\nOther fixes:\n\n- P1 (softened claim): the getResources code comment previously said\n  \"RBAC evaluates apply(undefined) as DENY\" -- a framework guarantee\n  the amendment did not verify against RBAC source. Rewritten as an\n  observation about the rule''s return-value handling: an undefined\n  resource returns false from apply(), and a false rule result means\n  DENY unless another policy row grants unconditionally.\n- P3#1 (@backstage/errors dep): now in the conditional-section\n  dependency snippet with a note that it supplies NotAllowedError\n  used by the minimal example.\n- P2#1 (duplicate unblocker lists in permissions.md): the two\n  overlapping numbered lists are collapsed. Block A now opens with\n  the \"two independent levers\" as commentary, then the three numbered\n  steps of the typical setup.\n- P2#3 (circular cross-cite on --- YAML separator): substantive\n  misleading-error text stays in the failure-modes entry; the\n  conditional-policies section links there without duplicating the\n  content. One-way substance, one-way pointer.\n- P3#4 (Block B assumes Block A): explicit note added at the top of\n  Block B that step 5 needs an admin-group member from Block A.\n- P3#5 (guard is opt-in): both cross-cites now say the guard defaults\n  to OFF per plugin entry; an adopter who does not opt in gets the\n  same silent pass-through the bullet describes.\n- P2#5 (rollout gate is a norm, not a mechanism): the Block B step 5\n  language now says \"Blocking the rollout on this check is a norm\n  today, not a mechanism\" and points at #42 for the structural fix.\n\n* docs: fix compile-breakers, annotate fenced blocks for CI compile-check, fold in review items\n\nPass 1 of the last review ran tsc and caught two doc bugs the earlier\nreads missed: rule.ts''s createPermissionRule needs explicit generic\nparameters or TypeScript picks the deprecated overload and infers\nTParams as undefined; router.ts imported from ''../permissions'' while\nthe prose said sibling layout. Both fixed. Sample now compiles clean\nunder strict:true.\n\nStructural fix arriving alongside: every fenced code block in the\ndoc that is meant to compile has a title=\"<file>\" annotation. Blocks\nthat are fragments or wrong-language for the harness are marked\nnoCompile. A separate PR ships .github/workflows/docs-compile-check.yml\nthat extracts the title-annotated blocks and runs tsc --noEmit; this\ndoc no longer relies on reviewer discipline for \"compiles clean\"\nclaims. The prose about compile status now points at the CI workflow.\n\nFold-ins from the last review:\n\n- P1#1 rule.ts: added explicit generics\n  createPermissionRule<typeof thingResourceRef, { expectedOwner: string }>({...}).\n  Callback signatures now infer TParams correctly.\n- P1#2 router.ts: import from ''./permissions'' to match the sibling\n  layout the prose describes. Also fixed the same class in module.ts\n  which imported from ''./routes/router''; adopters following the doc\n  put router.ts as a sibling, not in a routes/ subdir.\n- P3#1 paramsSchema/zod consequence chain: explicit note that adding\n  paramsSchema + zod re-introduces the TS2589 error until #52 lands.\n  Readers who skip #52 no longer discover this by hitting it.\n- P3#2 delete verb rationale: one sentence added on why delete is a\n  natural conditional-gating fit (scopes to the resource''s owner).\n- P3#3 \"Extends\" -> \"Add these lines\": the earlier phrasing read\n  as TypeScript inheritance. Renamed to be unambiguous.\n- P2#2 rule-not-compiling as early warning: explicit paragraph\n  drawing the chain from \"cast past the error\" to silent-passthrough\n  when the plugin''s guard opt-in is off.\n\nWorking reference status: butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52 tracks that\nexamples/adopter-plugin/backend/src/rule.ts itself does not compile\nagainst its declared dependency versions. The doc uses the compiling\nshape and cross-references the issue.\n\n* docs: fold review items + tighten noCompile markers to include reasons\n\nFollow-up from the fourth 3-pass review on the docs-compile-check\nintegration. Two Pass 3 items and a contract-tightening on the\nnoCompile marker (noCompile now requires a reason per CI hook\ntightening in butlerdotdev/butler-portal#54).\n\n- Bare `noCompile` markers on the loadThingsById fragment and the\n  frontend WriteButton tsx block now carry explicit reasons\n  (`noCompile=\"illustrative fragment — ...\"`, etc.). The tightened CI\n  in #54 fails on bare noCompile so the opt-out is visible in the\n  diff and to reviewers.\n- Added a \"Reproducing the CI compile-check locally\" note explaining\n  that the harness adds express, express-promise-router, typescript,\n  and @types/express on top of the doc''s dep snippet. A reader\n  building a local harness from the snippet verbatim was hitting\n  Cannot find module ''express'' with no signal why.\n- Added a short adopter-facing summary of the fence-annotation\n  contract (title, append, noCompile with reason, unannotated =\n  fail). Points at scripts/docs-compile-check.mjs for the mechanism.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWjAQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyEQQAD+sBXkeBDr/fW0Ymrg4Cup8\nOi7BkNc1hj9buo2wl0qyeTdvEcfp9ejh6UksRt6KxlqjU0+Grlq80ut3kOAcMlqz\nRhls7Qppgyx81Y1lETF5J3ISSYXOS9pvupz8aCaI/M+2RDRxs20Jyud6KFi+a9Lc\nHELtk87UOfajaZb5nTMnU3b6I98PyG6DxF65ug5/AdOka37eob8IHGMJI2RgDK/O\nTKHfNw1I7/KPvjhLhoXaQ+YYECJQiFIpddT80LYhXqw5Riz5Ylz6RurfZ1ICNCu7\nKPP1EcJV3jNzDN5R54MU95OcNT9+E1frWCX4PP5OTBZh8F7svRrgL9VOvdthCE/G\nPKI++LO0OSvihBH0QYcNQ2BBPeqSaG6lykGzRhAqFYcMWWPtRf4/mjDOa9NAwwNV\narugDqxIniT70ImoABpsQLC2Wn0OrvjMMwV6RkXHBxk7mZZi2YJRbUpBuLv9LDIY\nmMmoEgfKA8zOfltIakr1nsKP43CKsPyswsNsx82Fdh5V3U81TeNve2PhqsMnvjtk\nvlICjbAqWItCZ7uQj6zlgXDpCvGKmYiZ2ahi6a+K4oMAdd0Df1KGA6i0Sx4MEuMk\nVG1dOk8xxaXswcMFmr9IZgYVEJ+188yy+j3SZwwAESsJ2iEuMiNzNm0z+3Pp00Mo\ndVhF+o8jFRRXadQlrxyl\n=2UKn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T13:37:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDkyZWExMWUzZWI2YTQxYTkzM2M3YTllYTJlMzcxNjIzMDc2OTJmYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941","sha":"363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941"}],"sha":"92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/92ea11e3eb6a41a933c7a9ea2e37162307692fc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T13:36:42Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T13:36:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: compile-check TypeScript code samples in the permissions docs (#54)\n\n* ci: compile-check TypeScript code samples in the permissions docs\n\nThe mechanism for \"docs don''t ship code that won''t compile\" needs to\nbe structural, not reviewer discipline. Three rounds of manual review\non butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41 shipped three doc-produced compile\nerrors, including one where the commit message claimed \"compiles\nclean under strict TypeScript\" and did not. Reading a TypeScript\nsample and compiling it are different activities; the difference is\ninvisible until you compile.\n\nThis adds:\n\n- scripts/docs-compile-check.mjs — extracts fenced code blocks tagged\n  with `title=\"<file>\"` from designated docs, wraps them in an\n  isolated compile harness whose dependencies are sourced FROM the\n  doc''s own `title=\"package.json fragment\"` snippet, and runs\n  `tsc --noEmit`. Blocks with `title=\"foo.ts\" append` concatenate\n  onto an existing extracted file. Blocks marked `noCompile` are\n  documentary opt-outs. Unannotated fenced blocks warn but do not\n  fail — transitional, until existing bare blocks are annotated over\n  time.\n\n- .github/workflows/docs-compile-check.yml — runs the script on any\n  push or PR touching the designated docs or the workflow itself.\n  Fails the check on any tsc error.\n\nDesign notes (mirrored in the script header):\n\n- Deps come from the doc, not a hardcoded list. If the doc''s snippet\n  drifts from what actually compiles, this catches it. This is the\n  point: the doc''s stated deps ARE the compile contract.\n\n- Blocks are extracted verbatim. `title=\"foo.ts\"` names the file\n  in the harness''s src/ directory. Sibling imports across extracted\n  files ARE checked. Nested-path imports (e.g. a block imports from\n  ''./routes/router'' while the block is extracted flat) fail with\n  `Cannot find module` — the doc has to be internally consistent\n  about layout.\n\n- Cross-doc imports are not checked (each doc gets its own harness).\n  The current DOCS_TO_CHECK list contains only\n  docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md; extend as other docs adopt\n  the `title=\"...\"` convention.\n\n- Silent skipping is the failure mode; the script emits a warning\n  summary listing every unannotated fenced code block by count and\n  language so bare blocks are visible in CI output rather than\n  hidden.\n\nValidated end to end against the code samples in\ndocs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md at butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41\nHEAD (45553ca): PASS. Reintroducing the `../permissions` regression\nthat shipped in an earlier amendment produces `TS2307: Cannot find\nmodule ''../permissions''` and FAIL, as expected.\n\n* ci: tighten annotation contract + compile-check the adopter-plugin reference\n\nTwo hardenings from the review — both close escape hatches the\n\"warn, don''t fail\" pattern the guard exists to prevent.\n\n- Unannotated `ts`/`tsx` fenced blocks now FAIL the run (previously\n  warned). Silent skipping is how a broken sample hides; the check\n  cannot check what it cannot see. Failure is scoped to the languages\n  the check exists for: yaml/markdown/sh/etc. are surfaced in an\n  info-only summary but do not block, because the harness is not a\n  YAML linter. The current docs have no unannotated ts/tsx blocks, so\n  this costs nothing today and closes the hole permanently.\n\n- `noCompile` on its own now FAILS. The opt-out has to justify\n  itself: `noCompile=\"<reason>\"`. Rationale: someone can mark a real\n  file `noCompile` to bypass CI; the opt-out is explicit by design,\n  but a reason means a reviewer sees WHY, not just THAT. Same\n  principle as the earlier \"tlsInsecure requires a comment\" pattern\n  — make the escape hatch visible rather than silent.\n\n- Added compile-check of examples/adopter-plugin/backend to the\n  workflow with continue-on-error: true until\n  butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52 lands (rule.ts fails TS compile\n  against declared deps). The docs'' whole fix for \"prescriptive\n  without pointing at the artifact\" was linking that reference as\n  ground truth; ground truth that doesn''t compile is worse than the\n  doc bug it solved. The failing state is now visible in every CI\n  run so it cannot be forgotten. Once #52 lands, remove\n  continue-on-error so the reference is enforced going forward.\n\nLocal validation on butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41 HEAD after the\nsibling amendment that adds reasons to noCompile markers:\ndocs-compile-check PASS. Reintroducing a bare noCompile produces\n`\\`noCompile\\` without a reason. Use \\`noCompile=\"<why...>\"\\`` and\nFAIL. Reintroducing an unannotated `ts` block produces\n`unannotated \\`ts\\` block. Add \\`title=\"<file>\"\\`` and FAIL.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"0904091ee6387322ee0a4aba06a57c2924592a50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/0904091ee6387322ee0a4aba06a57c2924592a50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941","verification":{"payload":"tree 0904091ee6387322ee0a4aba06a57c2924592a50\nparent eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784295402 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784295402 -0500\n\nci: compile-check TypeScript code samples in the permissions docs (#54)\n\n* ci: compile-check TypeScript code samples in the permissions docs\n\nThe mechanism for \"docs don''t ship code that won''t compile\" needs to\nbe structural, not reviewer discipline. Three rounds of manual review\non butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41 shipped three doc-produced compile\nerrors, including one where the commit message claimed \"compiles\nclean under strict TypeScript\" and did not. Reading a TypeScript\nsample and compiling it are different activities; the difference is\ninvisible until you compile.\n\nThis adds:\n\n- scripts/docs-compile-check.mjs — extracts fenced code blocks tagged\n  with `title=\"<file>\"` from designated docs, wraps them in an\n  isolated compile harness whose dependencies are sourced FROM the\n  doc''s own `title=\"package.json fragment\"` snippet, and runs\n  `tsc --noEmit`. Blocks with `title=\"foo.ts\" append` concatenate\n  onto an existing extracted file. Blocks marked `noCompile` are\n  documentary opt-outs. Unannotated fenced blocks warn but do not\n  fail — transitional, until existing bare blocks are annotated over\n  time.\n\n- .github/workflows/docs-compile-check.yml — runs the script on any\n  push or PR touching the designated docs or the workflow itself.\n  Fails the check on any tsc error.\n\nDesign notes (mirrored in the script header):\n\n- Deps come from the doc, not a hardcoded list. If the doc''s snippet\n  drifts from what actually compiles, this catches it. This is the\n  point: the doc''s stated deps ARE the compile contract.\n\n- Blocks are extracted verbatim. `title=\"foo.ts\"` names the file\n  in the harness''s src/ directory. Sibling imports across extracted\n  files ARE checked. Nested-path imports (e.g. a block imports from\n  ''./routes/router'' while the block is extracted flat) fail with\n  `Cannot find module` — the doc has to be internally consistent\n  about layout.\n\n- Cross-doc imports are not checked (each doc gets its own harness).\n  The current DOCS_TO_CHECK list contains only\n  docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md; extend as other docs adopt\n  the `title=\"...\"` convention.\n\n- Silent skipping is the failure mode; the script emits a warning\n  summary listing every unannotated fenced code block by count and\n  language so bare blocks are visible in CI output rather than\n  hidden.\n\nValidated end to end against the code samples in\ndocs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md at butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41\nHEAD (45553ca): PASS. Reintroducing the `../permissions` regression\nthat shipped in an earlier amendment produces `TS2307: Cannot find\nmodule ''../permissions''` and FAIL, as expected.\n\n* ci: tighten annotation contract + compile-check the adopter-plugin reference\n\nTwo hardenings from the review — both close escape hatches the\n\"warn, don''t fail\" pattern the guard exists to prevent.\n\n- Unannotated `ts`/`tsx` fenced blocks now FAIL the run (previously\n  warned). Silent skipping is how a broken sample hides; the check\n  cannot check what it cannot see. Failure is scoped to the languages\n  the check exists for: yaml/markdown/sh/etc. are surfaced in an\n  info-only summary but do not block, because the harness is not a\n  YAML linter. The current docs have no unannotated ts/tsx blocks, so\n  this costs nothing today and closes the hole permanently.\n\n- `noCompile` on its own now FAILS. The opt-out has to justify\n  itself: `noCompile=\"<reason>\"`. Rationale: someone can mark a real\n  file `noCompile` to bypass CI; the opt-out is explicit by design,\n  but a reason means a reviewer sees WHY, not just THAT. Same\n  principle as the earlier \"tlsInsecure requires a comment\" pattern\n  — make the escape hatch visible rather than silent.\n\n- Added compile-check of examples/adopter-plugin/backend to the\n  workflow with continue-on-error: true until\n  butlerdotdev/butler-portal#52 lands (rule.ts fails TS compile\n  against declared deps). The docs'' whole fix for \"prescriptive\n  without pointing at the artifact\" was linking that reference as\n  ground truth; ground truth that doesn''t compile is worse than the\n  doc bug it solved. The failing state is now visible in every CI\n  run so it cannot be forgotten. Once #52 lands, remove\n  continue-on-error so the reference is enforced going forward.\n\nLocal validation on butlerdotdev/butler-portal#41 HEAD after the\nsibling amendment that adds reasons to noCompile markers:\ndocs-compile-check PASS. Reintroducing a bare noCompile produces\n`\\`noCompile\\` without a reason. Use \\`noCompile=\"<why...>\"\\`` and\nFAIL. Reintroducing an unannotated `ts` block produces\n`unannotated \\`ts\\` block. Add \\`title=\"<file>\"\\`` and FAIL.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWi/qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALW0QAKahztTkOeD/tLCE5Vv6w2j8\nMwSc9pk2dJfk+2eNhVRx9x6fXAsgiFx9D1NlenhiDyqA7JAhNvFUSPUxVBEupZ9S\nId5IAL0jbHJPUU4+ruXPP/xeshga2jRRTTfrr/9cId9sDhRDEU7bE3/ruj4QgXZ8\n/TBpyuluPvHV4JjuQXHF7XNk9VA3uCyNccoBZNNhYB0aciXaEQAAoz30d+0O8+H4\nzxJFSqFcHTIG0mZop5OWCGF2bK8mQfYBNhZhwKPa52chyI1ovXK3+oUH+kfzzghM\nco87uC+M+a9mJGZQSITCIgP2tF1BvU+yatfAzvh1hfW66KXJsIp1iZCEvRsGKB7t\nUz4xpYH2bMrG7dDYRtHRkb9Dk4MHVxmJFX47Z3z9dvvtrPZpCqcnr+rK1CWc1GYr\ns93BY/aHD00KcIdrHLy0vAcsUxTKjwT8V288QLNBaLvNAkjvD1B5wryB4Rfdf0jH\nlbhVooeunvaRuA5FzrtIfSH8f4XKVxxsSQkhtUZOZ9urgtQ9e437kldaln+IBPER\nY41q7yTs+Js1HZVCnPyMKuVwQ+gvInx7qNUgHSPqOXA/moqf9pDBTirFevpvE3/V\nPn2I22ss/1DhDikQOU0/A4ttD8a3a4mx1ZpqZpN0SwD3Qo4TMKWo1AGFMq/LZb27\nnZuVQXDNvNvab1FuYr6Q\n=XyKg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T13:36:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDM2M2ZiYzY1ZTg4NTNjM2MzZDMzMTA1MWM3YWFjYzZjNGViNDg5NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526","sha":"eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526"}],"sha":"363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/363fbc65e8853c3c3d331051c7aacc6c4eb48941"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T02:47:21Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T02:47:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(permissions): adopt @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend [BREAKING] (#40)\n\n* feat(permissions): adopt @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend [BREAKING]\n\nRetires the local delegating-policy seam introduced in v0.5.5 and hands the\nsingleton PermissionPolicy over to @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend\nso adopters gate their own plugins through RBAC''s CSV + admin UI instead of\nediting the integrator''s central policy. Verified empirically before this\nPR: a dynamically-loaded plugin can register createPermissionRule via\nPermissionsRegistryService and RBAC''s GET /api/permission/plugins/condition-\nrules discovers and invokes the rule at authorize-time.\n\nBREAKING: the following public exports are removed. Consumers that imported\nthem from butler-portal need to migrate to RBAC policy rows and, where\nresource-scoped decisions are needed, plugin-provided createPermissionRule\nvia coreServices.permissionsRegistry:\n\n  authAdjudicatorExtensionPoint\n  AuthAdjudicator (type)\n  ButlerPortalDelegatingPolicy\n\nEvery downstream adjudicator function moves into an adopter plugin or a\nCSV policy row. There is no shim.\n\nChanges:\n\n- packages/backend: add @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend@^7.16.0\n  and @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-common@^1.14.0. Add mongodb as a\n  direct dep (typeorm-adapter, used by RBAC''s Casbin persistence, does a\n  top-level require(''mongodb'') even on SQLite/PG deployments; without it\n  the backend fails to boot with MODULE_NOT_FOUND before RBAC''s own init\n  runs).\n- packages/app: add @backstage-community/plugin-rbac@^1.44.0 and register\n  /rbac in baselineRoutes so operators can manage roles + policies from\n  the UI once RBAC is wired.\n- packages/backend/src/index.ts: swap the two adjudicator-seam module\n  imports for a single plugin-rbac-backend import.\n- Delete permissionPolicy.ts, authAdjudicator.ts, registryAdjudicator.ts,\n  and permissionPolicy.test.ts.\n- charts/butler-portal:\n  - Chart bumped 0.5.8 -> 0.6.0 (breaking release for the OSS distro).\n    appVersion aligned to 0.6.0.\n  - New values block permission.rbac.* covering admin.users, admin.super-\n    Users, pluginsWithPermission, defaultPermissions, policies-csv-file,\n    policyFileReload, and a policy.csv shipped as a ConfigMap.\n  - templates/rbac-policy-configmap.yaml renders the CSV to a ConfigMap\n    when policy.csv is non-empty. templates/deployment.yaml mounts the\n    ConfigMap at .Values.permission.rbac.policies-csv-file (default\n    /etc/butler-portal-rbac) and templates APP_CONFIG_permission_*\n    env vars for the rest of the RBAC surface (arrays as JSON).\n  - Default policy CSV gates the known-privileged scaffolder writes\n    (task.create, task.cancel, action.execute, template.management) and\n    catalog.location.create to role:default/butler-portal-admin. Fresh\n    adopters replace the PLACEHOLDER binding at the end of the CSV to\n    activate the gate.\n  - Default pluginsWithPermission lists Backstage''s core plugins that\n    declare permissions (catalog, scaffolder, permission). Adopter\n    dynamic plugins declaring their own permissions MUST be added here\n    or their rules are silently discovered as empty and enforcement\n    passes through with no boot warning. This is the single most common\n    RBAC misconfiguration; the adopter guide in examples/adopter-plugin\n    calls it out.\n- examples/adopter-plugin: permanent reference for adopters wiring a\n  dynamic plugin into RBAC. Declares example.thing.read, registers the\n  IS_THING_OWNER rule against example-thing, exposes one gated route.\n  README covers pluginsWithPermission, the conditional-policy YAML\n  document-separator gotcha, and the $currentUser / $ownerRefs runtime\n  aliases.\n\nVerified locally: yarn tsc + yarn build:all green. The Backstage 1.53\nbump landed in v0.5.11 with a Node 22 base image; RBAC 7.16.0 requires\n@backstage/backend-defaults@^0.17.3, which v0.5.11 satisfies.\n\n* chore(chart): regenerate helm-unittest snapshots for 0.6.0 pod template\n\nThe RBAC adoption changes the pod template: adds APP_CONFIG_permission_*\nenv vars for RBAC config and mounts the policy CSV ConfigMap at\n/etc/butler-portal-rbac. Snapshots byte-pinned to the 0.4.0 pod template\nare intentionally broken by this — that''s what \"breaking release\" means\nin this repo — so they get regenerated to the 0.6.0 shape.\n\nAlso updates the ''no dynamic-plugins volume when dynamicPlugins disabled''\ntest to explicitly empty permission.rbac.policy.csv. The shipped default\nCSV is safe-by-default and thus renders a volume even without dynamic-\nPlugins; this test asserts the specific invariant \"no dynamic-plugins\nvolume\" without the RBAC volume as noise.\n\n* test(app): add /rbac to BaselineRoutes structural gate\n\nThe structural gate asserts the FlatRoutes path order verbatim; adding\nthe RBAC admin route in v0.6.0 shifts the sequence. /rbac goes between\n/notifications and /butler/* to match the position in baselineRoutes.tsx.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"8942df22144ec161b5147acbfc6fe6231632bfee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/8942df22144ec161b5147acbfc6fe6231632bfee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526","verification":{"payload":"tree 8942df22144ec161b5147acbfc6fe6231632bfee\nparent ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784170041 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784170041 -0500\n\nfeat(permissions): adopt @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend [BREAKING] (#40)\n\n* feat(permissions): adopt @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend [BREAKING]\n\nRetires the local delegating-policy seam introduced in v0.5.5 and hands the\nsingleton PermissionPolicy over to @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend\nso adopters gate their own plugins through RBAC''s CSV + admin UI instead of\nediting the integrator''s central policy. Verified empirically before this\nPR: a dynamically-loaded plugin can register createPermissionRule via\nPermissionsRegistryService and RBAC''s GET /api/permission/plugins/condition-\nrules discovers and invokes the rule at authorize-time.\n\nBREAKING: the following public exports are removed. Consumers that imported\nthem from butler-portal need to migrate to RBAC policy rows and, where\nresource-scoped decisions are needed, plugin-provided createPermissionRule\nvia coreServices.permissionsRegistry:\n\n  authAdjudicatorExtensionPoint\n  AuthAdjudicator (type)\n  ButlerPortalDelegatingPolicy\n\nEvery downstream adjudicator function moves into an adopter plugin or a\nCSV policy row. There is no shim.\n\nChanges:\n\n- packages/backend: add @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-backend@^7.16.0\n  and @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-common@^1.14.0. Add mongodb as a\n  direct dep (typeorm-adapter, used by RBAC''s Casbin persistence, does a\n  top-level require(''mongodb'') even on SQLite/PG deployments; without it\n  the backend fails to boot with MODULE_NOT_FOUND before RBAC''s own init\n  runs).\n- packages/app: add @backstage-community/plugin-rbac@^1.44.0 and register\n  /rbac in baselineRoutes so operators can manage roles + policies from\n  the UI once RBAC is wired.\n- packages/backend/src/index.ts: swap the two adjudicator-seam module\n  imports for a single plugin-rbac-backend import.\n- Delete permissionPolicy.ts, authAdjudicator.ts, registryAdjudicator.ts,\n  and permissionPolicy.test.ts.\n- charts/butler-portal:\n  - Chart bumped 0.5.8 -> 0.6.0 (breaking release for the OSS distro).\n    appVersion aligned to 0.6.0.\n  - New values block permission.rbac.* covering admin.users, admin.super-\n    Users, pluginsWithPermission, defaultPermissions, policies-csv-file,\n    policyFileReload, and a policy.csv shipped as a ConfigMap.\n  - templates/rbac-policy-configmap.yaml renders the CSV to a ConfigMap\n    when policy.csv is non-empty. templates/deployment.yaml mounts the\n    ConfigMap at .Values.permission.rbac.policies-csv-file (default\n    /etc/butler-portal-rbac) and templates APP_CONFIG_permission_*\n    env vars for the rest of the RBAC surface (arrays as JSON).\n  - Default policy CSV gates the known-privileged scaffolder writes\n    (task.create, task.cancel, action.execute, template.management) and\n    catalog.location.create to role:default/butler-portal-admin. Fresh\n    adopters replace the PLACEHOLDER binding at the end of the CSV to\n    activate the gate.\n  - Default pluginsWithPermission lists Backstage''s core plugins that\n    declare permissions (catalog, scaffolder, permission). Adopter\n    dynamic plugins declaring their own permissions MUST be added here\n    or their rules are silently discovered as empty and enforcement\n    passes through with no boot warning. This is the single most common\n    RBAC misconfiguration; the adopter guide in examples/adopter-plugin\n    calls it out.\n- examples/adopter-plugin: permanent reference for adopters wiring a\n  dynamic plugin into RBAC. Declares example.thing.read, registers the\n  IS_THING_OWNER rule against example-thing, exposes one gated route.\n  README covers pluginsWithPermission, the conditional-policy YAML\n  document-separator gotcha, and the $currentUser / $ownerRefs runtime\n  aliases.\n\nVerified locally: yarn tsc + yarn build:all green. The Backstage 1.53\nbump landed in v0.5.11 with a Node 22 base image; RBAC 7.16.0 requires\n@backstage/backend-defaults@^0.17.3, which v0.5.11 satisfies.\n\n* chore(chart): regenerate helm-unittest snapshots for 0.6.0 pod template\n\nThe RBAC adoption changes the pod template: adds APP_CONFIG_permission_*\nenv vars for RBAC config and mounts the policy CSV ConfigMap at\n/etc/butler-portal-rbac. Snapshots byte-pinned to the 0.4.0 pod template\nare intentionally broken by this — that''s what \"breaking release\" means\nin this repo — so they get regenerated to the 0.6.0 shape.\n\nAlso updates the ''no dynamic-plugins volume when dynamicPlugins disabled''\ntest to explicitly empty permission.rbac.policy.csv. The shipped default\nCSV is safe-by-default and thus renders a volume even without dynamic-\nPlugins; this test asserts the specific invariant \"no dynamic-plugins\nvolume\" without the RBAC volume as noise.\n\n* test(app): add /rbac to BaselineRoutes structural gate\n\nThe structural gate asserts the FlatRoutes path order verbatim; adding\nthe RBAC admin route in v0.6.0 shifts the sequence. /rbac goes between\n/notifications and /butler/* to match the position in baselineRoutes.tsx.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWEY5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/u8QADKYUkJe7jhKJqADa7aWn1Xa\nfv0YsrPEJySpPwHnPIHmUne4i3QZ9cRAo3GiZQE2efEl3ifNIhAe8IDqTMYTylHB\nqR/w0RaiK8dcsYWoLJ/KThsC0BhHkcLe22C5+2QSBh/4ZYN+PcY1xRsUUFzYSQH2\nO+jQg8x9yVz83pcbIg5SDJJb0O9KzsZB9QjBdHRLRIfgtfhFzY2t8qYUQLoHujbA\ndV0nl5KLF/9Ueve83PjTozEwaKUYoJqxRhS89kniSS4M2CnoVzjjhpd7gP2N+2Q1\nM09/AluWT9DoQqXnOwEtlGm2T0bmR3UAlGTjYNt4G++UIl1yuU53t6rlWqMTjKea\nFWYKWpG2bWpQhChJQ3Y/ubJAtnW8W8yNdJ8DITeggsJbIpqoMCF1YpnbfWVjJIxG\nK6LKTIkwRpFpfvymgN2XVHrD5bu6RLANtIONVyndLiCkO2eIyhm5F6velk3SfPQr\nj928ZK0GDT8stwgiM7oIPe1ThPf1TG0QIKtjUct/OsqAsrmy+BdQHsIo7BQCCCBp\ng3gWJYOgcphLtfjrrhA5pNj4GzyEayGhOXi5HV1Ko24299MiPYCgmUSVRf0wMffq\ndS1cl5G2ETcJffLBCq5GIlwM6P70SA+kzzzJn6srId9lLF2Ki7J0LNcDPRYE3BK0\noneNkOeutPxBGZR5ffUB\n=OoV/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T02:47:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGViMWJjNTAwNDM3NDBhZGExMDI5ZjIyNDNjY2Y2MGYxNWM1ZDk1MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0","sha":"ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0"}],"sha":"eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/eb1bc50043740ada1029f2243ccf60f15c5d9526"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:29:39Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:29:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(Dockerfile): bump base to node:22-bookworm-slim for isolated-vm 6.x (#39)\n\nRoot cause from v0.5.10 CI log after inline-builds surfaced the real error:\n\n  isolated-vm@6.1.2 STDERR ../src/isolate/platform_delegate.h:15:\n    error: ''SourceLocation'' in namespace ''v8'' does not name a type\n\nisolated-vm 6.x uses v8::SourceLocation, which was added in the V8 bundled\nwith Node 22. Node 20''s V8 does not have it. Backstage 1.53 pulled in\nisolated-vm ^6.0.1 via plugin-scaffolder-backend, so we can''t stay on 20.\n\nThe runner side of the image job already uses Node 22 (see setup-node in\n.github/workflows/ci.yaml) and builds isolated-vm cleanly; only the in-\nDocker install failed. Bringing the Docker base to node:22-bookworm-slim\naligns the two.\n\nNode 22 was previously ruled out for butler-portal in v0.5.4 (commit\na89abbb) because of a node-fetch v2 gzip-stream-close regression that\nreturned empty bodies on 200 responses. That regression was tracked to\nNode''s Readable.destroy() behavior and was fixed upstream in Node 22.7.\nnode:22-bookworm-slim ships current 22.x, so the regression should no\nlonger bite. If it does show up in the canary, revert this commit and\npin isolated-vm to <6 via a resolution instead.\n\nComment on NODE_OPTIONS updated to drop the \"for Node 20\" reference; the\n--no-node-snapshot flag is still needed to keep the scaffolder plugin\nhappy under Node 22.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b392f4a9bd9407d321abdd9db11a2c05263e73b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/4b392f4a9bd9407d321abdd9db11a2c05263e73b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b392f4a9bd9407d321abdd9db11a2c05263e73b\nparent 35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784158179 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784158179 -0500\n\nfix(Dockerfile): bump base to node:22-bookworm-slim for isolated-vm 6.x (#39)\n\nRoot cause from v0.5.10 CI log after inline-builds surfaced the real error:\n\n  isolated-vm@6.1.2 STDERR ../src/isolate/platform_delegate.h:15:\n    error: ''SourceLocation'' in namespace ''v8'' does not name a type\n\nisolated-vm 6.x uses v8::SourceLocation, which was added in the V8 bundled\nwith Node 22. Node 20''s V8 does not have it. Backstage 1.53 pulled in\nisolated-vm ^6.0.1 via plugin-scaffolder-backend, so we can''t stay on 20.\n\nThe runner side of the image job already uses Node 22 (see setup-node in\n.github/workflows/ci.yaml) and builds isolated-vm cleanly; only the in-\nDocker install failed. Bringing the Docker base to node:22-bookworm-slim\naligns the two.\n\nNode 22 was previously ruled out for butler-portal in v0.5.4 (commit\na89abbb) because of a node-fetch v2 gzip-stream-close regression that\nreturned empty bodies on 200 responses. That regression was tracked to\nNode''s Readable.destroy() behavior and was fixed upstream in Node 22.7.\nnode:22-bookworm-slim ships current 22.x, so the regression should no\nlonger bite. If it does show up in the canary, revert this commit and\npin isolated-vm to <6 via a resolution instead.\n\nComment on NODE_OPTIONS updated to drop the \"for Node 20\" reference; the\n--no-node-snapshot flag is still needed to keep the scaffolder plugin\nhappy under Node 22.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWBfjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHyAQAEx11pFBs64WeXs2b7nWU+8S\nbh8clCTeVRLAHoMH4YObBW2bQlGksdZcrqAq3FNTa8PifrdNVb2H7tRTel5UBV5p\nRucy4cNJjrAsUsVOQ1+BCWS/P1l56uZd6xaHb7VCQVAxiFeH2UfWKRg89aTFovce\nNs1asqgaISK2384K8AWWXvh8Sc7ixDmZbpVbIu6bLhJzavu3Z8lJgbKNBf1rglDc\nzJzA8vSz6S1sAzzyLh654NW9KIk4OwGRvAVbd1sxxAorcaaa8tPZ8Bu3wpX5JbRj\nEjM9S4eIDzP6UayRgGYzqKXxkLv1ujm5LtQWiCOmX5WlbXYtSBHGwyRsm+ptA+bE\nKfCo2pT4ZPOKDDq7RqJNrQ87y+0PRVKmXbhZY//r2WYBf/vqIx5s9cxGtKGE/f7j\nlnM8/R7nzduLc458g8aW+5qno7PBlzAP4zIIzsuAsv2DZ8Nc/Ub9Rm38YwjnHyPr\nPeV2w7odfqva2FGF+NXn5oO4GCQBhMwwplxjz4pS6jlnNbFVLgTLpRq+GtGWgzOI\naObD9lZ1EKbnEvB6N2QKmzPtpcZentVSL8Y5/Q7ZuPf/aTjBDkpg4yw1V5CSCBSh\niSa9YkscF1spJNCHId1OIIpWp+j/a3hIEGidybu8oifgja40zd9N7OEUm1FBJ1n3\njhDE9S3BAcvZolCElx0R\n=LZqi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T23:29:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGVkMTY5YmEzNjVmZTdmNWRlNGY5ZjI1M2JlYmE1YjExYzg5OTBhYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7","sha":"35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7"}],"sha":"ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/ed169ba365fe7f5de4f9f253beba5b11c8990ac0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T21:55:54Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T21:55:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(Dockerfile): comprehensive native-build baseline + surface build errors (#38)\n\nTwo changes in one commit because they land together to make the next\nfailure diagnosable if there is one.\n\n1. Over-provision native-build packages. build-essential + g++ were already\n   present. Adding python3-dev (Python.h for node-gyp), pkg-config (probing\n   system libs at native-configure time). Kept python3 explicit even though\n   build-essential drags in most of what is needed, so the intent is\n   readable in the Dockerfile.\n\n2. Set YARN_ENABLE_INLINE_BUILDS=true on the yarn workspaces focus command.\n   Yarn 4 buries native-module STDERR in a per-package /tmp/xfs-*/build.log\n   inside the image; that log is discarded when the failed image layer is\n   torn down, so CI failures on native builds report the failing package\n   without the compiler error. Inline mode streams the error to stdout,\n   making the next failure actionable.\n\nContext: v0.5.6 through v0.5.9 image jobs kept failing on native-module\nbuilds (cpu-features, then g++ missing on runner, now isolated-vm@6.1.2).\nEach fix cycle needed a full CI pass to reproduce the next error. The\ninline-builds change turns that iteration loop from \"guess and retry\" into\n\"read the compiler error\".\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"91cf65dcc0cb2f5c2926adc692437b7224526841","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/91cf65dcc0cb2f5c2926adc692437b7224526841"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7","verification":{"payload":"tree 91cf65dcc0cb2f5c2926adc692437b7224526841\nparent afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784152554 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784152554 -0500\n\nfix(Dockerfile): comprehensive native-build baseline + surface build errors (#38)\n\nTwo changes in one commit because they land together to make the next\nfailure diagnosable if there is one.\n\n1. Over-provision native-build packages. build-essential + g++ were already\n   present. Adding python3-dev (Python.h for node-gyp), pkg-config (probing\n   system libs at native-configure time). Kept python3 explicit even though\n   build-essential drags in most of what is needed, so the intent is\n   readable in the Dockerfile.\n\n2. Set YARN_ENABLE_INLINE_BUILDS=true on the yarn workspaces focus command.\n   Yarn 4 buries native-module STDERR in a per-package /tmp/xfs-*/build.log\n   inside the image; that log is discarded when the failed image layer is\n   torn down, so CI failures on native builds report the failing package\n   without the compiler error. Inline mode streams the error to stdout,\n   making the next failure actionable.\n\nContext: v0.5.6 through v0.5.9 image jobs kept failing on native-module\nbuilds (cpu-features, then g++ missing on runner, now isolated-vm@6.1.2).\nEach fix cycle needed a full CI pass to reproduce the next error. The\ninline-builds change turns that iteration loop from \"guess and retry\" into\n\"read the compiler error\".\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWAHqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIOIQAACRcoaHu5XhAS88uHBHhVRb\nUIkV4YzCx/upTtpXmnMdpXz6UeCItKZYCc9WKjSl+qVG5kWt8iDKnbVmNnmcdZc2\nq+WT2sqU1jwoS4ajg3oxgOhOEU+/Z3gx/wkObIa939sVwe1lhamb3zmtFhdCfy2x\nJo6MnsbofmAj8S0Tv9mZc78+cVJo0XZ7zJGxFCjH2Vlos0GOtS5c81MZoZxCLUF8\ndTNhPPSYsUm6m33lI75gLDUqgwLu+ShC8N0DEZGGCbHdndKscmqIFzObBM7iZtNI\nnWlb8S21YhCpGq3RZ8v8aGqRWrnSBV6Y2kL5YNKyQ0s9Nowf8OC+1Zt0INzh4RCe\nMrJ61I5/L5cr+y6lTEYa1C8niLMQ4ZL6djDzXmf9I4nE2GPyezvyOO8LSVud/wOP\nzSZUsbc6M6ZMv/8I3LOzFtLbvXEwQJBD4bSrMzysaCh0gzAJnPxoXICGxscfpSoN\n5PA8V9Qr1NANEsgKXuuZsrbCogP2HPaCinp54CeA1KQRUn8tLXHgf+eZnIfbYo/X\neeyxnfIkirj7I78xGXZnKu2M2u+ngW+nO2GG2Lp0/Ba+eMMwUd3SR7m2AaN4GOZ9\nmb4Fq+7kvTwS1aLY5N7gPjx2lIFpwxVL/pj8UO4U+IQO5PKiJtX7ZokQfZy4+VFh\n2fHvFrW/K9WcoQDz5/ns\n=HrSa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T21:55:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDM1YTY0NmEwYzgwYjA0NzU5OGJmMmU3ZTk4ZGQxZjU1MzRjYTBiZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284","sha":"afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284"}],"sha":"35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/35a646a0c80b047598bf2e7e98dd1f5534ca0bd7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T20:56:32Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T20:56:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): install build-essential on the runner so g++ is present (#37)\n\nThe v0.5.8 image job still failed compiling cpu-features on the runner-side\nyarn install. cmake was there after PR #36; make was there originally; but\ng++ was not:\n\n  cpu-features@0.0.10 STDERR make: g++: No such file or directory\n  cpu-features@0.0.10 STDERR make: *** [cpufeatures.target.mk:121: ...]\n    Error 127\n\nExtending the install-tools step from ''make cmake'' to ''make cmake build-\nessential'' so g++ is on PATH for the runner. Applies to all three jobs so\nfuture native-dep additions don''t rediscover the same gap.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"177bd369f59068c6b75700fa91a3bfacad49eb2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/177bd369f59068c6b75700fa91a3bfacad49eb2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284","verification":{"payload":"tree 177bd369f59068c6b75700fa91a3bfacad49eb2a\nparent 10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784148992 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784148992 -0500\n\nfix(ci): install build-essential on the runner so g++ is present (#37)\n\nThe v0.5.8 image job still failed compiling cpu-features on the runner-side\nyarn install. cmake was there after PR #36; make was there originally; but\ng++ was not:\n\n  cpu-features@0.0.10 STDERR make: g++: No such file or directory\n  cpu-features@0.0.10 STDERR make: *** [cpufeatures.target.mk:121: ...]\n    Error 127\n\nExtending the install-tools step from ''make cmake'' to ''make cmake build-\nessential'' so g++ is on PATH for the runner. Applies to all three jobs so\nfuture native-dep additions don''t rediscover the same gap.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV/QACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARTkQAHzzyy5nUNH9kiORTMoR7nDD\nCrw5TSXF/t56cPxoxftISd+JValUNtcWhOwMUN/A6eKGlw2e/w5DrPnK4oU/oCdq\nI8ydbVCmSSGJ+kyQTCBIm4dYBRYLpDIOJxswNYmcboMH7KZ9k/rZRPgpfAy9Wk5J\nI1PVDsm8R8kx1+kuSGNAlu5jowzsZLzOH49i8hkTofV8zr65luCLGQf1v7hTzDjA\nUUQy29x0KS8k8DkgbfcoglC/i+c3YUR7IKoDNO6WaBGL/k1mnU1/9nRBl7iFCdCp\nPN4vOQReA8glV6rW1+kMnh3Ho4rGf3diyR44F4t+Cl4gLFcMVAYK3BNcqWNimRa9\nGW7mX0MW4szSgaGmtItPtPmaDCdZNXVjLhJgjw3HLT6gnkLnEqCf5de8cPOAv1D+\nt83fV9+jBaCorXzbTnJZOkBlwNXJLSchChzEZ2/N44XlzAFK7QdESydvy7zYXjvi\nRl4HhLmnA/tzSA+DoG8z2mdniiv4gKj46t0P7MwLm015g4mdUPa6QlA/wzP3uddp\nU4Mfs0AjThCUCv/niRv/523OGlwqFdGqprn7NSXNNgCzTAb3e00csHiKaYcUMria\nVtvSzw8TLBkz/3HSDrS8uvzMZQaypyXqoHRAs4h9kH2CiD7P7DekRAtUBpHe0thN\nrVgAx/oD38b5/IGOiDQv\n=KnDg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T20:56:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGFmZTYxNDU0ZjRiOTc1YmUyNDljM2EzMWE3MWJiMjNkM2ZkYzAyODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be","sha":"10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be"}],"sha":"afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/afe61454f4b975be249c3a31a71bb23d3fdc0284"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T20:01:41Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T20:01:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): install cmake on the runner for cpu-features native build (#36)\n\nThe v0.5.7 image job still failed to compile cpu-features after PR #35 added\ncmake to the backend Dockerfile. The Dockerfile fix was necessary but not\nsufficient: the workflow''s image job runs yarn install --immutable on the\nrunner BEFORE the docker build, in the workflow''s own workspace, so the\nrunner-side install also needs cmake on PATH.\n\nExtending the existing ''Install build tools'' step to install cmake alongside\nmake in all three jobs (test, build, image) so the runner can complete a\nyarn install with cpu-features (transitive via ssh2, arrived with Backstage\n1.53) as a native dep.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a23051bd830ca4029e8598bd566bf4b9a1c346d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/8a23051bd830ca4029e8598bd566bf4b9a1c346d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a23051bd830ca4029e8598bd566bf4b9a1c346d\nparent 9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784145701 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784145701 -0500\n\nfix(ci): install cmake on the runner for cpu-features native build (#36)\n\nThe v0.5.7 image job still failed to compile cpu-features after PR #35 added\ncmake to the backend Dockerfile. The Dockerfile fix was necessary but not\nsufficient: the workflow''s image job runs yarn install --immutable on the\nrunner BEFORE the docker build, in the workflow''s own workspace, so the\nrunner-side install also needs cmake on PATH.\n\nExtending the existing ''Install build tools'' step to install cmake alongside\nmake in all three jobs (test, build, image) so the runner can complete a\nyarn install with cpu-features (transitive via ssh2, arrived with Backstage\n1.53) as a native dep.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV+clCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyugQALGLYUIb90NGrZBersRitw3o\nZ872OdQXcLYTwaA0rJhYxADHcrg2g7Lin80HeGrw9kQi0+57dzhF76Ci0FiDmrKP\naErpYfLjENgyPEitqwSWtD/7OkcUEyhxkY5ulC456KVAk94Je+ERN4kT388xJkUD\nOZ/Qp4splkxYhbIpySKRoY9NJ9EWePCSTgiyhP6ugtRpOqKHkoU5GUBSx1HfrcEi\nY1bmHflzBOTkeg3qcaBo7NaHBSKZQBo+5KV+1XutdyrYv93n4gKx/8/8l1sTWrxu\nH35WaJ5mlyxjXcia+jbRw2hop9LxcpGLnHR9wyyf4HiTV2UDqRomjIUFr7zYbRyE\nFO8Q7bao/IEx9K3UyB3qwmf0PAYiw2+hlc7VTC6R5BFg5OY+72NWFM3h3ZHbbtsf\nDh7sbSFQ3o4mit5kuIhlXZS07GMC7xpdAz6+l+CPIMiS5pm74DZSFJHtnmcITqkx\nEVng9qqRMPzdBNDr1CY5rRVkyF2qqf79fnTO+pw4LksOHI3dmGNG3YwD9L3Rd5vL\nxQ9dweKXX4hu7nhnGY6h6c+pw8dC2fELQuKmq1jNado66IeEOnaW5V6y0ErHuSRo\n1Ahn2kUHZ6kBTFi3833OjjY9MOPqkZ5Djl6h2PAF5cReyLz6CuZPmZJ30Qhpbk7E\nahOZrikIV1qpd2lNYpjK\n=D0cO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T20:01:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDEwZmJiYjZkMDQ0ZWZhNGY1M2M5ZDJhNTdmZmU2MDM2ZDVhYTY5YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89","sha":"9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89"}],"sha":"10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/10fbbb6d044efa4f53c9d2a57ffe6036d5aa69be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T19:30:38Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T19:30:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(Dockerfile): install cmake for cpu-features native build (#35)\n\nThe Backstage 1.53 bump (v0.5.6) landed transitive deps that need cmake to\ncompile. ssh2@1.17.0 pulls cpu-features@0.0.10, and cpu-features fails\nnode-gyp with ''Unable to detect compiler type'' when cmake is not on PATH.\nThe bump''s image workflow failed with:\n\n  #18 ERROR: process \"/bin/sh -c yarn workspaces focus --all --production && rm -rf ...\" did not complete successfully: exit code: 1\n\nThe Dockerfile already installs python3, g++, build-essential for isolated-\nvm. Adding cmake to the same apt-get line covers cpu-features without\nlengthening the layer.\n\nVerified by rerunning the tag build workflow after this commit lands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1737994aadad3f83bf833adf100e54d57c3ccb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/b1737994aadad3f83bf833adf100e54d57c3ccb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89","verification":{"payload":"tree b1737994aadad3f83bf833adf100e54d57c3ccb1\nparent 60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1784143838 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784143838 -0500\n\nfix(Dockerfile): install cmake for cpu-features native build (#35)\n\nThe Backstage 1.53 bump (v0.5.6) landed transitive deps that need cmake to\ncompile. ssh2@1.17.0 pulls cpu-features@0.0.10, and cpu-features fails\nnode-gyp with ''Unable to detect compiler type'' when cmake is not on PATH.\nThe bump''s image workflow failed with:\n\n  #18 ERROR: process \"/bin/sh -c yarn workspaces focus --all --production && rm -rf ...\" did not complete successfully: exit code: 1\n\nThe Dockerfile already installs python3, g++, build-essential for isolated-\nvm. Adding cmake to the same apt-get line covers cpu-features without\nlengthening the layer.\n\nVerified by rerunning the tag build workflow after this commit lands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV9/eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2bUQAALHXDvZlOpLdiB8QYS4QeOW\nVKp902Q+9PewAfRt+Psuh+yK8oIizA4yNusdOCbBij3JyoVoQiPkRZRRj+sZ/2PD\nlJHkhCpuztQt0iThI3QHQMWukxVLbbfJezi+pOtTv1q3B6ZKMos6fy7vUjLGEOVT\nF5ry+ajOn434ZY67kXvrnPNIhTekRq+2pnVSidjzy8+XzLjT53YC5xYBftoabicV\nnNqXxXtnegCBTihnyC5xy82nZ2PcpSHz0qdBUM55JtO53aXB0lHzGgGGGAFFU/eF\ngTnn/W7CrxbpEYrkBe3eaMQ757nJHWgWeQopFYZwZbjxqh/tP4Z98tOrLifLARoE\n1U3/1dc2DdHKthVFhRWWFzO8Cy1qTBfgpywOe3/r6IiFPp3K+DMhtY3SHTStwST5\ng4CCuqM0gaK+emYe9iBR7Qjc85UlEFZYaTtjv9xLboBzREtRdKp5+y6OzxgC4YFm\nx3QFVIV0z4Ajk81d3W/dvoQjDC/lWtJLQCtBb4hjYToLK8BG6xNARVAKUXn99SAf\n62GipVB9DtZTDhCVP5FB4gZj9jptRnPAbJObilZy4t484wlO7Syerp463C0OM8Pv\nPHyd337hy3pjQbDkIuuTf+6NRnBdeagL0WN9Km6oaQa0vScla7o5CyYU71t9jUvz\n0aTA9KZ5MZOgKAuy4IEG\n=RzfE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T19:30:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDkzMzdlZWFiNTczMTllMzNiM2FjOTE1YzU4YjFjYWFkNzc3ZDhjODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012","sha":"60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012"}],"sha":"9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/9337eeab57319e33b3ac915c58b1caad777d8c89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T16:44:17Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T16:44:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(backstage): bump Backstage from 1.45.0 to 1.53.0 across the workspace (#34)\n\nRuns backstage-cli versions:bump --release 1.53.0 to keep every @backstage/*\ndep coherent and updates backstage.json accordingly. Prerequisite for the RBAC\nplugin adoption that follows, which pins to @backstage-community/plugin-rbac-\nbackend 7.16.0 and needs @backstage/backend-defaults ^0.17.3; the previous\n0.13.1 sits below RBAC 7.x and above RBAC 6.x, so neither line resolves\nwithout this bump. Empirically verified in an isolated fresh app before this\nPR was opened: RBAC 7.16.0 discovers rules registered by a dynamically-loaded\nplugin via GET /api/permission/plugins/condition-rules, and the rule.apply()\nfires at authorize-time as documented.\n\nCoincident with the version step, three sites needed migration:\n\n- plugins/registry-backend/src/catalog/catalogModule.ts drops the\n  @backstage/plugin-catalog-node/alpha import. catalog-node 2.x removed the\n  deprecated alpha re-exports; catalogProcessingExtensionPoint now lives on\n  the main entry point. Added an explicit BackendFeature return-type\n  annotation on the module so the declaration emitter has a nameable type;\n  without it, tsc emits export {} for this file and rollup fails the type\n  build with ''not exported by catalogModule.d.ts''. Same shape works with or\n  without the annotation on smaller files, so the annotation is a safety net\n  for the dts-rollup step, not a behavioral change.\n\n- plugins/pipeline-backend/src/plugin.ts switches resolvePackagePath from\n  @backstage/backend-common (removed) to @backstage/backend-plugin-api, which\n  now re-exports it alongside resolveSafeChildPath.\n\n- packages/app/src/components/catalog/EntityPage.tsx drops the\n  variant=\"gridItem\" prop from every entity card. plugin-catalog 1.32 -> 2.0\n  removed the prop and the cards now size to the Grid item they render into.\n  Twenty call sites; no other layout change intended.\n\nRoot-level devDependencies pick up @types/jest, @types/semver, jest, jest-cli,\n@jest/environment-jsdom-abstract, and jsdom. Backstage 1.53''s cli-module-test-\njest expects Jest 30 and refuses to configure a jsdom environment without\nthese peers present at the workspace root; without them, yarn test:all bails\nbefore running any test.\n\nVerification:\n\n- yarn build:all succeeds end-to-end for packages/app, packages/backend, and\n  every first-party plugin (butler, butler-backend, pipeline, pipeline-\n  backend, pipeline-common, registry, registry-backend, registry-common,\n  workspaces).\n- yarn test:all runs the full suite: 943 tests across 29 suites, all pass.\n- Local yarn start:backend boots cleanly on port 7007. /healthcheck returns\n  200. Every plugin reaches ''Plugin initialization complete'' without an\n  error line: proxy, permission, kubernetes, signals, techdocs, search,\n  auth, scaffolder, notifications, catalog, app. /api/catalog/entities\n  correctly requires credentials and returns AuthenticationError to an\n  unauthenticated request, confirming the permission framework is engaged.\n\nThis bump is deliberately non-behavioral. It does not touch the delegating\npolicy seam or the registry adjudicator; it just moves the floor up so the\nRBAC plugin adoption in the next PR can land.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"2df3dc99261b8f0f664f4515ce1b8418b474a391","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/2df3dc99261b8f0f664f4515ce1b8418b474a391"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012","verification":{"payload":"tree 2df3dc99261b8f