card. plugin-catalog 1.32 -> 2.0\n  removed the prop and the cards now size to the Grid item they render into.\n  Twenty call sites; no other layout change intended.\n\nRoot-level devDependencies pick up @types/jest, @types/semver, jest, jest-cli,\n@jest/environment-jsdom-abstract, and jsdom. Backstage 1.53''s cli-module-test-\njest expects Jest 30 and refuses to configure a jsdom environment without\nthese peers present at the workspace root; without them, yarn test:all bails\nbefore running any test.\n\nVerification:\n\n- yarn build:all succeeds end-to-end for packages/app, packages/backend, and\n  every first-party plugin (butler, butler-backend, pipeline, pipeline-\n  backend, pipeline-common, registry, registry-backend, registry-common,\n  workspaces).\n- yarn test:all runs the full suite: 943 tests across 29 suites, all pass.\n- Local yarn start:backend boots cleanly on port 7007. /healthcheck returns\n  200. Every plugin reaches ''Plugin initialization complete'' without an\n  error line: proxy, permission, kubernetes, signals, techdocs, search,\n  auth, scaffolder, notifications, catalog, app. /api/catalog/entities\n  correctly requires credentials and returns AuthenticationError to an\n  unauthenticated request, confirming the permission framework is engaged.\n\nThis bump is deliberately non-behavioral. It does not touch the delegating\npolicy seam or the registry adjudicator; it just moves the floor up so the\nRBAC plugin adoption in the next PR can land.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV7jhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYWAQAA4clRbVER5LY+3SWWb/99q4\nGrq8SQmw3vMHQIaO6envlMn906w5WYyY9LEcaAw/25JQLuv4fDjOKQLhDAEOYrkf\nfQZfyhpZXmuvZ9nMJezsrmL8303x6XLscYf6ufx0DCG1ULYGYWtI9ae9L+ONLWFG\nJ12z0do+4S6lBdQrgCN0T3VQK54fJuu1i3/mYHMc2l7YHEqCh/DtcKBf+HCLvLvY\nwDp9nHG+SI5GvmY2eTbLMvLdT18HYuvguLAvlPFwOG+MWsueYDd4Rp9hmQwfa1zO\nN4z5jHZ7/F6ODt+hF0hqWsVVdPEaYtHGcUij7+jx7PGk8MU6QeK8TltiuoBpsczd\niYltHcWzARe3hb/cJnQt84vgNNwBZEq6l2cXXk/VaExwhTNf+IztWelcUssOKFtc\nN4FwmoHfcP4XX9nN6cccylFXvZ8H/kBcV4E1mycvcI90gLU3zO5tqof5jrGElxzy\nAlmOenYzxtOajYpWCBR4oqaFr6EbWpd/TpbQO0TO956YgMHGieP3+Mt3xSFOtDeu\nJ8Nlmwt3S3K59PsEJlNU8a19SUS5nDBcYjBe+6+zkYWDJy2VEZzGsSwjRVguTHh2\nQejOJ4LLhk6eyviIKZairkY7E5knOsc4iM69/CHIra+coFaIJMhi5mLYANEZ4TDo\nCIinI1Y//o7BU4yMBiHw\n=5C7G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T16:44:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDYwYzZkZGI3Mjk4Y2Q4ODdlMDllNDYyYTZjZTA5YzRiMTAwNmIwMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a","sha":"2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a"}],"sha":"60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/60c6ddb7298cd887e09e462a6ce09c4b1006b012"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:55:40Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:55:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(permissions): namespace-delegated policy so plugins gate their own authz (#33)\n\n* feat(permissions): namespace-delegated policy so plugins gate their own authz\n\nUpstream Backstage enforces exactly one PermissionPolicy per instance\n(PolicyExtensionPointImpl.setPolicy throws on second registration),\nwhich forced every plugin''s authz decisions into the integrator''s\ncentral policy file. This adds butler-portal''s namespace-delegated\nseam on top of that constraint.\n\nThe new ButlerPortalDelegatingPolicy routes each authorize() call to\na plugin-registered adjudicator by permission-name prefix, via a new\nAuthAdjudicatorExtensionPoint. Unclaimed namespaces fall through to\nALLOW so Backstage core plugins (catalog, scaffolder, techdocs,\nsearch, kubernetes) keep working with zero per-plugin edit.\n\nRegistry''s inline role logic moves out of the central policy into a\nregistryAdjudicator module that consumes the new extension point.\nBehavior is unchanged; a matrix test in permissionPolicy.test.ts\nexercises the same (permission, identity) inputs through the new\nshape and an independent copy of the pre-delegation body, asserting\nequal PolicyDecision outputs across every registry.* branch and\nevery unclaimed namespace.\n\nAuthoring guide at docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md documents\nthe seam for plugin authors; the existing dynamic-plugins/authoring\ndoc cross-links to it. In-code comment in authAdjudicator.ts notes\nthis seam exists because upstream lacks one and to migrate off if\nupstream ships an official interface.\n\n* docs: ASCII-only in committed text (no em-dashes, no unicode arrows)\n\nStyle-guide sweep on the new files from the delegating-policy PR.\nTest suite re-run post-replacement: 183/183 passing, 0.42s.\nNo behavioral change.\n\n* fix(permissions): fail closed on thrown adjudicator + clarify guide\n\n- Dispatcher wraps the adjudicator call in try/catch and returns DENY\n  on any thrown or rejected exception. Prevents a broken adjudicator\n  from silently becoming an accidental ALLOW.\n- Test covers both throw and async reject; test suite now 184/184.\n- Authoring guide gains a Consuming the extension point section\n  making the in-tree-only status explicit and a Failure handling\n  section describing the fail-closed behavior.\n\n* fix(permissions): prefix-conflict guard on adjudicator registration\n\nThe prior guard only rejected exact-duplicate namespace strings.\nThat left a residual: registering \"reg\" alongside an existing\n\"registry.\" would silently swallow registry.* traffic based on\nregistration order. Extend the boot-time check to reject any pair\nwhere one namespace is a prefix of the other, and reject the\nempty-namespace case that would swallow every permission the\ndispatcher sees.\n\nAdds 5 new guard tests. Total suite now 191/191.\n\n* fix(example): explicit BackendFeature annotation on helloDynamicBackendPlugin\n\nExample build-test triggers when packages/backend/src/index.ts changes.\nThis PR touches that file, so the workflow ran for the first time\nsince 2026-06-15 and surfaced a latent TS2742: the inferred return\ntype of createBackendPlugin references an internal Backstage\ndeclaration file whose portable path cannot be resolved during\nout-of-tree tsc. Annotating the export with BackendFeature pins the\npublic return type and the example builds cleanly outside the\nworkspace, the same shape the adopter quickstart tells adopters to\nuse.\n\nUnrelated to the delegating-policy seam; fixing so the PR''s CI is\ngreen before merge.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"32bd21f17c1f04ed7b898d5e0575289b2b97316c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/32bd21f17c1f04ed7b898d5e0575289b2b97316c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a","verification":{"payload":"tree 32bd21f17c1f04ed7b898d5e0575289b2b97316c\nparent a89abbb2a79e19fb60b4347054e6b965ec89013d\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1783698940 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783698940 -0500\n\nfeat(permissions): namespace-delegated policy so plugins gate their own authz (#33)\n\n* feat(permissions): namespace-delegated policy so plugins gate their own authz\n\nUpstream Backstage enforces exactly one PermissionPolicy per instance\n(PolicyExtensionPointImpl.setPolicy throws on second registration),\nwhich forced every plugin''s authz decisions into the integrator''s\ncentral policy file. This adds butler-portal''s namespace-delegated\nseam on top of that constraint.\n\nThe new ButlerPortalDelegatingPolicy routes each authorize() call to\na plugin-registered adjudicator by permission-name prefix, via a new\nAuthAdjudicatorExtensionPoint. Unclaimed namespaces fall through to\nALLOW so Backstage core plugins (catalog, scaffolder, techdocs,\nsearch, kubernetes) keep working with zero per-plugin edit.\n\nRegistry''s inline role logic moves out of the central policy into a\nregistryAdjudicator module that consumes the new extension point.\nBehavior is unchanged; a matrix test in permissionPolicy.test.ts\nexercises the same (permission, identity) inputs through the new\nshape and an independent copy of the pre-delegation body, asserting\nequal PolicyDecision outputs across every registry.* branch and\nevery unclaimed namespace.\n\nAuthoring guide at docs/plugin-authoring/authorization.md documents\nthe seam for plugin authors; the existing dynamic-plugins/authoring\ndoc cross-links to it. In-code comment in authAdjudicator.ts notes\nthis seam exists because upstream lacks one and to migrate off if\nupstream ships an official interface.\n\n* docs: ASCII-only in committed text (no em-dashes, no unicode arrows)\n\nStyle-guide sweep on the new files from the delegating-policy PR.\nTest suite re-run post-replacement: 183/183 passing, 0.42s.\nNo behavioral change.\n\n* fix(permissions): fail closed on thrown adjudicator + clarify guide\n\n- Dispatcher wraps the adjudicator call in try/catch and returns DENY\n  on any thrown or rejected exception. Prevents a broken adjudicator\n  from silently becoming an accidental ALLOW.\n- Test covers both throw and async reject; test suite now 184/184.\n- Authoring guide gains a Consuming the extension point section\n  making the in-tree-only status explicit and a Failure handling\n  section describing the fail-closed behavior.\n\n* fix(permissions): prefix-conflict guard on adjudicator registration\n\nThe prior guard only rejected exact-duplicate namespace strings.\nThat left a residual: registering \"reg\" alongside an existing\n\"registry.\" would silently swallow registry.* traffic based on\nregistration order. Extend the boot-time check to reject any pair\nwhere one namespace is a prefix of the other, and reject the\nempty-namespace case that would swallow every permission the\ndispatcher sees.\n\nAdds 5 new guard tests. Total suite now 191/191.\n\n* fix(example): explicit BackendFeature annotation on helloDynamicBackendPlugin\n\nExample build-test triggers when packages/backend/src/index.ts changes.\nThis PR touches that file, so the workflow ran for the first time\nsince 2026-06-15 and surfaced a latent TS2742: the inferred return\ntype of createBackendPlugin references an internal Backstage\ndeclaration file whose portable path cannot be resolved during\nout-of-tree tsc. Annotating the export with BackendFeature pins the\npublic return type and the example builds cleanly outside the\nworkspace, the same shape the adopter quickstart tells adopters to\nuse.\n\nUnrelated to the delegating-policy seam; fixing so the PR''s CI is\ngreen before merge.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqURX8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs14QABceKStm1cl0sk2GUAaTQDCp\njfMSvJlSqpeD0OhtHSq7SPDZmlnxMzXfFU3nmN9SRG2l5Og9Bfbu2p8ky7aJlDtp\nhBbR4oVxHHvWxfOF40YtsaWKBCyqR2UOIucYZ7NPs/ZMe1Kerp+DSuYG6vvUaVTA\nGabP6sYv9sIN1REDqTcd90qE3cPWp0zhgQiYSxrEQLSS1CjP8sQn9NmyPaJoYmoL\n46YSaCJk5jJ92e4snhmqdadvDk/4hLgv11MrtrUxSAiUV2yvmbKEjtY8+ZdtUfam\nm8ndWSnbkmMEmXzBODdRxfoRu4nD9gaLNiPQECq68myw5JNsEDuT8tQBXANr2WyT\nfdZPj96zcn3UT7j7f7HzHs3lzJLdjLyLE13OT6l9xiQRN9Ms6KyXyvnr2/y8aTn4\njMs7Y1zzz9B8YFL7EfiOGxrysI1asA6CUn+82BoSL7g3uw18ylpF961FeCNL21UV\no0QFDckMZi0ZxfLGxwYS5qkunS9bt8+q2ZV9tg1jj7A7wq++hqJj9jGHLBulaYWr\nyBlxkQpss/hfWNFvSiVY7GTXGtDloG/rv22nFuvr6+Fm3iB6iZo6NTqh11VH9Wps\n4URfA229PLR2f6Z/sUwDbWkRfMwCe3O9l7QWXQUnOdMvq1vxlBBgPFC6Ca/DS/bM\nuwxsLrwPiRnmlOjDeBrY\n=6RaV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-10T15:55:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDJhMTc3MmFlNTZlMWFhOWQzZTNkM2FlZDA3Yjg4MGJjM2FkMmEzNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/a89abbb2a79e19fb60b4347054e6b965ec89013d","sha":"a89abbb2a79e19fb60b4347054e6b965ec89013d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/a89abbb2a79e19fb60b4347054e6b965ec89013d"}],"sha":"2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/2a1772ae56e1aa9d3e3d3aed07b880bc3ad2a35a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/a89abbb2a79e19fb60b4347054e6b965ec89013d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T15:19:35Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T15:19:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(Dockerfile): downgrade node base image to node:20-bookworm-slim (#32)\n\nNode 22 changed stream close semantics in a way that races node-fetch\nv2.7.0''s gunzip pipeline, causing ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE on\nevery gzipped HTTP response. In Backstage this breaks all plugin-to-\nplugin catalog fetches (localhost:7007 calls returning 200 with\nAccept-Encoding: gzip get gunzip errors), all GitLab discovery API\ncalls, and any TechDocs UrlPreparer path that fetches via node-fetch.\nUser-visible symptom: /docs pages 500 on metadata + sync endpoints\neven with permission plugin and default auth policy disabled.\n\nNode 20 has the older stream close semantics node-fetch v2 was written\nagainst. Docs render correctly under node:20-bookworm-slim.\n\nLong-term fix: bump Backstage core to 1.28+ which uses native fetch /\nundici. Out of scope for this patch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","tree":{"sha":"42d2a9f9462631a572dc988c050266555c240654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/42d2a9f9462631a572dc988c050266555c240654"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/a89abbb2a79e19fb60b4347054e6b965ec89013d","verification":{"payload":"tree 42d2a9f9462631a572dc988c050266555c240654\nparent 70f780dd2c87eff6ffe8bd57b19aa3b3858ad2ae\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1783523975 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783523975 -0500\n\nfix(Dockerfile): downgrade node base image to node:20-bookworm-slim (#32)\n\nNode 22 changed stream close semantics in a way that races node-fetch\nv2.7.0''s gunzip pipeline, causing ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE on\nevery gzipped HTTP response. In Backstage this breaks all plugin-to-\nplugin catalog fetches (localhost:7007 calls returning 200 with\nAccept-Encoding: gzip get gunzip errors), all GitLab discovery API\ncalls, and any TechDocs UrlPreparer path that fetches via node-fetch.\nUser-visible symptom: /docs pages 500 on metadata + sync endpoints\neven with permission plugin and default auth policy disabled.\n\nNode 20 has the older stream close semantics node-fetch v2 was written\nagainst. Docs render correctly under node:20-bookworm-slim.\n\nLong-term fix: bump Backstage core to 1.28+ which uses native fetch /\nundici. Out of scope for this patch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Bagan <andrew.bagan-2@corteva.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTmqHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXJUQAJ+197zBc+dhKRkD92rsQQwe\nsKxtmEm3VRZ+ihsfX5B5yxt937p3CIycnw/Goy3lWALcwzOZNGQh00n5QY8w25vr\nqFsGGGRDJ2IASnXS2NVpEEy+vHVXVSw3p731E4owazKZYWql1Pq7MYnmXTk/imJM\n2pnPYqFYlp3XNAL8ahmnj9mXr4vDIXBT5a17K3JiYQaiI6AE1aI/7FslBldciqI/\n/zsPorCVbSeEm4iio7VkQTUyiqb8SswZLNgg6pPF6XPONOeYchr/AL6PEjacsCJu\nn+22B0HM0KQWXuz1+UG9ajluMAhuCk0lr2gHFTdoI5vjebFCCXNZEcTUy1KjLZW0\nolM7TA3LOUp0ZoB3jZnbsPl1aSLQ1VAbAsT1HW/Q2+yDaK/8WNSQHZ3FqFZ6A12d\n9H6wXWaOPAYBxL2WixwCqui30SBq4fXyD9VI9+smZiTg2vJ93c/SHN/Y8GYY3dBs\n/hgGZXYtcYAmRJC4fnj3d9T4cfXghf/MqNMsRFbIl68lSicaOtzjPmdwjP8xYyak\nCFrrH5rwBlj+VpFTGm59E