/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/3e9c0802efef69c6db458660b839dd7682c2ee74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:57:30Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:57:30Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"ci(boot-test): smoke-test fixture access before installer step\n\nIsolates whether the GITHUB_TOKEN inherits the package access grant\nthe org owner added via UI, or whether the installer''s auth mount path\nis the failure point. The smoke step runs oras manifest fetch\nagainst the test fixture using the same GH_USER + GH_TOKEN combo the\ninstaller container''s docker auth uses.","tree":{"sha":"88c05e405a2b53801250b3b986ed2c3b4a7f9e9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/88c05e405a2b53801250b3b986ed2c3b4a7f9e9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/3e9c0802efef69c6db458660b839dd7682c2ee74","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/3e9c0802efef69c6db458660b839dd7682c2ee74","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDNlOWMwODAyZWZlZjY5YzZkYjQ1ODY2MGI4MzlkZDc2ODJjMmVlNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c","sha":"eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c"}],"sha":"3e9c0802efef69c6db458660b839dd7682c2ee74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/3e9c0802efef69c6db458660b839dd7682c2ee74"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:09:29Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:09:29Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"ci(boot-test): allocate WORK under RUNNER_TEMP for runner-managed Docker\n\nOn butler-runners the host''s /tmp is not inside the Docker daemon''s\nview of the filesystem. mktemp -d defaulted to /tmp; subsequent\nbind-mounts of single-file paths under WORK silently resolved as\nempty directories inside the installer container, producing\n''read /etc/butler-portal/dynamic-plugins.yaml: is a directory''.\n\nRUNNER_TEMP is the GitHub Actions tempdir guaranteed to live inside\nthe runner''s bind-mounted workspace; GITHUB_WORKSPACE is the same\nguarantee one directory up. Fall back to /tmp for local runs (where\nthe daemon and host share filesystem).","tree":{"sha":"927fdaf6d6a630dd37e70f5bac656f71143baed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/927fdaf6d6a630dd37e70f5bac656f71143baed3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGViMzM3ODM2ZWMyZWQ1MmI5NjRkZmYxMTBlZmMxYjcwNGRkMzgzNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886","sha":"e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886"}],"sha":"eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/eb337836ec2ed52b964dff110efc1b704dd3836c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:02:50Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:02:50Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"ci(boot-test): surface installer raw output for CI diagnosis\n\nReplace the | grep | head filter on the installer pipeline with a\nwrite-to-file + cat. The filter swallows installer failures (Docker\nauth, oras pull, integrity, write permissions) when none of the\nexpected events match. Without seeing the raw output, a CI failure\nshows ''plugin not in /remotes'' with no signal about why the install\nstep did or did not produce a populated volume.","tree":{"sha":"a7af02b6aa2ca3cf25a8e0ff5c26713046f5c430","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/a7af02b6aa2ca3cf25a8e0ff5c26713046f5c430"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGU2MmU4ZjhlODQ2ODMzMjE3NzQwNWZmYWU4NzM4ZTRhYThkZTI4ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f","sha":"832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f"}],"sha":"e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/e62e8f8e8468332177405ffae8738e4aa8de2886"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:56:42Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:56:42Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"ci(boot-test): GH_USER/GH_TOKEN env fallbacks for CI runs\n\nThe boot-test scripts called `gh api user --jq .login` to resolve\nthe Docker auth username. In CI the workflow''s GITHUB_TOKEN cannot\nhit the /user endpoint (Resource not accessible by integration / 403).\nFall back to env-provided GH_USER and GH_TOKEN when present; the\nworkflow sets GH_USER=github.actor and GH_TOKEN=GITHUB_TOKEN, the\nsame combination docker/login-action used above to log into ghcr.","tree":{"sha":"a029da5dfbd324e600036615e7fde88396ea1062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/a029da5dfbd324e600036615e7fde88396ea1062"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDgzMmNlM2NmMDJlNzFmOThkYTkzOTMzZDdiYTRhYjE5ZjAzMmQzOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e","sha":"7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e"}],"sha":"832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/832ce3cf02e71f98da93933d7ba4ab19f032d38f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:52:31Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:52:31Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"ci(boot-test): track playwright package-lock.json for npm ci\n\nThe release-boot-test workflow uses npm ci so it gets a deterministic\nPlaywright install. The lockfile was gitignored from the example\nplugin''s .gitignore copy, which excluded it from the harness''s own\npackage-lock.json. Track it: ~2300-line file, but only generated once\nwhen the @playwright/test version bumps, and it pins the exact tree\nthe boot-test harness exercises against.","tree":{"sha":"6f1e32a1df28ae1070e224f98676b89e1cf6c0ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/6f1e32a1df28ae1070e224f98676b89e1cf6c0ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDcwMjViYjhhZjYxMDgxMDJlNzlhOTU0ZTliZjk0YzQwZjhiMDAxOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c","sha":"21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c"}],"sha":"7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/7025bb8af6108102e79a954e9bf94c40f8b0018e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:49:39Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:49:39Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"ci: add release-boot-test workflow on butler-runners for amd64 verify\n\nCloses the off-prod amd64 verify gap before the live cutover. The local\nboot-test on the maintainer''s arm64 laptop validates the SOURCE; the\nreleased image is amd64-only and was unproven on real amd64 before\nthis. The Rosetta path crashes the installer Go binary under emulation,\nso the maintainer-laptop verification cannot reach the published\nartifact. butler-runners are amd64 Ubuntu Noble (confirmed via the\nexisting image-build job logs) and built the released image; running\nthe boot-test harness there proves the same artifact boots on the same\narch that produced it.\n\nThe workflow_dispatch inputs default to the 0.5.1 release identifiers\nso running with no overrides verifies \"is butler-portal:0.5.1 actually\nbootable end-to-end.\" The runtime 3-case test and the Playwright\nmarker assertion both run against the pulled artifact. uname check at\nthe top of the job hard-fails if a runner ever changes arch.","tree":{"sha":"3cb576d16098d21f87a11bbfeace872c6d963df7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/3cb576d16098d21f87a11bbfeace872c6d963df7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDIxOTI3ZmRiNWY2MTM4OWNmOWViNjA1MTJkN2RjZjYzMGY4YWM4MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95","sha":"ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95"}],"sha":"21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/21927fdb5f61389cf9eb60512d7dcf630f8ac82c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T15:26:48Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T15:26:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(portal): 0.5.1 dynamic frontend plugin loading + chart NODE_PATH + plugin CLI wrapper (#23)\n\nCloses the deferred 0.5.0 frontend stub. THE GATE is green: a real\nfederated remote loads through the real manifest path and renders the\nmarker at /hello-dynamic-plugin.\n\nThree changes:\n1. Frontend bridge replaced -- @scalprum/* -> @module-federation/runtime\n   directly. Scalprum requires webpack MF host runtime that Backstage\n   CLI does not build; runtime package maintains its own scope map.\n   Host singleton table includes the Material-UI v4 split (both\n   @material-ui/core/styles AND @material-ui/styles; second is\n   non-obvious, captured for adopter docs).\n2. Chart 0.5.0 -> 0.5.1 with NODE_PATH=/app/node_modules on the\n   backstage container when dynamicPlugins.enabled. Without it the\n   plugin scanner crashes at boot. Gated on enabled so disabled-state\n   pod template stays byte-identical to 0.4.0/0.5.0-disabled.\n3. @butlerlabs/portal-plugin-cli wrapper at cli/portal-plugin-cli --\n   thin honest delegation to rhdh-cli; the adopter-facing command\n   surface is stable independent of rhdh-cli evolution.\n\nVerification: tsc clean, 749 tests pass, 26/26 helm unittests pass,\nruntime 3-case boot-test distinguishable, Playwright marker assertion\nvisible on /hello-dynamic-plugin.","tree":{"sha":"19549807f8f53f7b68319f256134ddd999a3d658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/19549807f8f53f7b68319f256134ddd999a3d658"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95","verification":{"payload":"tree 19549807f8f53f7b68319f256134ddd999a3d658\nparent 0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1781450808 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781450808 -0500\n\nfeat(portal): 0.5.1 dynamic frontend plugin loading + chart NODE_PATH + plugin CLI wrapper (#23)\n\nCloses the deferred 0.5.0 frontend stub. THE GATE is green: a real\nfederated remote loads through the real manifest path and renders the\nmarker at /hello-dynamic-plugin.\n\nThree changes:\n1. Frontend bridge replaced -- @scalprum/* -> @module-federation/runtime\n   directly. Scalprum requires webpack MF host runtime that Backstage\n   CLI does not build; runtime package maintains its own scope map.\n   Host singleton table includes the Material-UI v4 split (both\n   @material-ui/core/styles AND @material-ui/styles; second is\n   non-obvious, captured for adopter docs).\n2. Chart 0.5.0 -> 0.5.1 with NODE_PATH=/app/node_modules on the\n   backstage container when dynamicPlugins.enabled. Without it the\n   plugin scanner crashes at boot. Gated on enabled so disabled-state\n   pod template stays byte-identical to 0.4.0/0.5.0-disabled.\n3. @butlerlabs/portal-plugin-cli wrapper at cli/portal-plugin-cli --\n   thin honest delegation to rhdh-cli; the adopter-facing command\n   surface is stable independent of rhdh-cli evolution.\n\nVerification: tsc clean, 749 tests pass, 26/26 helm unittests pass,\nruntime 3-case boot-test distinguishable, Playwright marker assertion\nvisible on /hello-dynamic-plugin.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLsg4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANCoQAC2ht95TEW5rIA7WrIiQ7KRw\ncQBvPs+rpjlAN8dzPBB4q5OQYln4cW4LaX6WPNKaAbq5NUshQdzbJUknwnszf+F3\n59eZ3mAOmSgBzptQggrRYTYJRGL5w1doyRwYWXEbDzQ1p7cRBb4DLXPZydKFBoXc\nHp9BQpABtM48i1WvlcOXTvHLnSynMvmTs8dOo/mn7Nhk23HEGbTCneTtsgwmwiFT\n7CS8UIyyyfBAcRn5iFTAdxxddW7ga/+PpeKv2dGLZJPG1ADOqTfoIP0oFblPCIJm\nVSOZlb5BQLHK07hGyv2VA4p3CqTGIXtJiTS1wBlhMw+d+S9tp7i65Y779iIP/6ZI\n/CYQ4txQZdGB3GqmQpEDW75/OZhvgrMCfmQZejnu1Utcg2xvzrmz8P3/kOOHTr+h\naiKOaKIrSlF89TWRwCrL2AQ+7yhzkLAX7tfxYtn5efFYWFO332ZZ3Qek7YcDav6f\n3EBo7krn5yKDGb9M/uSZz3yaZA6b7NFAaCdzMVecBiYW9bCCaeM4wB6P3Vy0MrAu\nMMvaS8axvGAyQBCjSn/D3396GyguVlIgGWhLlu7XiRP5X5PQkhNuVgPyW4tw9B8B\nT192zVORSG/YtTkRH/H+s9D+G7ViD0vjff5+bMEvoFubDVLDbp8zgr6qUPoH66oV\nzWXi8aYATnNQfGcSyWS3\n=YaV6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-14T15:26:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGFiOWNiYjY1Zjk3MGYzYjAyMTgyMGFjYjdlNzFlYTBiMGIzZmFjOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895","sha":"0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895"}],"sha":"ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/ab9cbb65f970f3b021820acb7e71ea0b0b3fac95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T01:48:05Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T01:48:05Z","email":"agtbstunts@gmail.com","name":"atbagan"},"message":"docs(chart): pin helm-unittest to CI version when running locally\n\nThe .github/workflows/helm.yaml CI workflow pins helm-unittest to\n0.5.2. Local installs default to the latest 1.x release, which is more\npermissive about absent paths in notContains assertions. Tests that\npass locally on 1.x can fail in CI on 0.5.2 with ''unknown path'' errors.\nDocument the local install command so contributors can keep parity\nwith CI.","tree":{"sha":"d6f9843ae29ce80e7c6f170b8653cd04c118055c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/d6f9843ae29ce80e7c6f170b8653cd04c118055c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDAyNTRlODAwMjczOTZlYmIwYzhmY2JiMTI1ZjVjNWZjMmQwY2Q4OTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600","sha":"98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600"}],"sha":"0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/0254e80027396ebb0c8fcbb125f5c5fc2d0cd895"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T00:38:18Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T00:38:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(portal): chart 0.5.0 dynamic plugins (backend + chart + frontend normalization + installer + boot-test green) (#22)\n\n* feat(portal): wire dynamicPluginsFeatureLoader alongside the static gates\n\nPhase 1 of chart 0.5.0 -- dynamic plugin support.\n\nAdds @backstage/backend-dynamic-feature-service pinned at 0.7.6 (the\nhighest version that''s peer-dep compatible with our backend-defaults\n^0.13.1 + backend-plugin-api ^1.6.1 pins; ^0.7.9 wants backend-defaults\n^0.15.2 and ^0.8.x wants backend-plugin-api ^1.9.1 which we cannot\ntake per PR #20''s module-v1.1 startup-crash story).\n\nbackend.add(dynamicPluginsFeatureLoader()) runs alongside the existing\ncreateBackendFeatureLoader for the four Butler-Labs-branded plugins.\nThe static gates (butler/workspaces/registry/pipeline) are untouched\n-- selectEnabledButlerLabsPlugins still drives feature yielding for\nthose four, and the genuine-off semantics are preserved.\n\nWhen dynamicPlugins.rootDirectory is unset in app-config (the default),\nthe loader is a no-op: no directory to scan, no plugins to register.\nNon-adopters render identically to the pre-0.5.0 backend.\n\nOpen-product framing recorded in the comment block: enabling a dynamic\nplugin is operator config, not a license check. No entitlement call,\nno remote check. Customer ships a plugin in their own OCI registry,\nreferences it in HelmRelease values, it loads.\n\nBackend tests: 7/7 still passing. yarn tsc clean. No frontend changes\nyet (Phase 3). No chart changes yet (Phase 2).\n\n* feat(portal): chart 0.5.0 dynamicPlugins infrastructure (disabled = byte-identical to 0.4.0)\n\nPhase 2 of chart 0.5.0 -- dynamic plugin support. Chart now ships the\ninfrastructure (init container, volumes, env, ConfigMap) gated on a\ndefault-disabled values block. With dynamicPlugins.enabled=false (the\nchart default), the rendered pod template is byte-identical to chart\n0.4.0 -- proven by a snapshot test captured against 0.4.0 baseline and\nasserted at 0.5.0. Customers bumping from 0.4.0 to 0.5.0 do NOT roll\ntheir running pods until they opt in.\n\nWhat ships:\n\n- Chart.yaml: version 0.4.0 -> 0.5.0, appVersion 0.4.0 -> 0.5.0\n- values.yaml: new dynamicPlugins block (enabled default false,\n  installer image/tag/pullPolicy/continueOnError, allowedSources,\n  plugins[])\n- templates/deployment.yaml: conditional init container\n  install-dynamic-plugins, conditional dynamic-plugins emptyDir +\n  dynamic-plugins-config ConfigMap volumes, conditional volumeMount\n  into the main container, conditional APP_CONFIG_dynamicPlugins_*\n  env vars. All conditionals gate on dynamicPlugins.enabled\n- templates/dynamic-plugins-configmap.yaml (new): ConfigMap consumed\n  by the init container, rendered only when dynamicPlugins.enabled.\n  Schema fields: continueOnError, allowedSources, plugins (each with\n  required package + required integrity + optional disabled +\n  optional pluginConfig)\n\nThe values schema enforces from day one:\n\n- integrity sha512 MANDATORY per plugin entry. The chart''s required-\n  guard fails render when missing, with a clear remediation message.\n  Test pins this.\n- allowedSources UNSET semantics: PERMISSIVE (any source the operator\n  references accepted). Documented explicitly in the chart comment\n  and the ConfigMap rendering. Production operators SHOULD set\n  allowedSources to constrain registries; documented permissive is\n  fine, silent permissive would be a footgun.\n- continueOnError default FALSE: pod fails to start on any pull or\n  integrity error so operators see it immediately. Tunable per\n  cluster.\n\nOpen-product framing recorded in the values block comment: enabling\na plugin is OPERATOR CONFIG, not a license check. Software is fully\nopen and complete; the operator decides what runs in their portal.\nA customer can ship any plugin in their own OCI registry, reference\nit in values, and it loads. No entitlement call anywhere in the\nchart or backend wiring.\n\nTests:\n\n- tests/dynamic-plugins-disabled_test.yaml: snapshot proves pod template\n  byte-identical to 0.4.0 baseline AND explicit notContains assertions\n  on init container / volume / env vars. The load-bearing contract for\n  customer upgrades.\n- tests/dynamic-plugins-enabled_test.yaml: positive tests on init\n  container presence, installer image + pullPolicy from values,\n  volume + volumeMount shape, env wiring, continueOnError both\n  values, ConfigMap rendering with allowedSources empty + set,\n  integrity required-guard, well-formed plugin entry round-trip.\n- tests/plugins-override_test.yaml (existing): 9 chart tests for the\n  0.4.0 per-plugin gates still pass.\n\nTotal: 26 chart tests + 2 snapshots, all passing. helm template\nsanity-checked with enabled-with-plugin, defaults, and butler-on-no-\nsecret (required-guard still fires).\n\nNo backend or frontend changes in this commit. Backend wiring landed\nin 2839e5a (Phase 1). Frontend host shell refactor is Phase 3, next.\n\n* feat(portal): data-driven route table + DiscoveryAnchor for dynamic-plugin host shell (Phase 3)\n\nApp.tsx''s hardcoded FlatRoutes children move to a BASELINE_ROUTES constant in\npackages/app/src/baselineRoutes.tsx. DataDrivenFlatRoutes (function component)\nrenders FlatRoutes from BASELINE_ROUTES merged with dynamic routes from\nDynamicRootContext. A DiscoveryAnchor (function component returning null)\ncarries the same Route JSX at module scope so the Backstage createApp walker\nindexes every routable extension''s routeRef via childDiscoverer recursion.\nThe walker cannot recurse into DataDrivenFlatRoutes'' render output, so the\nanchor is the indexing path.\n\nRoot.tsx gets a single new <DynamicMenuSlot /> inside the Menu SidebarGroup.\nWhen DynamicRootContext is empty (chart 0.5.0 default), the Slot renders zero\nDOM nodes; the rendered sidebar is identical to 0.4.0.\n\nPR #20 gating is preserved verbatim: each Butler Labs entry wraps its plugin\npage in <ButlerLabsRouteElement configKey=\"...\"> with the page passed as\nchildren (the walker contract from 287025e).\n\nRegression net:\n\n* BaselineRoutes.test.tsx (12 tests): structural pins on each Butler Labs\n  path''s wrapping + configKey + children identity, plus render-path tests\n  that mount the actual DataDrivenFlatRoutes under MockConfigApi and\n  confirm the disabled state through the new mounting produces the same\n  PluginNotEnabledPage UX as 0.4.0.\n* AppNormalization.test.tsx (2 tests, made load-bearing): visible FlatRoutes\n  wrapped in VisibleRenderRoutes function component so the DiscoveryAnchor\n  is the only walker-visible path; mutation that empties the anchor surfaces\n  as \"Routable extension was not discovered\".\n* DisabledStateParity.test.tsx (1 test): DynamicMenuSlot renders zero DOM\n  nodes when dynamicMenuItems is empty (chart 0.5.0 default state).\n\nMutation-proven: render-path gate removal, dependency mis-read via configKey\nswap, two-path divergence (anchor correct, render bypasses gate), and\nanchor-only entry removal each trip a specifically named test with the exact\nerror class (integrity/gate behavior or walker \"was not discovered\").\n\nThe 5 source files producing the user-visible Butler Labs UX\n(ButlerLabsRouteElement, ButlerLabsSubmenuItem, butlerLabsPluginsMeta,\nPluginNotEnabledPage, HomeNavigationCards) are bit-for-bit identical to\n0.4.0 (git diff exit=0 vs 90ccb1e). The mounting mechanism changed; the\ncomponents producing the UX did not.\n\n66 tests pass across 10 suites in packages/app. yarn tsc clean. yarn lint\nclean.\n\n* test(portal): Phase 5 boot-test harness against the published 0.5.0-rc image\n\nAdds the boot-test scripts and Playwright tests that close the Phase 3\nINFERRED enabled-render against the actual published image (rc.1\nbutler-portal + rc.2 butler-portal-plugin-installer), not local builds.\n\nscripts/phase-5-boot-test/run-installer-e2e.sh\n\n* Pushes a real fixture tarball to ghcr.io as an OCI artifact, computes\n  its sha512 SRI, then runs the published installer image against three\n  scenarios:\n   A. integrity matches -> install succeeds, audit logs structured\n   B. wrong sha512 + continueOnError=false (default) -> exit non-zero,\n      no plugin installed, audit log surfaces expected vs computed +\n      continueOnError_false fatal\n   C. wrong sha512 + continueOnError=true -> exit 0, rejected plugin\n      not installed, rejection logged (best-effort opt-in)\n* Mounts Docker auth via DOCKER_CONFIG env (operator path uses\n  ImagePullSecrets via the chart).\n* The Phase 4 bats tests at the unit layer pin the contracts; this\n  e2e proves they hold on the real image against a real GHCR pull\n  (the published-image gate the config.d.ts lesson called for).\n\nscripts/phase-5-boot-test/playwright/butler-labs-enabled-render.spec.ts\n\n* Closes Task #65 (Phase 3 INFERRED enabled-render verified on real\n  artifact). Boots the published portal with all four Butler Labs flags\n  on (Butler Labs deployment shape) plus a postgres sidecar; for each\n  plugin route navigates the headless browser there and asserts:\n   - URL matches the route (catches silent sign-in redirect)\n   - SignIn Guest tile is detached (catches vacuous-pass on the\n     sign-in fallback page, which Backstage renders at any URL when\n     auth fails)\n   - main element renders >50 chars (catches blank/error states)\n   - \"was not discovered\" error absent (the 287025e contract: the\n     DiscoveryAnchor indexed the routable extension via createApp''s\n     walker pass on the published image)\n   - PluginNotEnabledPage role string absent\n   - configKey chip absent\n* The disabled-state branch verifies the Phase 3 #6 guarantee on the\n  real image: with all four flags off, each route renders\n  PluginNotEnabledPage with the correct role string and the right\n  configKey chip.\n\nscripts/phase-5-boot-test/run-boot-test.sh\n\n* Driver script chaining the boot + installer e2e + Playwright tests.\n\nThe harness caught two real bugs the unit tests missed:\n\n1. lib/oci-pull.sh used `oras pull --quiet` which does not exist on\n   oras 1.2.0 (now fixed in installer 0.1.0-rc.2: --no-tty). The bats\n   fakebin accepted any flag; the strict-mode fakebin in installer\n   rc.2 rejects unknown flags.\n\n2. Backstage''s guest provider returns 403 outside development unless\n   `auth.providers.guest.dangerouslyAllowOutsideDevelopment=true`.\n   Test harness now sets this env var; deployments inherit production\n   auth providers from the chart.\n\n* fix(chart): isNull instead of notContains on absent volumes path (helm-unittest 0.5.2 CI pin)\n\nhelm-unittest 0.5.2 (the version pinned in .github/workflows/helm.yaml)\nerrors with \"unknown path spec.template.spec.volumes\" when notContains\nis asserted against a path that does not exist in the rendered template.\nhelm-unittest 1.x is lenient about absent paths; the Phase 2 local test\nruns were against 1.x and passed silently.\n\nIn the chart-default disabled state (no butlerSigning secret, no\ndynamicPlugins), the deployment template gates the entire spec.template.spec.volumes\nblock behind `or .butlerSigning .dynamicPlugins.enabled`; neither is\npresent in this test''s config, so the block does not render and the\npath is absent.\n\nThe intent of the test is \"no volume named dynamic-plugins appears in\nthe rendered pod template.\" An absent volumes section satisfies that\nas strongly as an empty one. isNull is the version-portable assertion\nfor absence: 0.5.2 + 1.x both accept it, and a future regression that\nadds any volume (dynamic-plugins or otherwise) when dynamicPlugins is\noff would trip this assertion the same way notContains would have.\n\nVerified locally with both helm-unittest 0.5.2 (CI pin) and 1.1.1\n(local default). 26 tests pass on both.","tree":{"sha":"d8e50e9d41f8c0dd761e9867db60eb22921e2d32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/d8e50e9d41f8c0dd761e9867db60eb22921e2d32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600","verification":{"payload":"tree d8e50e9d41f8c0dd761e9867db60eb22921e2d32\nparent c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1781397498 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781397498 -0500\n\nfeat(portal): chart 0.5.0 dynamic plugins (backend + chart + frontend normalization + installer + boot-test green) (#22)\n\n* feat(portal): wire dynamicPluginsFeatureLoader alongside the static gates\n\nPhase 1 of chart 0.5.0 -- dynamic plugin support.\n\nAdds @backstage/backend-dynamic-feature-service pinned at 0.7.6 (the\nhighest version that''s peer-dep compatible with our backend-defaults\n^0.13.1 + backend-plugin-api ^1.6.1 pins; ^0.7.9 wants backend-defaults\n^0.15.2 and ^0.8.x wants backend-plugin-api ^1.9.1 which we cannot\ntake per PR #20''s module-v1.1 startup-crash story).\n\nbackend.add(dynamicPluginsFeatureLoader()) runs alongside the existing\ncreateBackendFeatureLoader for the four Butler-Labs-branded plugins.\nThe static gates (butler/workspaces/registry/pipeline) are untouched\n-- selectEnabledButlerLabsPlugins still drives feature yielding for\nthose four, and the genuine-off semantics are preserved.\n\nWhen dynamicPlugins.rootDirectory is unset in app-config (the default),\nthe loader is a no-op: no directory to scan, no plugins to register.\nNon-adopters render identically to the pre-0.5.0 backend.\n\nOpen-product framing recorded in the comment block: enabling a dynamic\nplugin is operator config, not a license check. No entitlement call,\nno remote check. Customer ships a plugin in their own OCI registry,\nreferences it in HelmRelease values, it loads.\n\nBackend tests: 7/7 still passing. yarn tsc clean. No frontend changes\nyet (Phase 3). No chart changes yet (Phase 2).\n\n* feat(portal): chart 0.5.0 dynamicPlugins infrastructure (disabled = byte-identical to 0.4.0)\n\nPhase 2 of chart 0.5.0 -- dynamic plugin support. Chart now ships the\ninfrastructure (init container, volumes, env, ConfigMap) gated on a\ndefault-disabled values block. With dynamicPlugins.enabled=false (the\nchart default), the rendered pod template is byte-identical to chart\n0.4.0 -- proven by a snapshot test captured against 0.4.0 baseline and\nasserted at 0.5.0. Customers bumping from 0.4.0 to 0.5.0 do NOT roll\ntheir running pods until they opt in.\n\nWhat ships:\n\n- Chart.yaml: version 0.4.0 -> 0.5.0, appVersion 0.4.0 -> 0.5.0\n- values.yaml: new dynamicPlugins block (enabled default false,\n  installer image/tag/pullPolicy/continueOnError, allowedSources,\n  plugins[])\n- templates/deployment.yaml: conditional init container\n  install-dynamic-plugins, conditional dynamic-plugins emptyDir +\n  dynamic-plugins-config ConfigMap volumes, conditional volumeMount\n  into the main container, conditional APP_CONFIG_dynamicPlugins_*\n  env vars. All conditionals gate on dynamicPlugins.enabled\n- templates/dynamic-plugins-configmap.yaml (new): ConfigMap consumed\n  by the init container, rendered only when dynamicPlugins.enabled.\n  Schema fields: continueOnError, allowedSources, plugins (each with\n  required package + required integrity + optional disabled +\n  optional pluginConfig)\n\nThe values schema enforces from day one:\n\n- integrity sha512 MANDATORY per plugin entry. The chart''s required-\n  guard fails render when missing, with a clear remediation message.\n  Test pins this.\n- allowedSources UNSET semantics: PERMISSIVE (any source the operator\n  references accepted). Documented explicitly in the chart comment\n  and the ConfigMap rendering. Production operators SHOULD set\n  allowedSources to constrain registries; documented permissive is\n  fine, silent permissive would be a footgun.\n- continueOnError default FALSE: pod fails to start on any pull or\n  integrity error so operators see it immediately. Tunable per\n  cluster.\n\nOpen-product framing recorded in the values block comment: enabling\na plugin is OPERATOR CONFIG, not a license check. Software is fully\nopen and complete; the operator decides what runs in their portal.\nA customer can ship any plugin in their own OCI registry, reference\nit in values, and it loads. No entitlement call anywhere in the\nchart or backend wiring.\n\nTests:\n\n- tests/dynamic-plugins-disabled_test.yaml: snapshot proves pod template\n  byte-identical to 0.4.0 baseline AND explicit notContains assertions\n  on init container / volume / env vars. The load-bearing contract for\n  customer upgrades.\n- tests/dynamic-plugins-enabled_test.yaml: positive tests on init\n  container presence, installer image + pullPolicy from values,\n  volume + volumeMount shape, env wiring, continueOnError both\n  values, ConfigMap rendering with allowedSources empty + set,\n  integrity required-guard, well-formed plugin entry round-trip.\n- tests/plugins-override_test.yaml (existing): 9 chart tests for the\n  0.4.0 per-plugin gates still pass.\n\nTotal: 26 chart tests + 2 snapshots, all passing. helm template\nsanity-checked with enabled-with-plugin, defaults, and butler-on-no-\nsecret (required-guard still fires).\n\nNo backend or frontend changes in this commit. Backend wiring landed\nin 2839e5a (Phase 1). Frontend host shell refactor is Phase 3, next.\n\n* feat(portal): data-driven route table + DiscoveryAnchor for dynamic-plugin host shell (Phase 3)\n\nApp.tsx''s hardcoded FlatRoutes children move to a BASELINE_ROUTES constant in\npackages/app/src/baselineRoutes.tsx. DataDrivenFlatRoutes (function component)\nrenders FlatRoutes from BASELINE_ROUTES merged with dynamic routes from\nDynamicRootContext. A DiscoveryAnchor (function component returning null)\ncarries the same Route JSX at module scope so the Backstage createApp walker\nindexes every routable extension''s routeRef via childDiscoverer recursion.\nThe walker cannot recurse into DataDrivenFlatRoutes'' render output, so the\nanchor is the indexing path.\n\nRoot.tsx gets a single new <DynamicMenuSlot /> inside the Menu SidebarGroup.\nWhen DynamicRootContext is empty (chart 0.5.0 default), the Slot renders zero\nDOM nodes; the rendered sidebar is identical to 0.4.0.\n\nPR #20 gating is preserved verbatim: each Butler Labs entry wraps its plugin\npage in <ButlerLabsRouteElement configKey=\"...\"> with the page passed as\nchildren (the walker contract from 287025e).\n\nRegression net:\n\n* BaselineRoutes.test.tsx (12 tests): structural pins on each Butler Labs\n  path''s wrapping + configKey + children identity, plus render-path tests\n  that mount the actual DataDrivenFlatRoutes under MockConfigApi and\n  confirm the disabled state through the new mounting produces the same\n  PluginNotEnabledPage UX as 0.4.0.\n* AppNormalization.test.tsx (2 tests, made load-bearing): visible FlatRoutes\n  wrapped in VisibleRenderRoutes function component so the DiscoveryAnchor\n  is the only walker-visible path; mutation that empties the anchor surfaces\n  as \"Routable extension was not discovered\".\n* DisabledStateParity.test.tsx (1 test): DynamicMenuSlot renders zero DOM\n  nodes when dynamicMenuItems is empty (chart 0.5.0 default state).\n\nMutation-proven: render-path gate removal, dependency mis-read via configKey\nswap, two-path divergence (anchor correct, render bypasses gate), and\nanchor-only entry removal each trip a specifically named test with the exact\nerror class (integrity/gate behavior or walker \"was not discovered\").\n\nThe 5 source files producing the user-visible Butler Labs UX\n(ButlerLabsRouteElement, ButlerLabsSubmenuItem, butlerLabsPluginsMeta,\nPluginNotEnabledPage, HomeNavigationCards) are bit-for-bit identical to\n0.4.0 (git diff exit=0 vs 90ccb1e). The mounting mechanism changed; the\ncomponents producing the UX did not.\n\n66 tests pass across 10 suites in packages/app. yarn tsc clean. yarn lint\nclean.\n\n* test(portal): Phase 5 boot-test harness against the published 0.5.0-rc image\n\nAdds the boot-test scripts and Playwright tests that close the Phase 3\nINFERRED enabled-render against the actual published image (rc.1\nbutler-portal + rc.2 butler-portal-plugin-installer), not local builds.\n\nscripts/phase-5-boot-test/run-installer-e2e.sh\n\n* Pushes a real fixture tarball to ghcr.io as an OCI artifact, computes\n  its sha512 SRI, then runs the published installer image against three\n  scenarios:\n   A. integrity matches -> install succeeds, audit logs structured\n   B. wrong sha512 + continueOnError=false (default) -> exit non-zero,\n      no plugin installed, audit log surfaces expected vs computed +\n      continueOnError_false fatal\n   C. wrong sha512 + continueOnError=true -> exit 0, rejected plugin\n      not installed, rejection logged (best-effort opt-in)\n* Mounts Docker auth via DOCKER_CONFIG env (operator path uses\n  ImagePullSecrets via the chart).\n* The Phase 4 bats tests at the unit layer pin the contracts; this\n  e2e proves they hold on the real image against a real GHCR pull\n  (the published-image gate the config.d.ts lesson called for).\n\nscripts/phase-5-boot-test/playwright/butler-labs-enabled-render.spec.ts\n\n* Closes Task #65 (Phase 3 INFERRED enabled-render verified on real\n  artifact). Boots the published portal with all four Butler Labs flags\n  on (Butler Labs deployment shape) plus a postgres sidecar; for each\n  plugin route navigates the headless browser there and asserts:\n   - URL matches the route (catches silent sign-in redirect)\n   - SignIn Guest tile is detached (catches vacuous-pass on the\n     sign-in fallback page, which Backstage renders at any URL when\n     auth fails)\n   - main element renders >50 chars (catches blank/error states)\n   - \"was not discovered\" error absent (the 287025e contract: the\n     DiscoveryAnchor indexed the routable extension via createApp''s\n     walker pass on the published image)\n   - PluginNotEnabledPage role string absent\n   - configKey chip absent\n* The disabled-state branch verifies the Phase 3 #6 guarantee on the\n  real image: with all four flags off, each route renders\n  PluginNotEnabledPage with the correct role string and the right\n  configKey chip.\n\nscripts/phase-5-boot-test/run-boot-test.sh\n\n* Driver script chaining the boot + installer e2e + Playwright tests.\n\nThe harness caught two real bugs the unit tests missed:\n\n1. lib/oci-pull.sh used `oras pull --quiet` which does not exist on\n   oras 1.2.0 (now fixed in installer 0.1.0-rc.2: --no-tty). The bats\n   fakebin accepted any flag; the strict-mode fakebin in installer\n   rc.2 rejects unknown flags.\n\n2. Backstage''s guest provider returns 403 outside development unless\n   `auth.providers.guest.dangerouslyAllowOutsideDevelopment=true`.\n   Test harness now sets this env var; deployments inherit production\n   auth providers from the chart.\n\n* fix(chart): isNull instead of notContains on absent volumes path (helm-unittest 0.5.2 CI pin)\n\nhelm-unittest 0.5.2 (the version pinned in .github/workflows/helm.yaml)\nerrors with \"unknown path spec.template.spec.volumes\" when notContains\nis asserted against a path that does not exist in the rendered template.\nhelm-unittest 1.x is lenient about absent paths; the Phase 2 local test\nruns were against 1.x and passed silently.\n\nIn the chart-default disabled state (no butlerSigning secret, no\ndynamicPlugins), the deployment template gates the entire spec.template.spec.volumes\nblock behind `or .butlerSigning .dynamicPlugins.enabled`; neither is\npresent in this test''s config, so the block does not render and the\npath is absent.\n\nThe intent of the test is \"no volume named dynamic-plugins appears in\nthe rendered pod template.\" An absent volumes section satisfies that\nas strongly as an empty one. isNull is the version-portable assertion\nfor absence: 0.5.2 + 1.x both accept it, and a future regression that\nadds any volume (dynamic-plugins or otherwise) when dynamicPlugins is\noff would trip this assertion the same way notContains would have.\n\nVerified locally with both helm-unittest 0.5.2 (CI pin) and 1.1.1\n(local default). 26 tests pass on both.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLff6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd7cQAEEu7f9iSscVTU2/2PzH0mKT\nogGCF+FiT6SiH/K+8gLl2M7kZrUYWHiQQN5FM68vdeSUXEcp+vqfe+gs1amjnM7+\ntdlzZ0Qz5dWatTajSSfVvXdzhnSVPfIVNBbNlncUr+PGo2W5C2XAMM/6+5H62eyc\n9juq5sRZU1hcnZY7eMMsvbMQof47tBUTRtC+AaTEm3+r+gvqbewmA28uk9yZEzSv\nLmERoOhbWfIS1ILn+PA6UEAaHrbxjxOIByHHJY5+hy8gUaGtHprnw7EN7hXifO6i\nJOSX9kzzwgT2RcigADQelZ5fuoR2IJSzrpzmOEOwS71m5VCgoVAo1zwX+JieDl9H\nme6Wf9ChAZmIz7vydj85Ifs0hLfWfltkn6y7H1daadQE8uNTUn12UBinREvXxv15\napr6VWkoiUUsl/I0jRU3PJqMc4q5cZncjrGYffnpb1drVeloIAF6FCwq+JkXgvg2\nEh2CLYaK/EUBIVnN7I2ZgIXFO+kyweHQPStI9a4jDy4oZ4rM5+ri0Ym5BunXjd5L\nOot9We5QhIBpiaMXs+E3RIE4LApsNjSeQZhTozcUyVUQeTnY5wsrmRTsS88lpobX\nDUMCvc46Pm1h0Sqt8bgQk/HVP8viWvE1cKcbRf6oPPtzSXJOs7jZyNMHrJF5zpYz\nEXDNd22gaIUIyKVDa4CJ\n=dmyp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-14T00:38:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDk4NTA3ZGQ5OWIyZWI1MDI5YzMzZDJjNzEwZDc1M2Q5ZGEyOWQ2MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede","sha":"c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede"}],"sha":"98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/98507dd99b2eb5029c33d2c710d753d9da29d600"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T13:12:30Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T13:12:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(portal): ship packages/app/config.d.ts in backend image (#21)\n\nThe post-PR-#20 image crashlooped at backend boot with\n\n  Error: Invalid schema in packages/app/config.d.ts, missing Config export\n  File ''packages/app/config.d.ts'' not found.\n    at compileTsSchemas\n    at collectConfigSchemas\n    at loadConfigSchema\n    at createConfigSecretEnumerator\n    at #doStart (BackendInitializer)\n\nRoot cause: PR #20 added packages/app/config.d.ts (new source file) and\ndeclared configSchema: \"config.d.ts\" in packages/app/package.json so the\nfour plugins.<name>.enabled keys could carry the @visibility frontend\nannotation. Backstage''s config-loader walks every workspace package''s\nconfigSchema declaration at backend init via the same loadConfigSchema\nfunction used at build time (loadCliConfig). For paths ending in .d.ts\nthe loader tries to compile from source at the file''s package-relative\nlocation.\n\nThe backend bundle ships packages/app/dist/.config-schema.json\n(the pre-compiled artifact written by bundle.cjs.js as build OUTPUT)\nbut the Dockerfile only COPY''s the bundle + skeleton, not the raw\nconfig.d.ts source. createConfigSecretEnumerator fails before any\nplugin loader runs, regardless of chart''s APP_CONFIG_plugins_*_enabled\nenv vars.\n\nWhy repointing configSchema at dist/.config-schema.json (option A) was\nrejected: same loadConfigSchema runs at build time and writes that JSON\nas output. Repointing the field at it makes the build-time read target\nits own future output. Clean build fails; subsequent builds read stale.\n\nFix: one COPY in the Dockerfile that lands config.d.ts at\n/app/packages/app/config.d.ts where the loader resolves it. tsc and\ntypescript are both present in the prod image, so runtime compile\nworks.\n\nVerified locally by rebuilding the image and boot-testing it:\n- /healthcheck = 200 at t = 20s\n- \"Found 1 new secrets in config that will be redacted\" log line\n  prints (createConfigSecretEnumerator succeeded; this is the exact\n  line the broken image crashed BEFORE printing)\n- 11 plugins initialize: app, proxy, scaffolder, techdocs, auth,\n  catalog, permission, search, kubernetes, notifications, signals\n- All four plugins.<name>.enabled keys reach the HTML config bundle\n  serialized for the browser, confirming @visibility frontend flows\n  through the schema pipeline end-to-end\n\nCaught in production immediately after the PR #20 image rolled out via\nbutler-portal-live''s ImageUpdateAutomation. The old pre-#20 pod kept\nserving via Flux''s helm rollback to v19, so the live portal was\ndegraded (rollout stuck on retry loop) but not blanked. PR B on\nbutler-portal-live (chart 0.4.0 + all-four enables) is held until this\nfix lands and the new image is verified booting through CI publish.","tree":{"sha":"30c22216c7037ffe2cb60f3461e45e58af466c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/30c22216c7037ffe2cb60f3461e45e58af466c93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede","verification":{"payload":"tree 30c22216c7037ffe2cb60f3461e45e58af466c93\nparent 90ccb1e2882228d583e1d5d9df39f8b7b0bd4c7f\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1781269950 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781269950 -0500\n\nfix(portal): ship packages/app/config.d.ts in backend image (#21)\n\nThe post-PR-#20 image crashlooped at backend boot with\n\n  Error: Invalid schema in packages/app/config.d.ts, missing Config export\n  File ''packages/app/config.d.ts'' not found.\n    at compileTsSchemas\n    at collectConfigSchemas\n    at loadConfigSchema\n    at createConfigSecretEnumerator\n    at #doStart (BackendInitializer)\n\nRoot cause: PR #20 added packages/app/config.d.ts (new source file) and\ndeclared configSchema: \"config.d.ts\" in packages/app/package.json so the\nfour plugins.<name>.enabled keys could carry the @visibility frontend\nannotation. Backstage''s config-loader walks every workspace package''s\nconfigSchema declaration at backend init via the same loadConfigSchema\nfunction used at build time (loadCliConfig). For paths ending in .d.ts\nthe loader tries to compile from source at the file''s package-relative\nlocation.\n\nThe backend bundle ships packages/app/dist/.config-schema.json\n(the pre-compiled artifact written by bundle.cjs.js as build OUTPUT)\nbut the Dockerfile only COPY''s the bundle + skeleton, not the raw\nconfig.d.ts source. createConfigSecretEnumerator fails before any\nplugin loader runs, regardless of chart''s APP_CONFIG_plugins_*_enabled\nenv vars.\n\nWhy repointing configSchema at dist/.config-schema.json (option A) was\nrejected: same loadConfigSchema runs at build time and writes that JSON\nas output. Repointing the field at it makes the build-time read target\nits own future output. Clean build fails; subsequent builds read stale.\n\nFix: one COPY in the Dockerfile that lands config.d.ts at\n/app/packages/app/config.d.ts where the loader resolves it. tsc and\ntypescript are both present in the prod image, so runtime compile\nworks.\n\nVerified locally by rebuilding the image and boot-testing it:\n- /healthcheck = 200 at t = 20s\n- \"Found 1 new secrets in config that will be redacted\" log line\n  prints (createConfigSecretEnumerator succeeded; this is the exact\n  line the broken image crashed BEFORE printing)\n- 11 plugins initialize: app, proxy, scaffolder, techdocs, auth,\n  catalog, permission, search, kubernetes, notifications, signals\n- All four plugins.<name>.enabled keys reach the HTML config bundle\n  serialized for the browser, confirming @visibility frontend flows\n  through the schema pipeline end-to-end\n\nCaught in production immediately after the PR #20 image rolled out via\nbutler-portal-live''s ImageUpdateAutomation. The old pre-#20 pod kept\nserving via Flux''s helm rollback to v19, so the live portal was\ndegraded (rollout stuck on retry loop) but not blanked. PR B on\nbutler-portal-live (chart 0.4.0 + all-four enables) is held until this\nfix lands and the new image is verified booting through CI publish.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLAW+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgLEQAGlYk+tp18vi/bmHiMYuEodv\nxZXNwOPmFGDhL045O4t7zjJswusdB/a379ROTFDnv0GGS5TpVQS4eodaio/OpIuw\nRYxjaeziaauQ5bdjpySox/eMzzkX8Ec0YEX8siLgcOmhrGSGCw+RV0EsGfOQ5Jz7\nspkmENObfV14kgdYdKvQ5vzDUobN1ymrHs570l4aqmGQuNRqzvvpFdgkBaM4GB3K\nWjbJq/FG15nduCfbHTzDOnLm+z21SnuCMauWtsgo0I+48/I11d1NQ5NaaUTOph5s\nRoJ+DQ1tOAWtO9uDHjcQhPPXQfodk8F+ozdEh9yOxSurbOw79KhLDZFv/R5IxlM8\nbaEUKGfXhx9uKxUcGldCG7BFVU1JfA03gi53s5r/jibKGUECpz8H8A/syodRKsE7\nsQpURsMAdvlOyRttNr06DZkdyp7yX0ZCZlh1BDoW2wP6LRE/PXTOFyRNvFaqpwCl\n3rG1Lbbj+xh6V0ruIM3SbWCOFqwSYlRLxvNmYEZ9YolDxrzQW4CkelTdpnH1hHHx\nqMO4t3mp7YFMG/v0fJPgLzFBn7Sn333uhbQ7Qh/MpCyp1LZE9yo9xe7465RbKHtw\neQv8YII30QixYSKr11GtECJs8C8ah8VtHV17uDth4AdDoZ9U0iycTPWxH3zzOPsN\nrF+kldS9AhmtOV+XH+5V\n=uMj3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T13:12:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKGM4Nzk4ODUyOGY4YWNmMjhiODA2MjA0ZDk5NTkxZmE3MGY2ZGNlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/90ccb1e2882228d583e1d5d9df39f8b7b0bd4c7f","sha":"90ccb1e2882228d583e1d5d9df39f8b7b0bd4c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/90ccb1e2882228d583e1d5d9df39f8b7b0bd4c7f"}],"sha":"c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/c87988528f8acf28b806204d99591fa70f6dcede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/90ccb1e2882228d583e1d5d9df39f8b7b0bd4c7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:15:44Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:15:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(portal): runtime per-plugin gates for Butler-Labs-branded plugins (#20)\n\nIntroduces runtime gates so external customer deployments default to OFF\nfor all four Butler-Labs-branded plugins (Butler / Chambers / Keeper /\nHerald) and Butler Labs'' own HelmRelease overrides them to true.\n\nBackend stays genuine-off: createBackendFeatureLoader yields features\nonly when the flag is true, so /api/<plugin>/* routes are 404 (not 401,\nnot a sham handler). Catalog entity provider for Keeper piggy-backs on\nplugins.registry.enabled.\n\nFrontend is discoverable-but-disabled: routes always mount, the route\nelement renders a branded PluginNotEnabledPage (themed role + origin\ncopy + mascot hero) when the flag is off, the sidebar item is greyed\nwith a brand-card tooltip naming plugins.<key>.enabled, and the\nhomepage card is similarly greyed with the Origin lore badge.\n\nChambers depends on Butler at runtime (it proxies every backend call\nthrough butler-backend). The route element, sidebar, and homepage card\nall consume getButlerLabsPluginRuntimeState and render the dependency-\nmissing variant of PluginNotEnabledPage when workspaces=true with\nbutler=false -- the operator sees the misconfiguration before clicking,\nnot as a trickle of broken API toasts.\n\nChart 0.4.0 changes: per-plugin gate env vars under APP_CONFIG_plugins_\n*_enabled with default-false safety so partial overrides do not crash\nthe backend; butlerAuth.existingSecret gated on plugins.butler.enabled;\nmascot assets shipped as WebP (95-97% size reduction).\n\nTests pin all three regression classes: gate logic (12 tests across 4\nsuites), routable-extension discovery (AppDiscovery.test.tsx with\nmountedRoutes omitted so the walker is the source of truth), and\nconfigSchema visibility annotations. helm-unittest suite runs from CI\nwith the new fail-guard cases (defaults-render-OK + butler-on-requires-\nsecret + butler-on-with-secret-renders-OK).\n\nSix commits squashed: 31543cc, 8004764, 734c094, 01ea6c1, 51a0057,\nc5a80cc, 7fe78fb, 287025e, cf9bb73, 603d169.","tree":{"sha":"e8826eca4a53827f82b452d78e720b02c0eebb89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/e8826eca4a53827f82b452d78e720b02c0eebb89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/90ccb1e2882228d583e1d5d9df39f8b7b0bd4c7f","verification":{"payload":"tree e8826eca4a53827f82b452d78e720b02c0eebb89\nparent 6c6be1b594795c265365131009816aeaac28d4b0\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1781234144 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781234144 -0500\n\nfeat(portal): runtime per-plugin gates for Butler-Labs-branded plugins (#20)\n\nIntroduces runtime gates so external customer deployments default to OFF\nfor all four Butler-Labs-branded plugins (Butler / Chambers / Keeper /\nHerald) and Butler Labs'' own HelmRelease overrides them to true.\n\nBackend stays genuine-off: createBackendFeatureLoader yields features\nonly when the flag is true, so /api/<plugin>/* routes are 404 (not 401,\nnot a sham handler). Catalog entity provider for Keeper piggy-backs on\nplugins.registry.enabled.\n\nFrontend is discoverable-but-disabled: routes always mount, the route\nelement renders a branded PluginNotEnabledPage (themed role + origin\ncopy + mascot hero) when the flag is off, the sidebar item is greyed\nwith a brand-card tooltip naming plugins.<key>.enabled, and the\nhomepage card is similarly greyed with the Origin lore badge.\n\nChambers depends on Butler at runtime (it proxies every backend call\nthrough butler-backend). The route element, sidebar, and homepage card\nall consume getButlerLabsPluginRuntimeState and render the dependency-\nmissing variant of PluginNotEnabledPage when workspaces=true with\nbutler=false -- the operator sees the misconfiguration before clicking,\nnot as a trickle of broken API toasts.\n\nChart 0.4.0 changes: per-plugin gate env vars under APP_CONFIG_plugins_\n*_enabled with default-false safety so partial overrides do not crash\nthe backend; butlerAuth.existingSecret gated on plugins.butler.enabled;\nmascot assets shipped as WebP (95-97% size reduction).\n\nTests pin all three regression classes: gate logic (12 tests across 4\nsuites), routable-extension discovery (AppDiscovery.test.tsx with\nmountedRoutes omitted so the walker is the source of truth), and\nconfigSchema visibility annotations. helm-unittest suite runs from CI\nwith the new fail-guard cases (defaults-render-OK + butler-on-requires-\nsecret + butler-on-with-secret-renders-OK).\n\nSix commits squashed: 31543cc, 8004764, 734c094, 01ea6c1, 51a0057,\nc5a80cc, 7fe78fb, 287025e, cf9bb73, 603d169.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK3ngCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa44QAKWJC7I4IgEoLLFuOqLfD4GW\nrL2Ai6Sxqcb9k+k9VugC0E+QHuZzBQMtlxaPhdhnuXah1jHkj0tNQdt5ewEIuGII\nCqazgg3A3VVQp8BxTqfWpOKyzqpxDlXPwaeZ4VDsaClo63X3ZBaZWdhPsGTpo3YS\ntmw6V/zm6gkyG7OUf6JNslf1cuXT15raF/9wg+RB5QjNC/6VkfwFwbLBI/eLv/6V\nFlbCZUQj325Qsr3qPzXl75oNtgoUBKEOhapsVSm1pkJ5xDEQuDTZwecPEBStzP4Y\no2seTURts1lY3cdAxsGmQMgTw48bEZ7XdcZ6FE8UDvrMFdNBn27CxtCotmCmV4Xl\n6ImN37PRnxxUdh4ANmHVt+cu3NGhMbpCYMRNgvXL/5KllBIXAdybUUGfyVHILML3\nre5n23kHIp03p/uTTdYFhKqqkfN4w2wx6oMTBOFMaGEq/W8LxjymPStr+u82Ov42\nEzfpM/dyaKxnVWNaYrh4O9wULQlIFRwYanX4k9GkqQ27KspZ+ba5RIHAZW8XPT2F\nC0fTncZrsbxJtHFCuAP6NwhENr7zAaacfKZAaM1wCmXVUTqr8fl6iK3LfdKw68LW\nKcgnJXxImvUpePZ1WRpw4ijJ+n0X3bu9v40ReyubQB6miY4PjKHx+ihP3JQczGci\nSj3PxnWHIRHi1c5ld+Cy\n=fpzo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T03:15:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","foll