ving to butler-labs-ops.","tree":{"sha":"7cdc2b01d74444d93e1ccf9fe7d5dc614c258b75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/7cdc2b01d74444d93e1ccf9fe7d5dc614c258b75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/09bf93cc1f1b17de9bd4f9cdac5b22fe39b72b19","verification":{"payload":"tree 7cdc2b01d74444d93e1ccf9fe7d5dc614c258b75\nparent 42cb1d122ef8d881d62cd9dca734e340c3aa5f36\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1771977929 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771977929 -0600\n\nfeat: apply butler household naming taxonomy (#6)\n\n* feat: apply butler household naming taxonomy to portal products\n\nRename sub-products using British estate household tradition:\n- Workspaces → Chambers (chamberlain''s private rooms)\n- Registry → Keeper (Keeper of the Wardrobe — governed stores)\n- Pipelines → Herald (estate messenger — signal routing)\n\nUpdates sidebar submenu labels, home page navigation cards,\ndescriptions, and typewriter search prompts. Routes unchanged.\n\nAdds docs/product-naming.md as canonical naming reference with\ncharacter profiles and UI copy guidelines for all products.\n\n* chore: remove product naming doc from portal repo\n\nNaming taxonomy is a cross-ecosystem brand reference, not\nportal-specific. Moving to butler-labs-ops.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpnjzJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3GMQAIt5nmM2RvSlIL2/62NYzVXE\nFlRdFSXO36kcQD+poytERdPsBQNjiDtu6ZIX5PbGl1aU0ejiB1DPtiIRg8sb0Mmy\nINJUOZQSawkSin9FbgKwlux72LKmfYPRKATeQYJ2F1NFTg0+LfGDQqklCv36tQno\nxRXTzgWDHHnEtvAl25CaQbWJpoEk2yPnBfEFDH9Z6SR3zLsJk1L7aDUVPSlZOvYJ\neoDMeVVVoEH6TCQM9Um3Oj88e0j7CirhDoqwSLAd3N4nJ++xneytRVygIFMkT4F5\nLszPqTZH0qOhEUxywePn+BEC1IOcwUYKS+pBVUAd4e3rXu+4vVlomHgxcV/kM8N7\n2Zg50ojyrICkhNYEnDPRX48d00fGi4t6lELJmhP+jSx8FKFXB76QRzlyuqq+lXvf\nonqioS/oIqrnVEzdfTqYgWzz7SjQwJOnlkeywappome0URaRpXXk+7LXqQXUqhFg\nivG3sKhmiWWnXl+3PmlAVBZPM8squXQ88rXcwFjbBLEvQu5VUzbPem2NS