:"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/42cb1d122ef8d881d62cd9dca734e340c3aa5f36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-24T22:11:54Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-24T22:11:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: complete Butler Portal theme refactor with brand identity (#5)\n\nRefactor the portal theme system to support dark/light modes and\ncolorblind accessibility (deuteranopia, protanopia, tritanopia) with\n8 theme variants selectable from Settings.\n\nTheme system:\n- Factory-based theme creation with brand colors and surface palettes\n- Custom appearance settings card with theme mode and color vision toggles\n- Kill Backstage wave headers, replace with flat branded design\n- Global component overrides for cards, inputs, tables, dialogs, tabs\n- Themed submenu popup backgrounds via navigation palette\n\nSidebar:\n- New Butler Portal logo (bpnowords.svg) with theme-aware text\n- Butler Labs submenu with brand-colored icons for all products\n- Catalog submenu with brand-colored icons\n- External links: Butler Labs site, Docs, GitHub, Discord\n- Updated favicons from new logo\n\nHome page:\n- Animated gradient border shimmer on search bar\n- Typewriter placeholder cycling through Butler-relevant prompts\n- Unified brand-colored card icons (theme-aware)\n- Responsive grid breakpoints for narrow screens\n\nPlugin updates:\n- Replace hardcoded purple/teal admin banners with theme-aware opacity\n- Use theme palette values throughout butler, registry, pipeline plugins","tree":{"sha":"81c9f939482d561440926bf16415218fbb22f860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/81c9f939482d561440926bf16415218fbb22f860"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/42cb1d122ef8d881d62cd9dca734e340c3aa5f36","verification":{"payload":"tree 81c9f939482d561440926bf16415218fbb22f860\nparent 3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1771971114 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771971114 -0600\n\nfeat: complete Butler Portal theme refactor with brand identity (#5)\n\nRefactor the portal theme system to support dark/light modes and\ncolorblind accessibility (deuteranopia, protanopia, tritanopia) with\n8 theme variants selectable from Settings.\n\nTheme system:\n- Factory-based theme creation with brand colors and surface palettes\n- Custom appearance settings card with theme mode and color vision toggles\n- Kill Backstage wave headers, replace with flat branded design\n- Global component overrides for cards, inputs, tables, dialogs, tabs\n- Themed submenu popup backgrounds via navigation palette\n\nSidebar:\n- New Butler Portal logo (bpnowords.svg) with theme-aware text\n- Butler Labs submenu with brand-colored icons for all products\n- Catalog submenu with brand-colored icons\n- External links: Butler Labs site, Docs, GitHub, Discord\n- Updated favicons from new logo\n\nHome page:\n- Animated gradient border shimmer on search bar\n- Typewriter placeholder cycling through Butler-relevant prompts\n- Unified brand-colored card icons (theme-aware)\n- Responsive grid breakpoints for narrow screens\n\nPlugin updates:\n- Replace hardcoded purple/teal admin banners with theme-aware opacity\n- Use theme palette values throughout butler, registry, pipeline plugins","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpniIqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9swQAHR3NIaIeCiao1/iSNB9Zyxj\n9kuZycsx3/ANQJSI9TBawbFiabTLPoG4/U4RC8ErYpJYT39PZgNkK34sTE155laz\nzBTQ9O9Fjwi7MCBl9jovPa15dsF70ezzXGinZ3StkXbcOna+4VlTNstd7b7qGXyu\nNabdSMLW8/g0qRIeZ6eMSwWatjXMpS3B9YvgBQZnHiyZm5ap2f8ObXhfMlw8UTP6\nZ2C2FxwJ+8BwRqrGehXanKu3NdWONIS47DQNBOyxEObpF0r7kUKGVbI66ey+mfNg\nbIayPis7QASWKAq4wR+ScMpjUoNQM+gtN1KXYqWQux/VFvz5cACPD4ZWHwOWB8tG\nU0flQvcZ/1l1KnFzRaSCMnQBoFnIZuiRcySL68aHV1zv6Je2In/ir4nk50TD87gA\nw6DW3bm+VZyGlDkwdwEhqUlzjvr5dSvesDR+iEHEljXduM+DTOAvISP7QshUmwvf\n5xqXfkYydFauc4pi9bSZBKmeOtxDxKMMjGoVGbIHZVC3xRgCpsBZ3iX8Dh9DYIfS\ny4+FojVhSroD7B/3+WNc+TyiUxVh9E7Nejxh+FVogBAF4AOeZAS6R+PZpWLI8XTf\n5lGDrpd6EpJYdtgDV+vJlr6YQ4uL4CAzW9e0mXi73ZAbf2ZE3J5EGhNWMXpVKvs5\n1lWLUvdQNGh8KbxGQDbv\n=4V/0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-24T22:11:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/42cb1d122ef8d881d62cd9dca734e340c3aa5f36","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDQyY2IxZDEyMmVmOGQ4ODFkNjJjZDlkY2E3MzRlMzQwYzNhYTVmMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99","sha":"3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99"}],"sha":"42cb1d122ef8d881d62cd9dca734e340c3aa5f36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/42cb1d122ef8d881d62cd9dca734e340c3aa5f36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-23T02:35:06Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-23T02:35:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add pipeline plugin with fleet management and config deployment (#4)\n\nAdd a new Backstage plugin for building, validating, and deploying\nVector observability pipelines to fleet agents.\n\nBackend (pipeline-backend):\n- Pipeline CRUD with versioned DAGs and deterministic config compilation\n- Fleet agent management: registration, heartbeat, config delivery via ETag\n- Fleet tokens with scoped authentication for agent-to-server communication\n- Agent groups with label-based matching and merged config delivery\n- Managed configs for per-agent and per-group Vector configuration\n- Deployment tracking with collision detection across overlapping agents\n- Pipeline-agent linking for targeted deployments\n- Component schema registry (sources, transforms, sinks)\n- Import from existing Vector YAML with auto-discovery\n- VRL playground with Vector binary execution (graceful degradation)\n- Structural DAG validation (server-side, no Vector binary required)\n- Agent-side validation: agents run vector validate locally and report\n  results via heartbeat (applied/rejected/unchanged with error details)\n\nFrontend (pipeline):\n- Visual pipeline builder with drag-and-drop DAG editor (ReactFlow)\n- Collapsible component library organized by category\n- Component configuration panel with schema-driven forms\n- Live YAML preview with deterministic compilation\n- Validate button (structural) on pipeline builder, agent, and group editors\n- Deploy dialog showing target agents and online status\n- Fleet management: agent list, agent detail with config editor\n- Group management: create/edit groups with label selectors\n- Token management for fleet agent authentication\n- Deployment history with per-agent sync status\n- Version history with diff view\n- VRL editor with syntax highlighting and completions\n- Pipeline preview with sample event transformation\n- Team-scoped navigation with team picker\n\nCommon (pipeline-common):\n- Permission definitions for pipeline RBAC\n- Role hierarchy (viewer, operator, admin)","tree":{"sha":"19197954ad8788394da3bb8659a48b9f1c51816a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/19197954ad8788394da3bb8659a48b9f1c51816a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99","verification":{"payload":"tree 19197954ad8788394da3bb8659a48b9f1c51816a\nparent aa99339368b6603719aff0057926e5b7d13b2024\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1771814106 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771814106 -0600\n\nfeat: add pipeline plugin with fleet management and config deployment (#4)\n\nAdd a new Backstage plugin for building, validating, and deploying\nVector observability pipelines to fleet agents.\n\nBackend (pipeline-backend):\n- Pipeline CRUD with versioned DAGs and deterministic config compilation\n- Fleet agent management: registration, heartbeat, config delivery via ETag\n- Fleet tokens with scoped authentication for agent-to-server communication\n- Agent groups with label-based matching and merged config delivery\n- Managed configs for per-agent and per-group Vector configuration\n- Deployment tracking with collision detection across overlapping agents\n- Pipeline-agent linking for targeted deployments\n- Component schema registry (sources, transforms, sinks)\n- Import from existing Vector YAML with auto-discovery\n- VRL playground with Vector binary execution (graceful degradation)\n- Structural DAG validation (server-side, no Vector binary required)\n- Agent-side validation: agents run vector validate locally and report\n  results via heartbeat (applied/rejected/unchanged with error details)\n\nFrontend (pipeline):\n- Visual pipeline builder with drag-and-drop DAG editor (ReactFlow)\n- Collapsible component library organized by category\n- Component configuration panel with schema-driven forms\n- Live YAML preview with deterministic compilation\n- Validate button (structural) on pipeline builder, agent, and group editors\n- Deploy dialog showing target agents and online status\n- Fleet management: agent list, agent detail with config editor\n- Group management: create/edit groups with label selectors\n- Token management for fleet agent authentication\n- Deployment history with per-agent sync status\n- Version history with diff view\n- VRL editor with syntax highlighting and completions\n- Pipeline preview with sample event transformation\n- Team-scoped navigation with team picker\n\nCommon (pipeline-common):\n- Permission definitions for pipeline RBAC\n- Role hierarchy (viewer, operator, admin)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpm7zaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5p8QADXr3wgTz3iNzv/cm2BRSe0h\ngNA/pQoB7+09YE9rMHf7wc0HverPTbmfC5IGZaIxA0EY3qVWjh618UJR9/EOYO9S\no3s6ca2XSEev+BBs2EG4Vb1LnU2UjO0/W0Xh/AExXO7rOkXDkcouPb8VL+U6LG6m\nHvx0Sjq2ycc9BzYKm8mLTBUibo46ehG6Vux9FRydmBEt6mOPiH18FnWar2F/khbk\n1m5r2KEKZhoMTNyubKTDFgiwCCAGW2cwMEsfx0R6bm4+wq+32nInuIFwJcaFP3MG\n6el+K1fiw6FJmERgq+FN4rEx3gewdua4N+tbfWW1KO+CDw2PNAkx+q50Dk+1v+MV\nbGiJOSOOQ/DSruO4OGTP4z3q/+I6bg1stRXqjwgq/92YBLwXpcz9fwE/qE5xQ5UV\nYHfLx1m5HWQUFXqVlvlNW9hISJlJqg4yfcvi+mG9rAduy/H75bVDG3J3ex35v0jF\ncT4c8BJ3kjuNrZlMHqWL3Qpm8yEr3GysSug1GI/OBEgJKvbA8ydf9V7MWyMgYv+N\nmLDGPc1KGN1OHNNp8oQ0Qbzxg5wdkdJoTyYWXHoM5U+KcQWmlhoulpkN1gBXaNxU\n7tqQOcYKvNhNO1/LKTf9SzcFiINZ4SZHY44amBG3DMq8EsQI5Mb2a6Fmpf0x/PJj\nNSBr9s0gPULEWxamsr1N\n=2DfS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-23T02:35:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99","node_id":"C_kwDORPLoK9oAKDNlZmQzNmI4NTFjZWZjYWQxZjY3MDNmY2UzYWY2ZGYyYmI0MWZlOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commit/aa99339368b6603719aff0057926e5b7d13b2024","sha":"aa99339368b6603719aff0057926e5b7d13b2024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/aa99339368b6603719aff0057926e5b7d13b2024"}],"sha":"3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/3efd36b851cefcad1f6703fce3af6df2bb41fe99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46534421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/atbagan","id":46534421,"login":"atbagan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTM0NDIx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atbagan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/commits/aa99339368b6603719aff0057926e5b7d13b2024/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-23T02:35:04Z","email":"46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"atbagan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-23T02:35:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(registry): projects, cloud integrations, and PeaaS execution (#3)\n\n* feat: include cloud integration env vars in runner config endpoint\n\nAdd envVars field to the /config response so butler-runner can set\ncloud provider credentials (GOOGLE_PROJECT, AWS_REGION, etc.) and\nvariable set entries as environment variables before running terraform.\n\n* feat: include cloud integration OIDC details in dispatch payload\n\nResolve GCP/AWS OIDC cloud integrations and include provider details\n(workload identity provider, service account, role ARN) in the\nrepository_dispatch client_payload so the GitHub Actions workflow\ncan run provider-specific auth steps before the runner container.\n\n* feat(registry): add copy-all button to RunLogViewer\n\nAdds a toolbar with a copy icon that copies all log lines (ANSI\nstripped) to the clipboard. Shows a brief \"Copied!\" confirmation.\n\n* feat(registry): add SeaweedFS S3 state backend for PeaaS runs\n\nWhen a PeaaS module run has no explicit state backend configured,\nauto-generate an S3 backend pointing at the platform-managed SeaweedFS\ninstance. State key is namespaced per environment/module. Config is\nread from registry.iac.peaas.stateBackend in app-config.\n\n* fix(registry): provide dummy S3 credentials for unauthenticated SeaweedFS\n\nTerraform S3 backend requires credentials even when the store has no\nauth. Provide ''unused'' dummy values when no real keys are configured.\n\n* feat(registry): UI fixes - back nav, clickable env runs, state backend config\n\n- Fix back navigation to use browser history (navigate(-1)) in\n  EnvironmentDetail, ModuleDetail, ModuleRunDetail\n- Rename \"Plan All\" button to \"Run Actions\"\n- Create EnvironmentRunDetail page with module runs table, progress,\n  confirm/cancel actions\n- Make environment run rows clickable in EnvironmentDetail\n- Add StateBackendForm component for BYOC backend configuration\n- Show \"managed by Butler Labs\" message for PeaaS modules\n- Add route for /environments/:envId/runs/:runId\n\n* feat(registry): add projects, cloud integrations, and UI improvements\n\n- Add projects feature: migration, routes, types, CRUD components\n- Add cloud integration wizard with OIDC configuration\n- Add CreateEnvironmentInProject component for scoped env creation\n- Refactor environment and module routes for cleaner team-scoped queries\n- Improve state backend configuration form with provider-specific fields\n- Restyle MuiTabs/MuiTab for consistent dark theme across plugins\n- Update permissions, API client, and type definitions","tree":{"sha":"40ed33ebc9120c89a042f5e3e1cfc0c3d5a8d010","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/trees/40ed33ebc9120c89a042f5e3e1cfc0c3d5a8d010"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/butlerdotdev/butler-portal/git/commits/aa99339368b6603719aff0057926e5b7d13b2024","verification":{"payload":"tree 40ed33ebc9120c89a042f5e3e1cfc0c3d5a8d010\nparent a5fc33accf1f9344a028ac550ec5a1580da5f3d3\nauthor atbagan <46534421+atbagan@users.noreply.github.com> 1771814104 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771814104 -0600\n\nfeat(registry): projects, cloud integrations, and PeaaS execution (#3)\n\n* feat: include cloud integration env vars in runner config endpoint\n\nAdd envVars field to the /config response so butler-runner can set\ncloud provider credentials (GOOGLE_PROJECT, AWS_REGION, etc.) and\nvariable set entries as environment variables before running terraform.\n\n* feat: include cloud integration OIDC details in dispatch payload\n\nResolve GCP/AWS OIDC cloud integrations and include provider details\n(workload identity provider, service account, role ARN) in the\nrepository_dispatch client_payload so the GitHub Actions workflow\ncan run provider-specific auth steps before the runner container.\n\n* feat(registry): add copy-all button to RunLogViewer\n\nAdds a toolbar with a copy icon that copies all log lines (ANSI\nstripped) to the clipboard. Shows a brief \"Copied!\" confirmation.\n\n* feat(registry): add SeaweedFS S3 state backend for PeaaS runs\n\nWhen a PeaaS module run has no explicit state backend configured,\nauto-generate an S3 backend pointing at the platform-managed SeaweedFS\ninstance. State key is namespaced per environment/module. Config is\nread from registry.iac.peaas.stateBackend in app-config.\n\n* fix(registry): provide dummy S3 credentials for unauthenticated SeaweedFS\n\nTerraform S3 backend requires credentials even when the store has no\nauth. Provide ''unused'' dummy values when no real keys are configured.\n\n* feat(registry): UI fixes - back nav, clickable env runs, state backend config\n\n- Fix back navigation to use browser history (navigate(-1)) in\n  EnvironmentDetail, ModuleDetail, ModuleRunDetail\n- Rename \"Plan All\" button to \"Run Actions\"\n- Create EnvironmentRunDetail page with module runs table, progress,\n  confirm/cancel actions\n- Make environment run rows clickable in EnvironmentDetail\n- Add StateBackendForm component for BYOC backend configuration\n- Show \"managed by Butler Labs\" message for PeaaS modules\n- Add route for /environments/:envId/runs/:runId\n\n* feat(registry): add projects, cloud integrations, and UI improvements\n\n- Add projects feature: migration, routes, types, CRUD components\n- Add cloud integration wizard with OIDC configuration\n- Add CreateEnvironmentInProject component for scoped env creation\n- Refactor environment and module routes for cleaner team-scoped queries\n- Improve state backend configuration form with provider-specific fie