d7849d730cfa396","node_id":"C_kwDORQKVF9oAKDUxN2Y4ODQ3NWU4NzJmNGNkZTdkZDU2OTVkNzg0OWQ3MzBjZmEzOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platform-mesh/contrib-generic-resource-ui/commit/9f41e443c0be27c1fe03900633c9ae1d6627ef7a","sha":"9f41e443c0be27c1fe03900633c9ae1d6627ef7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/contrib-generic-resource-ui/commits/9f41e443c0be27c1fe03900633c9ae1d6627ef7a"}],"sha":"517f88475e872f4cde7dd5695d7849d730cfa396","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/contrib-generic-resource-ui/commits/517f88475e872f4cde7dd5695d7849d730cfa396"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7794387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/contrib-generic-resource-ui/commits/9f41e443c0be27c1fe03900633c9ae1d6627ef7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T09:25:17Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T09:25:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): resolve npm audit vulnerabilities via Angular 21 upgrade (#92)\n\nClears all 51 npm audit findings (1 critical, 37 high, 12 moderate, 1 low).\nThe high/moderate bulk came from `@angular/*` framework advisories plus the\n`vite`/`esbuild`/`piscina`/`undici` build-tooling chain, none of which had a\nfix within the 19.2.x line — the fix required moving off Angular 19.\n\nSince `@ngrx` and `@fundamental-ngx` do not yet support Angular 22, the\ncommon compatible target is Angular 21:\n\n- Angular 19 -> 21 via `ng update` (framework + `@angular/build`/`cli`),\n  including the bootstrap-options -> providers migration in main.ts.\n- Ecosystem bumped to Angular-21-compatible majors: `@ngrx/*` 21.1.1,\n  `@fundamental-ngx/*` 0.63.0 (+ fundamental-styles 0.41.7 /\n  theming-base-content ^11.36), `@luigi-project/client-support-angular`\n  21.1.0, `apollo-angular` 13, `@apollo/client` 4, `@angular/cdk` 21.\n- Test tooling bumped for Angular 21 / jest 30: `jest` 30, `@types/jest` 30,\n  `jest-preset-angular` 17, `jest-junit` 17, `jest-mock-extended` 4,\n  `ng-mocks` 14.17, plus `jest-environment-jsdom` 30 (no longer bundled).\n\nApollo Client v3 -> v4 code migration (non-generic `ApolloClientOptions`,\n`HttpHeaders` context, `result.data` now possibly-undefined) applied to the\nresource/dashboard/schema services.\n\n`npm audit` reports 0 vulnerabilities; `ng build` and the full jest suite\n(237 tests) pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"bff9dfd7726c87602517ce00f5d4a5b6a7bfe358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/contrib-generic-resource-ui/git/trees/bff9dfd7726c87602517ce00f5d4a5b6a7bfe358"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/contrib-generic-resource-ui/git/commits/9f41e443c0be27c1fe03900633c9ae1d6627ef7a","verification":{"payload":"tree bff9dfd7726c87602517ce00f5d4a5b6a7bfe358\nparent 566fba0823f512ad5565952b792917fdf9bc5b81\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1786613117 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786613117 +0200\n\nfix(deps): resolve npm audit vulnerabilities via Angular 21 upgrade (#92)\n\nClears all 51 npm audit findings (1 critical, 37 high, 12 moderate, 1 low).\nThe high/moderate bulk came from `@angular/*` framework advisories plus the\n`vite`/`esbuild`/`piscina`/`undici` build-tooling chain, none of which had a\nfix within the 19.2.x line — the fix required moving off Angular 19.\n\nSince `@ngrx` and `@fundamental-ngx` do not yet support Angular 22, the\ncommon compatible target is Angular 21:\n\n- Angular 19 -> 21 via `ng update` (framework + `@angular/build`/`cli`),\n  including the bootstrap-options -> providers migration in main.ts.\n- Ecosystem bumped to Angular-21-compatible majors: `@ngrx/*` 21.1.1,\n  `@fundamental-ngx/*` 0.63.0 (+ fundamental-styles 0.41.7 /\n  theming-base-content ^11.36), `@luigi-project/client-support-angular`\n  21.1.0, `apollo-angular` 13, `@apollo/client` 4, `@angular/cdk` 21.\n- Test tooling bumped for Angular 21 / jest 30: `jest` 30, `@types/jest` 30,\n  `jest-preset-angular` 17, `jest-junit` 17, `jest-mock-extended` 4,\n  `ng-mocks` 14.17, plus `jest-environment-jsdom` 30 (no longer bundled).\n\nApollo Client v3 -> v4 code migration (non-generic `ApolloClientOptions`,\n`HttpHeaders` context, `result.data` now possibly-undefined) applied to the\nresource/dashboard/schema services.\n\n`npm audit` reports 0 vulnerabilities; `ng build` and the full jest suite\n(237 tests) pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfY19CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARsUQAKRZy4Czz/ZmVMY1fsJ8zpVg\n5/A0IncAzRqJPqW03JaIxriSv6+0sZbSQ8aqI2diAKmrG9JTv69V1514Wtb+3+v6\n03tnXMaMMMIURaluajF6Rr/OhcD22IBYKrBi/EiM3LZpm7NwQjFebMCWLxuFeWoC\nTBI/SwwR8e+YcBquu0zzACeFAMoiOi5OPWMTqFxCSdJlR/UOmP+IAYIdf43LTySU\n9re25KerLK19jmeXGVWqpDZsjU3AobHqILFNoG3q/q2rc7cie7fK7d9+AEa8LvqG\nmdhLMHob4hXURYNAF2cVtTUdm7jU09sH+CGPUjVFfjxmGHBQqq4dUA8rCXnUN+QX\nDVgi4IR5Rn0Osk2Mz4+22q/QepfVmeQO6FcdYsNp/EvxJa+ehIui/n/R4dWehAlz\nC4/5JKc9KspcoCXQ335UMBx/GQ3n3Cs05hccX