 dependency\n- Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with the new package and its dependencies\n\n### 2. Layout Configuration (app/layout.tsx)\n- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from ''@vercel/speed-insights/next''`\n- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, placed after the `<Footer />` component\n- This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all page interactions properly\n\n## Implementation Details:\n\nSince this project uses:\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (which is >= 13.5)\n- App Router architecture (app/ directory structure)\n\nThe implementation followed the recommended approach for modern Next.js with App Router:\n- Used the `@vercel/speed-insights/next` import path\n- Added the component to the root layout (app/layout.tsx)\n- No need for ''use client'' directive or usePathname() as the component handles this internally\n\n## Verification:\n\n✓ Build completed successfully (pnpm build)\n✓ All production pages generated without errors\n✓ TypeScript compilation passed\n✓ Lock file updated with all dependencies\n\n## Files Modified:\n\n- app/layout.tsx - Added SpeedInsights component\n- package.json - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency\n- pnpm-lock.yaml - Updated with new package dependencies\n\n## Notes:\n\nThe Speed Insights component will automatically:\n- Track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)\n- Send performance metrics to Vercel dashboard\n- Only activate when deployed to Vercel (no-op in local development)\n\nNo additional configuration is required. The integration is complete and ready for deployment.\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5b8d0093ef2d24f7142499b4f0519728bcacd1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thushanthbengre22-dev/portfolio-react-app/git/trees/d5b8d0093ef2d24f7142499b4f0519728bcacd1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thushanthbengre22-dev/portfolio-react-app/git/commits/c34c8aca15cdde9835a0661203a0b02bc9839ca5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","sign